 notes.push(...[["11. Blood cells: formation and functions","Haematopoiesis occurs mainly in red bone marrow in adults. Erythrocytes transport oxygen and part of carbon dioxide; leukocytes defend against infection; platelets support primary haemostasis. Neutrophils are important in acute bacterial infection, lymphocytes in adaptive immunity, monocytes become macrophages, eosinophils are associated with parasites/allergy, and basophils release inflammatory mediators. RBC lifespan is about 120 days.","वयस्कमा रक्तकोष निर्माण मुख्यतः red bone marrow मा हुन्छ। RBC ले oxygen बोक्छ, WBC ले संक्रमणसँग लड्छ र platelet ले रक्तस्राव रोक्न सहयोग गर्छ। Neutrophil acute bacterial infection, lymphocyte adaptive immunity, monocyte macrophage बन्ने, eosinophil parasite/allergy र basophil inflammatory mediator सँग सम्बन्धित हुन्छ।"],["12. Haemoglobin and oxygen transport","Haemoglobin is a tetrameric protein in red cells; each haem group contains iron that reversibly binds oxygen. Oxyhaemoglobin forms in the lungs and releases oxygen in tissues. Carbon monoxide binds haemoglobin with very high affinity and reduces oxygen delivery. Anaemia reduces oxygen-carrying capacity even when arterial oxygen saturation may appear normal.","Haemoglobin RBC भित्रको protein हो। यसको haem मा iron हुन्छ जसले oxygen लाई reversible रूपमा बाँध्छ। फोक्सोमा oxyhaemoglobin बन्छ र tissue मा oxygen छोड्छ। Carbon monoxide ले haemoglobin सँग धेरै बलियोसँग बाँधिएर oxygen पुर्‍याउने क्षमता घटाउँछ।"],["13. Anaemia: definition and classification","Anaemia is a reduction in haemoglobin concentration below the appropriate reference range for age, sex and pregnancy status. Morphological classification uses MCV: microcytic, normocytic and macrocytic. Common causes include iron deficiency, blood loss, haemolysis, chronic inflammation, renal disease and vitamin B12/folate deficiency. Interpret CBC, reticulocyte count and blood film together.","उमेर, लिङ्ग र गर्भावस्थाअनुसार अपेक्षित सीमाभन्दा haemoglobin कम हुनु anaemia हो। MCV अनुसार microcytic, normocytic र macrocytic वर्गीकरण गरिन्छ। Iron कमी, रक्तस्राव, haemolysis, chronic inflammation, renal disease र B12/folate कमी कारण हुन सक्छन्। CBC, reticulocyte र blood film सँगै हेर्नुपर्छ।"],["14. Jaundice and bilirubin metabolism","Jaundice is yellow discoloration due to increased bilirubin. Pre-hepatic jaundice commonly follows increased haemolysis and raises unconjugated bilirubin; hepatic jaundice results from hepatocyte dysfunction; post-hepatic jaundice is often due to biliary obstruction and raises conjugated bilirubin. Urine bilirubin is generally absent in isolated unconjugated hyperbilirubinaemia.","Bilirubin बढ्दा छाला र आँखामा पहेँलोपन देखिनु jaundice हो। Pre-hepatic मा haemolysis का कारण unconjugated bilirubin बढ्छ; hepatic मा liver cell समस्या हुन्छ; post-hepatic मा bile duct अवरोधका कारण conjugated bilirubin बढ्न सक्छ।"],["15. ESR, PCV and osmotic fragility","ESR measures the distance red cells settle in a vertical tube over a specified time; it is non-specific and affected by inflammation, anaemia, pregnancy and red-cell shape. PCV is the fraction of blood volume occupied by red cells. Osmotic fragility assesses RBC susceptibility to lysis in hypotonic saline; increased fragility is classically seen in hereditary spherocytosis.","ESR निश्चित समयमा RBC कति तल बस्छ भन्ने मापन हो र यो non-specific हुन्छ। PCV ले रगतमा RBC को आयतन अनुपात देखाउँछ। Osmotic fragility ले hypotonic saline मा RBC फुट्ने संवेदनशीलता जाँच्छ; hereditary spherocytosis मा fragility बढ्न सक्छ।"],["16. Red-cell indices and reticulocytes","MCV = average red-cell volume; MCH = average haemoglobin mass per red cell; MCHC = average haemoglobin concentration in packed red cells; RDW reflects variation in red-cell size. Reticulocytes are immature red cells and indicate marrow response. High reticulocytes may occur after haemorrhage or haemolysis; low response may occur with marrow suppression or nutrient deficiency.","MCV ले RBC को औसत आकार, MCH ले प्रति RBC haemoglobin मात्रा, MCHC ले RBC भित्र haemoglobin concentration र RDW ले आकारको फरक देखाउँछ। Reticulocyte अपरिपक्व RBC हो र bone marrow को प्रतिक्रिया जनाउँछ।"],["17. Haemostasis and coagulation pathways","Primary haemostasis involves vasoconstriction and platelet adhesion, activation and aggregation. Secondary haemostasis activates coagulation factors to generate thrombin, which converts fibrinogen to fibrin. PT/INR assesses the extrinsic and common pathways; aPTT assesses intrinsic and common pathways. Fibrinolysis later breaks down fibrin, mainly through plasmin.","Primary haemostasis मा रक्तनली खुम्चिने र platelet adhesion, activation तथा aggregation हुन्छ। Secondary haemostasis मा coagulation factor सक्रिय भई thrombin बनाउँछ र fibrinogen लाई fibrin बनाउँछ। PT/INR ले extrinsic/common र aPTT ले intrinsic/common pathway जाँच्छ।"],["18. ABO, Rh and compatibility","Group A red cells carry A antigen; group B carry B; AB carry both; O carry neither A nor B. Plasma naturally contains antibodies against absent ABO antigens. RhD status is clinically important in transfusion and pregnancy. ABO-compatible selection, antibody screening and crossmatching must follow blood-bank policy; emergency release is a defined institutional process.","A समूहमा A antigen, B मा B, AB मा दुवै र O मा A/B antigen हुँदैन। Plasma मा नभएको ABO antigen विरुद्ध antibody हुन सक्छ। RhD transfusion र गर्भावस्थामा महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छ। Blood-bank policy अनुसार group, antibody screen र crossmatch गर्नुपर्छ।"],["19. Cardiac chambers, valves and circulation","The right atrium receives systemic venous blood and passes it through the tricuspid valve to the right ventricle; the pulmonary valve leads to the lungs. The left atrium receives pulmonary venous blood and passes it through the mitral valve to the left ventricle; the aortic valve leads to systemic circulation. Valves maintain one-way flow.","Right atrium मा शरीरबाट आएको venous blood आउँछ र tricuspid valve हुँदै right ventricle जान्छ। Pulmonary valve बाट फोक्सो पुग्छ। Left atrium मा फोक्सोबाट आएको रगत आउँछ, mitral valve हुँदै left ventricle र aortic valve बाट शरीरमा जान्छ।"],["20. Cardiac cycle, output and blood pressure","The cardiac cycle includes ventricular filling, isovolumetric contraction, ejection, isovolumetric relaxation and filling. Stroke volume is blood ejected per beat; cardiac output = heart rate × stroke volume. Blood pressure depends on cardiac output and systemic vascular resistance. Preload relates to ventricular filling; afterload is the load against which the ventricle ejects.","Cardiac cycle मा ventricular filling, contraction, ejection र relaxation पर्छन्। Stroke volume प्रत्येक धड्कनमा निस्कने रगत हो। Cardiac output = heart rate × stroke volume। Blood pressure cardiac output र systemic vascular resistance मा निर्भर हुन्छ।"],["21. Conduction system and ECG basics","The sinoatrial node normally initiates the impulse, which travels through atria to the AV node, bundle of His, bundle branches and Purkinje fibres. The ECG P wave represents atrial depolarisation, QRS ventricular depolarisation and T wave ventricular repolarisation. ECG must be interpreted with symptoms and clinical assessment.","SA node ले सामान्यतया impulse सुरु गर्छ। यो atria, AV node, bundle of His, bundle branches र Purkinje fibres हुँदै फैलिन्छ। ECG मा P wave atrial depolarisation, QRS ventricular depolarisation र T wave ventricular repolarisation हो।"],["22. Respiratory mechanics and lung volumes","Inspiration at rest is active, mainly using the diaphragm and external intercostals; quiet expiration is usually passive. Tidal volume is air moved in a normal breath. Vital capacity is the maximum exhaled volume after maximal inspiration. Residual volume remains after maximal expiration. Compliance describes ease of lung expansion; resistance describes opposition to airflow.","आरामको अवस्थामा inspiration मुख्यतः diaphragm र external intercostal को कामले सक्रिय हुन्छ; सामान्य expiration प्रायः passive हुन्छ। Tidal volume सामान्य सासमा सर्ने हावा हो। Compliance ले फोक्सो कति सजिलै फैलिन्छ र resistance ले airflow को अवरोध जनाउँछ।"],["23. Gas exchange and transport","Gas exchange occurs across the alveolar-capillary membrane by diffusion down partial-pressure gradients. Most oxygen is carried bound to haemoglobin; a small amount is dissolved in plasma. Carbon dioxide is transported mainly as bicarbonate, with smaller amounts dissolved or bound to proteins. Ventilation-perfusion matching is essential for efficient oxygenation.","Alveoli र capillary बीच partial pressure gradient अनुसार diffusion बाट gas exchange हुन्छ। धेरैजसो oxygen haemoglobin सँग बाँधिएर र थोरै plasma मा घुलिएर बोकिन्छ। CO2 मुख्यतः bicarbonate रूपमा बोकिन्छ। प्रभावकारी oxygenation का लागि ventilation-perfusion मिल्नुपर्छ।"],["24. Gastrointestinal digestion and absorption","Salivary amylase begins starch digestion; gastric acid and pepsin support protein digestion. Pancreatic enzymes digest carbohydrates, proteins and fats in the small intestine. Bile emulsifies fats but is not an enzyme. Most nutrient absorption occurs in the small intestine; the colon absorbs water and electrolytes and forms stool.","Salivary amylase ले starch पचाउन सुरु गर्छ। पेटको acid र pepsin ले protein digestion मा मद्दत गर्छ। Pancreatic enzyme ले सानो आन्द्रामा carbohydrate, protein र fat पचाउँछ। Bile ले fat emulsify गर्छ तर enzyme होइन।"],["25. Liver, pancreas and jaundice relevance","The liver processes nutrients, detoxifies substances, produces bile, albumin and many clotting factors, and handles bilirubin. The pancreas releases digestive enzymes and bicarbonate into the intestine; its islets secrete insulin and glucagon. Liver dysfunction may affect drug metabolism, albumin, coagulation and glucose regulation—important considerations in peri-anaesthetic assessment.","Liver ले nutrient process, detoxification, bile, albumin र धेरै clotting factor बनाउँछ तथा bilirubin process गर्छ। Pancreas ले digestive enzyme र bicarbonate छोड्छ; islet ले insulin र glucagon बनाउँछ। Liver समस्या हुँदा औषधि metabolism, albumin, coagulation र glucose प्रभावित हुन सक्छ।"],["26. Renal physiology and urine formation","Nephrons filter plasma at the glomerulus, then selectively reabsorb and secrete substances along renal tubules. Kidneys regulate water, sodium, potassium, acid–base balance and blood pressure; they also produce erythropoietin and activate vitamin D. Urine output and renal function are important perioperative observations.","Nephron मा glomerulus ले plasma filter गर्छ र tubule ले आवश्यक पदार्थ reabsorb तथा secretion गर्छ। मिर्गौलाले पानी, sodium, potassium, acid–base र blood pressure नियन्त्रण गर्छ। Erythropoietin बनाउँछ र vitamin D सक्रिय गर्छ।"],["27. Endocrine regulation","The pituitary coordinates several endocrine functions; thyroid hormones influence metabolic rate; parathyroid hormone regulates calcium; adrenal cortex produces corticosteroids and mineralocorticoids; adrenal medulla releases catecholamines. Insulin lowers blood glucose and glucagon raises it. Hormone secretion is commonly controlled by negative feedback.","Pituitary ले धेरै endocrine काम समन्वय गर्छ। Thyroid hormone ले metabolism, parathyroid hormone ले calcium, adrenal cortex ले corticosteroid/mineralocorticoid र adrenal medulla ले catecholamine बनाउँछ। Insulin ले glucose घटाउँछ र glucagon ले बढाउँछ।"],["28. Nervous system and autonomic control","The brain and spinal cord form the CNS. The PNS includes cranial and spinal nerves. Sensory/afferent pathways carry information toward the CNS; motor/efferent pathways carry commands away. Sympathetic activity generally increases heart rate and supports fight-or-flight; parasympathetic activity generally supports rest-and-digest functions. Autonomic effects are important during anaesthesia.","Brain र spinal cord मिलेर CNS बन्छ। PNS मा cranial र spinal nerve पर्छन्। Afferent pathway ले सूचना CNS तर्फ र efferent ले आदेश बाहिर लैजान्छ। Sympathetic ले सामान्यतया heart rate बढाउँछ; parasympathetic ले rest-and-digest काम बढाउँछ।"],["29. Reproductive system and embryology","The male reproductive system produces sperm and testosterone; the female system produces ova and hormones and supports fertilisation and pregnancy. Fertilisation usually occurs in the uterine tube. Implantation follows early embryonic development. The placenta supports exchange of gases, nutrients and waste and produces hormones. Developmental age and maternal conditions influence anaesthetic planning in pregnancy.","पुरुष प्रजनन प्रणालीले sperm र testosterone बनाउँछ; महिला प्रणालीले ovum/hormone उत्पादन र गर्भधारणमा सहयोग गर्छ। Fertilisation प्रायः uterine tube मा हुन्छ। Placenta ले gas, nutrient र waste exchange तथा hormone उत्पादन गर्छ।"]]);
 const anatomyBatch=[["The main site of haematopoiesis in a healthy adult is:","स्वस्थ वयस्कमा रक्तकोष निर्माणको मुख्य स्थान कुन हो?",["Red bone marrow","Yellow bone marrow","Spleen only","Liver only"],0,"Red bone marrow is the principal site of blood-cell production in adults.","वयस्कमा रक्तकोष उत्पादनको मुख्य स्थान red bone marrow हो।"],["The usual lifespan of a circulating red blood cell is approximately:","रक्तसञ्चारमा रहेको RBC को सामान्य आयु कति हो?",["120 days","12 days","30 days","365 days"],0,"An RBC circulates for about 120 days before removal, mainly by the reticuloendothelial system.","RBC करिब १२० दिन बाँच्छ र त्यसपछि मुख्यतः reticuloendothelial system ले हटाउँछ।"],["Which leukocyte is commonly increased in acute bacterial infection?","Acute bacterial infection मा कुन WBC प्रायः बढ्छ?",["Neutrophil","Eosinophil","Basophil","Lymphocyte only"],0,"Neutrophils are key first responders in many acute bacterial infections.","धेरै acute bacterial infection मा neutrophil मुख्य प्रारम्भिक प्रतिरक्षा कोष हो।"],["Which cell becomes a macrophage after entering tissues?","Tissue मा गएपछि कुन कोष macrophage बन्छ?",["Monocyte","Erythrocyte","Platelet","Basophil"],0,"Monocytes migrate into tissues and can differentiate into macrophages.","Monocyte tissue मा गएर macrophage मा विकसित हुन सक्छ।"],["The iron-containing part of haemoglobin is:","Haemoglobin मा iron भएको भाग कुन हो?",["Haem group","Globin chain only","Albumin","Fibrin"],0,"Each haem group contains iron that binds oxygen reversibly.","प्रत्येक haem group मा oxygen लाई reversible बाँध्ने iron हुन्छ।"],["Carbon monoxide reduces oxygen delivery mainly because it:","Carbon monoxide ले oxygen delivery किन घटाउँछ?",["Binds haemoglobin with high affinity","Destroys all platelets","Raises plasma albumin","Increases lung surfactant"],0,"Carbon monoxide forms carboxyhaemoglobin and reduces available oxygen-carrying sites.","Carbon monoxide haemoglobin सँग बाँधिएर oxygen बोक्ने स्थान घटाउँछ।"],["Microcytic anaemia is commonly associated with:","Microcytic anaemia सामान्यतया केसँग सम्बन्धित हुन्छ?",["Iron deficiency","Vitamin B12 deficiency","Acute blood loss only","Aplastic marrow only"],0,"Iron deficiency commonly produces small red cells with low MCV.","Iron कमीमा प्रायः सानो RBC र कम MCV हुन्छ।"],["Macrocytosis may be caused by deficiency of:","Macrocytosis कुन vitamin कमीले हुन सक्छ?",["Vitamin B12 or folate","Vitamin C only","Vitamin K only","Sodium"],0,"B12 or folate deficiency can impair DNA synthesis and produce macrocytosis.","B12 वा folate कमीले DNA synthesis बिगारी macrocytosis गराउन सक्छ।"],["Unconjugated bilirubin is generally not found in urine because it is:","Unconjugated bilirubin सामान्यतया पिसाबमा किन हुँदैन?",["Albumin-bound and water-insoluble","Highly water-soluble","Filtered freely by kidney","Produced in urine"],0,"Unconjugated bilirubin is albumin-bound and not water-soluble enough for urinary excretion.","Unconjugated bilirubin albumin सँग बाँधिएको र पानीमा नघुल्ने भएकाले पिसाबमा निस्कँदैन।"],["A classic cause of increased osmotic fragility is:","Osmotic fragility बढ्ने classic कारण कुन हो?",["Hereditary spherocytosis","Iron deficiency","Thalassaemia trait","Sickle trait"],0,"Spherocytes have reduced surface-area-to-volume ratio and lyse more readily in hypotonic solutions.","Spherocyte को surface-area-to-volume ratio कम हुँदा hypotonic solution मा छिटो फुट्छ।"],["Which index represents average red-cell volume?","RBC को औसत आयतन कुन index ले देखाउँछ?",["MCV","MCH","MCHC","RDW"],0,"MCV is mean corpuscular volume.","MCV भनेको mean corpuscular volume हो।"],["Which test primarily assesses the extrinsic and common coagulation pathways?","Extrinsic र common coagulation pathway मुख्यतः कुन test ले जाँच्छ?",["PT/INR","aPTT","Bleeding time only","ESR"],0,"PT/INR is sensitive to the extrinsic and common pathways.","PT/INR ले extrinsic र common pathway जाँच्छ।"],["Which test primarily assesses intrinsic and common coagulation pathways?","Intrinsic र common coagulation pathway कुन test ले जाँच्छ?",["aPTT","PT only","PCV","Reticulocyte count"],0,"aPTT evaluates intrinsic and common pathway function.","aPTT ले intrinsic र common pathway को अवस्था मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ।"],["The enzyme that converts fibrinogen to fibrin is:","Fibrinogen लाई fibrin मा बदल्ने enzyme कुन हो?",["Thrombin","Plasmin","Amylase","Pepsin"],0,"Thrombin cleaves fibrinogen to form fibrin strands.","Thrombin ले fibrinogen बाट fibrin बनाउँछ।"],["The universal red-cell donor type in emergency teaching is commonly described as:","Emergency teaching मा universal RBC donor कुन समूह भनिन्छ?",["O negative","AB positive","A positive","B negative"],0,"O negative red cells lack A, B and RhD antigens; actual transfusion still requires protocol and compatibility procedures.","O negative RBC मा A, B र RhD antigen हुँदैन; वास्तविक transfusion मा protocol र compatibility प्रक्रिया चाहिन्छ।"],["The valve between the left atrium and left ventricle is:","Left atrium र left ventricle बीच कुन valve हुन्छ?",["Mitral valve","Tricuspid valve","Pulmonary valve","Aortic valve"],0,"The mitral (bicuspid) valve separates the left atrium and ventricle.","Mitral valve ले left atrium र ventricle छुट्याउँछ।"],["The valve that prevents backflow from the aorta into the left ventricle is:","Aorta बाट left ventricle मा रगत फर्कन नदिने valve कुन हो?",["Aortic valve","Mitral valve","Tricuspid valve","Pulmonary valve"],0,"The aortic valve closes after ventricular ejection to prevent backflow.","Ventricular ejection पछि aortic valve बन्द भएर रगत फर्कन रोक्छ।"],["Cardiac output is calculated as:","Cardiac output कसरी गणना गरिन्छ?",["Heart rate × stroke volume","Blood pressure × temperature","Respiratory rate × tidal volume","Pulse pressure × height"],0,"Cardiac output equals heart rate multiplied by stroke volume.","Cardiac output = heart rate × stroke volume हो।"],["The normal pacemaker of the heart is the:","मुटुको सामान्य pacemaker कुन हो?",["Sinoatrial node","AV node","Bundle of His","Purkinje fibres"],0,"The SA node normally initiates each heartbeat.","SA node ले सामान्यतया प्रत्येक heartbeat सुरु गर्छ।"],["The ECG P wave represents:","ECG को P wave ले के जनाउँछ?",["Atrial depolarisation","Ventricular depolarisation","Ventricular repolarisation","Atrial repolarisation only"],0,"The P wave represents atrial depolarisation.","P wave ले atrial depolarisation जनाउँछ।"],["The main muscle of quiet inspiration is the:","सामान्य inspiration को मुख्य muscle कुन हो?",["Diaphragm","Internal intercostal","Abdominal rectus","Trapezius"],0,"Diaphragmatic contraction increases thoracic volume during quiet inspiration.","Diaphragm खुम्चिँदा thoracic volume बढेर inspiration हुन्छ।"],["Quiet expiration at rest is usually:","आराममा सामान्य expiration प्रायः कस्तो हुन्छ?",["Passive","An active forced process","Dependent on abdominal muscle contraction","Impossible without oxygen"],0,"Elastic recoil of the lungs and chest wall usually drives quiet expiration.","फोक्सो र छातीको elastic recoil ले सामान्य expiration गराउँछ।"],["Gas exchange across the alveolar-capillary membrane occurs mainly by:","Alveoli र capillary बीच gas exchange मुख्यतः कसरी हुन्छ?",["Diffusion","Active transport","Filtration","Osmosis of whole blood"],0,"Oxygen and carbon dioxide diffuse down their partial-pressure gradients.","Oxygen र carbon dioxide partial pressure gradient अनुसार diffusion गर्छन्।"],["Most oxygen in blood is transported:","रगतमा धेरैजसो oxygen कसरी बोकिन्छ?",["Bound to haemoglobin","Dissolved freely in plasma","As bicarbonate","Bound to albumin"],0,"Most oxygen is carried as oxyhaemoglobin; only a small fraction is dissolved.","धेरै oxygen oxyhaemoglobin रूपमा र थोरै plasma मा घुलेर बोकिन्छ।"],["Most carbon dioxide is transported in blood as:","रगतमा धेरैजसो carbon dioxide कुन रूपमा बोकिन्छ?",["Bicarbonate","Oxyhaemoglobin","Dissolved gas only","Carbon monoxide"],0,"Most CO2 is converted to bicarbonate, largely in red cells.","धेरै CO2 RBC भित्र bicarbonate मा परिवर्तन भएर बोकिन्छ।"],["Which organ produces bile?","Bile कुन अंगले बनाउँछ?",["Liver","Pancreas","Stomach","Spleen"],0,"The liver produces bile, which is stored and concentrated in the gallbladder.","Liver ले bile बनाउँछ; gallbladder मा भण्डारण र गाढा हुन्छ।"],["Most nutrient absorption occurs in the:","धेरैजसो पोषक तत्व कहाँ सोसिन्छ?",["Small intestine","Oesophagus","Stomach","Large intestine"],0,"The small intestine is the major site of nutrient digestion and absorption.","सानो आन्द्रा पोषक तत्व पाचन र अवशोषणको मुख्य स्थान हो।"],["Which pancreatic hormone lowers blood glucose?","कुन pancreatic hormone ले blood glucose घटाउँछ?",["Insulin","Glucagon","Adrenaline","Cortisol"],0,"Insulin promotes glucose uptake and storage, lowering blood glucose.","Insulin ले glucose uptake र storage बढाएर blood glucose घटाउँछ।"],["The functional unit of the kidney is the:","मिर्गौलाको functional unit कुन हो?",["Nephron","Alveolus","Neuron","Hepatocyte"],0,"Each nephron filters plasma and modifies filtrate to form urine.","प्रत्येक nephron ले plasma filter गरी filtrate परिवर्तन गरेर पिसाब बनाउँछ।"],["Erythropoietin is produced mainly by the:","Erythropoietin मुख्यतः कहाँ उत्पादन हुन्छ?",["Kidney","Pancreas","Thyroid","Lung"],0,"Renal interstitial cells release erythropoietin in response to reduced oxygen delivery.","Oxygen कम पुगेमा kidney का interstitial cell ले erythropoietin निकाल्छन्।"],["The hormone that raises blood calcium is:","रगतको calcium बढाउने hormone कुन हो?",["Parathyroid hormone","Insulin","Aldosterone","Melatonin"],0,"Parathyroid hormone increases serum calcium through actions on bone, kidney and vitamin D activation.","Parathyroid hormone ले bone, kidney र vitamin D मार्फत calcium बढाउँछ।"],["The adrenal medulla primarily secretes:","Adrenal medulla ले मुख्यतः के निकाल्छ?",["Catecholamines","Thyroxine","Insulin","Parathyroid hormone"],0,"The adrenal medulla releases epinephrine and norepinephrine.","Adrenal medulla ले epinephrine र norepinephrine निकाल्छ।"],["The central nervous system consists of:","Central nervous system मा के पर्छ?",["Brain and spinal cord","Cranial nerves only","Spinal nerves only","Autonomic ganglia only"],0,"The CNS is formed by the brain and spinal cord.","CNS मा brain र spinal cord पर्छन्।"],["Afferent nerves carry information:","Afferent nerve ले सूचना कुन दिशामा लैजान्छ?",["Toward the central nervous system","Away from the CNS to muscles only","Only to glands","Only between muscles"],0,"Afferent pathways carry sensory input toward the CNS.","Afferent pathway ले sensory सूचना CNS तर्फ लैजान्छ।"],["Sympathetic activation commonly causes:","Sympathetic activation हुँदा सामान्यतया के हुन्छ?",["Increased heart rate","Reduced alertness in all cases","Increased gut motility","Pupil constriction"],0,"Sympathetic activity supports fight-or-flight responses, including increased heart rate.","Sympathetic ले fight-or-flight प्रतिक्रिया र heart rate बढाउन सक्छ।"],["Fertilisation in humans usually occurs in the:","मानिसमा fertilisation प्रायः कहाँ हुन्छ?",["Uterine tube","Cervix","Vagina","Endometrium"],0,"Fertilisation most commonly occurs in the ampullary region of the uterine tube.","Fertilisation प्रायः uterine tube को ampullary भागमा हुन्छ।"],["The placenta primarily supports:","Placenta को मुख्य काम के हो?",["Maternal-fetal exchange","Production of sperm","Urine storage","Digestion of maternal food"],0,"The placenta enables exchange of gases, nutrients and waste and produces hormones.","Placenta ले gas, nutrient र waste exchange तथा hormone उत्पादन गर्छ।"]];
 notes.push(...[["30. Cell membrane transport and homeostasis","The cell membrane is a selectively permeable phospholipid bilayer containing proteins. Diffusion moves substances down a concentration gradient; osmosis is water movement across a selectively permeable membrane; facilitated diffusion uses channels/carriers without direct ATP use; active transport uses energy to move substances against a gradient. Homeostasis maintains a relatively stable internal environment through feedback systems.","Cell membrane phospholipid bilayer हो र selectively permeable हुन्छ। Diffusion मा पदार्थ concentration gradient अनुसार सर्छ; osmosis पानीको movement हो; facilitated diffusion मा channel/carrier प्रयोग हुन्छ; active transport मा energy प्रयोग गरी gradient विरुद्ध पदार्थ सारिन्छ। Homeostasis ले शरीरको आन्तरिक अवस्था स्थिर राख्छ।"],["31. Tissue types and connective tissue","The four primary tissue classes are epithelial, connective, muscle and nervous tissue. Connective tissue supports, binds and protects; examples include blood, bone, cartilage, adipose tissue, tendons and ligaments. Collagen provides tensile strength, while elastic fibres allow stretch and recoil.","मुख्य tissue चार प्रकारका हुन्छन्: epithelial, connective, muscle र nervous। Connective tissue ले support, binding र protection गर्छ। Blood, bone, cartilage, fat, tendon र ligament उदाहरण हुन्। Collagen ले मजबुती र elastic fibre ले तन्किने क्षमता दिन्छ।"],["32. Bone, joints and muscle","Bone provides support, protection, mineral storage and blood-cell production in marrow. Osteoblasts form bone; osteoclasts resorb it; osteocytes maintain it. Fibrous, cartilaginous and synovial joints differ in movement. Skeletal muscle is voluntary and striated; smooth muscle is involuntary; cardiac muscle is involuntary and striated.","Bone ले support, protection, mineral storage र marrow मा blood-cell production गर्छ। Osteoblast ले bone बनाउँछ, osteoclast ले भत्काउँछ र osteocyte ले कायम राख्छ। Joint fibrous, cartilaginous र synovial हुन्छन्। Skeletal muscle voluntary, smooth involuntary र cardiac muscle involuntary तथा striated हुन्छ।"],["33. Blood groups, transfusion reactions and safe practice","ABO and Rh typing are essential but do not replace antibody screening and crossmatching. Acute haemolytic transfusion reactions may present with fever, chills, pain, hypotension, dyspnoea or dark urine. If a reaction is suspected, stop the transfusion, maintain IV access with compatible fluid according to local protocol, urgently notify the responsible clinician and blood bank, and follow institutional reaction procedures.","ABO र Rh typing आवश्यक भए पनि antibody screening र crossmatch को विकल्प होइन। Acute haemolytic reaction मा ज्वरो, कम्पन, दुखाइ, hypotension, सास फेर्न गाह्रो वा गाढा पिसाब हुन सक्छ। शंका भए transfusion रोक्ने, local protocol अनुसार IV access कायम राख्ने र तुरुन्त clinician तथा blood bank लाई खबर गर्ने।"],["34. Blood pressure regulation and shock physiology","Arterial pressure is influenced by cardiac output and systemic vascular resistance. Baroreceptors in the carotid sinus and aortic arch detect pressure changes and adjust autonomic output. The kidneys regulate long-term volume and pressure through sodium-water balance and the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system. Shock is inadequate tissue perfusion and requires urgent clinical recognition and management.","Arterial pressure cardiac output र systemic vascular resistance मा निर्भर हुन्छ। Carotid sinus र aortic arch का baroreceptor ले pressure परिवर्तन पहिचान गर्छन्। Kidney ले sodium-water balance र renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system मार्फत दीर्घकालीन नियन्त्रण गर्छ। Shock भनेको tissue मा पर्याप्त blood perfusion नपुग्नु हो।"],["35. Acid-base physiology","Normal arterial pH is maintained within a narrow range. The lungs regulate carbon dioxide by changing ventilation; the kidneys regulate bicarbonate and hydrogen-ion excretion. Respiratory disorders primarily alter PaCO2, while metabolic disorders primarily alter bicarbonate. Compensation reduces pH disturbance but does not necessarily correct the underlying cause.","रगतको pH साँघुरो सीमाभित्र कायम राखिन्छ। फोक्सोले ventilation परिवर्तन गरी CO2 नियन्त्रण गर्छ; kidney ले bicarbonate र hydrogen ion नियन्त्रण गर्छ। Respiratory समस्या मुख्यतः PaCO2 र metabolic समस्या मुख्यतः bicarbonate मा परिवर्तन ल्याउँछ।"],["36. Reproductive hormones and menstrual cycle","The hypothalamus releases GnRH, stimulating pituitary FSH and LH. FSH supports ovarian follicle development; LH triggers ovulation and supports corpus luteum function. Oestrogen and progesterone regulate the endometrium and reproductive cycle. Pregnancy changes cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic physiology, which matters in peri-anaesthetic assessment.","Hypothalamus बाट GnRH निस्केर pituitary को FSH र LH सक्रिय हुन्छ। FSH ले ovarian follicle विकासमा र LH ले ovulation मा सहयोग गर्छ। Oestrogen र progesterone ले endometrium तथा menstrual cycle नियन्त्रण गर्छन्। गर्भावस्थामा cardiovascular, respiratory र metabolic परिवर्तन हुन्छन्।"],["37. Embryonic development and congenital anomalies","After fertilisation, cleavage produces a morula and then a blastocyst; implantation occurs in the endometrium. Gastrulation forms ectoderm, mesoderm and endoderm, which give rise to different tissues and organs. Organogenesis occurs mainly during the embryonic period; harmful exposures during this stage may cause congenital abnormalities. The placenta is not a complete barrier to drugs or pathogens.","Fertilisation पछि cleavage हुँदै morula र blastocyst बन्छ र endometrium मा implantation हुन्छ। Gastrulation बाट ectoderm, mesoderm र endoderm बन्छन्, जसबाट विभिन्न अंग र tissue विकास हुन्छन्। Organogenesis embryonic period मा मुख्य हुन्छ। Placenta ले सबै औषधि वा रोगाणु रोक्दैन।"]]);
 anatomyBatch.push(...[["Which process moves water across a selectively permeable membrane?","Selectively permeable membrane बाट पानी सर्ने प्रक्रियालाई के भनिन्छ?",["Osmosis","Active transport","Phagocytosis","Exocytosis"],0,"Osmosis is the net movement of water across a selectively permeable membrane.","Osmosis भनेको selectively permeable membrane बाट पानीको net movement हो।"],["Which transport mechanism requires cellular energy to move a substance against its gradient?","Gradient विरुद्ध पदार्थ सार्न cellular energy चाहिने प्रक्रिया कुन हो?",["Active transport","Simple diffusion","Osmosis","Filtration only"],0,"Active transport uses energy, often ATP, to move substances against an electrochemical gradient.","Active transport मा electrochemical gradient विरुद्ध पदार्थ सार्न energy चाहिन्छ।"],["Which tissue type forms glands and lines body cavities?","Gland बनाउने र body cavity को lining गर्ने tissue कुन हो?",["Epithelial tissue","Nervous tissue","Cardiac muscle","Bone"],0,"Epithelial tissue covers surfaces, lines cavities and forms glands.","Epithelial tissue ले सतह र cavity ढाक्छ तथा gland बनाउँछ।"],["Which connective tissue stores energy and provides insulation?","ऊर्जा भण्डारण र insulation गर्ने connective tissue कुन हो?",["Adipose tissue","Cartilage","Tendon","Blood plasma"],0,"Adipose tissue stores triglycerides and provides insulation and cushioning.","Adipose tissue ले triglyceride भण्डारण गरी insulation र cushioning दिन्छ।"],["Which bone cell is responsible for bone formation?","Bone निर्माण गर्ने cell कुन हो?",["Osteoblast","Osteoclast","Erythrocyte","Chondrocyte"],0,"Osteoblasts synthesise and deposit bone matrix.","Osteoblast ले bone matrix बनाउँछ।"],["Which bone cell resorbs bone?","Bone resorption गर्ने cell कुन हो?",["Osteoclast","Osteoblast","Osteocyte","Fibroblast"],0,"Osteoclasts break down bone matrix during remodelling.","Osteoclast ले bone remodelling मा matrix भत्काउँछ।"],["A freely movable joint is usually classified as:","स्वतन्त्र रूपमा चल्ने joint लाई के भनिन्छ?",["Synovial","Fibrous","Suture","Immovable"],0,"Synovial joints have a joint cavity and permit a wide range of movement.","Synovial joint मा joint cavity हुन्छ र धेरै movement सम्भव हुन्छ।"],["Which muscle type is voluntary and striated?","Voluntary र striated कुन muscle हुन्छ?",["Skeletal muscle","Smooth muscle","Cardiac muscle","Visceral epithelium"],0,"Skeletal muscle is generally under voluntary control and has striations.","Skeletal muscle सामान्यतया voluntary control मा हुन्छ र striated हुन्छ।"],["The main function of platelets is to:","Platelet को मुख्य काम के हो?",["Help form a haemostatic plug","Transport oxygen","Produce antibodies","Carry glucose"],0,"Platelets adhere and aggregate at injured vessels to form the primary haemostatic plug.","Platelet चोट लागेको रक्तनलीमा टाँसिएर primary haemostatic plug बनाउँछ।"],["Which plasma protein contributes most to colloid oncotic pressure?","Colloid oncotic pressure मा मुख्य योगदान गर्ने plasma protein कुन हो?",["Albumin","Haemoglobin","Fibrin only","Myosin"],0,"Albumin is the major contributor to plasma oncotic pressure.","Albumin ले plasma oncotic pressure मा मुख्य योगदान गर्छ।"],["Which blood group has both A and B antigens on red cells?","RBC मा A र B दुवै antigen भएको blood group कुन हो?",["AB","O","A","B"],0,"AB red cells express both A and B antigens.","AB समूहको RBC मा A र B दुवै antigen हुन्छन्।"],["A person with group O red cells has which ABO antibodies in plasma?","O समूहको व्यक्तिको plasma मा कुन ABO antibody हुन्छ?",["Anti-A and anti-B","Anti-D only","Neither anti-A nor anti-B","Anti-AB only"],0,"Group O plasma usually contains both anti-A and anti-B antibodies.","O समूहको plasma मा सामान्यतया anti-A र anti-B दुवै हुन्छन्।"],["The RhD antigen is located on the:","RhD antigen कहाँ हुन्छ?",["Red blood cell membrane","Platelet granules","Plasma albumin","White-cell nucleus"],0,"RhD is an antigen expressed on the red-cell membrane in Rh-positive individuals.","Rh-positive व्यक्तिको RBC membrane मा RhD antigen हुन्छ।"],["Which action is the first priority when an acute transfusion reaction is suspected?","Acute transfusion reaction शंका हुँदा पहिलो प्राथमिकता के हो?",["Stop the transfusion","Increase the transfusion rate","Discard the blood bag immediately without reporting","Give another unit"],0,"Stop the transfusion immediately and activate the institution's reaction protocol.","तुरुन्त transfusion रोक्दै संस्थाको reaction protocol सुरु गर्नुपर्छ।"],["Which blood component is primarily responsible for oxygen carriage?","Oxygen बोक्ने मुख्य blood component कुन हो?",["Red blood cells","Platelets","Plasma water","Neutrophils"],0,"Haemoglobin within red blood cells carries most oxygen in blood.","RBC भित्रको haemoglobin ले रगतमा धेरैजसो oxygen बोक्छ।"],["Which chamber receives deoxygenated blood from the venae cavae?","Vena cava बाट आएको deoxygenated blood कुन chamber मा आउँछ?",["Right atrium","Left atrium","Left ventricle","Aorta"],0,"The superior and inferior venae cavae empty into the right atrium.","Superior र inferior vena cava right atrium मा खुल्छन्।"],["The pulmonary artery carries blood from the:","Pulmonary artery ले रगत कहाँबाट कहाँ लैजान्छ?",["Right ventricle to lungs","Left ventricle to body","Lungs to left atrium","Right atrium to left atrium"],0,"The pulmonary trunk leaves the right ventricle and carries blood to the lungs.","Pulmonary trunk right ventricle बाट निस्केर फोक्सोमा रगत लैजान्छ।"],["The pulmonary veins normally carry:","Pulmonary vein ले सामान्यतया कस्तो रगत बोक्छ?",["Oxygenated blood to the left atrium","Deoxygenated blood to the right atrium","Blood to the liver","Lymph to the heart"],0,"Pulmonary veins return oxygenated blood from the lungs to the left atrium.","Pulmonary vein ले फोक्सोबाट oxygenated blood left atrium मा ल्याउँछ।"],["Stroke volume is the:","Stroke volume भनेको के हो?",["Volume ejected by one ventricle per beat","Blood pumped per minute","Total blood volume","Pressure during diastole"],0,"Stroke volume is the amount ejected by a ventricle in one contraction.","एक ventricular contraction मा निस्कने रगतको मात्रा stroke volume हो।"],["The first heart sound (S1) is mainly due to closure of the:","पहिलो heart sound (S1) मुख्यतः कुन valve बन्द हुँदा आउँछ?",["Mitral and tricuspid valves","Aortic and pulmonary valves","Only aortic valve","Only pulmonary valve"],0,"S1 is associated with closure of the atrioventricular valves at the start of ventricular systole.","Ventricular systole सुरु हुँदा mitral र tricuspid valve बन्द हुँदा S1 आउँछ।"],["The second heart sound (S2) is mainly due to closure of the:","दोस्रो heart sound (S2) मुख्यतः कुन valve बन्द हुँदा आउँछ?",["Aortic and pulmonary valves","Mitral and tricuspid valves","Only mitral valve","Only tricuspid valve"],0,"S2 occurs with closure of the semilunar valves at the end of systole.","Systole को अन्त्यमा aortic र pulmonary valve बन्द हुँदा S2 आउँछ।"],["Which ECG interval includes atrial depolarisation and AV nodal conduction time?","Atrial depolarisation र AV nodal conduction time समेट्ने ECG interval कुन हो?",["PR interval","QT interval","ST segment only","RR interval"],0,"The PR interval runs from the start of P to the start of QRS and reflects atrial-to-ventricular conduction.","PR interval ले P को सुरुदेखि QRS सुरु हुँदासम्मको conduction देखाउँछ।"],["The QRS complex represents:","QRS complex ले के जनाउँछ?",["Ventricular depolarisation","Atrial depolarisation","Ventricular repolarisation","SA node recovery only"],0,"QRS represents ventricular depolarisation.","QRS ले ventricular depolarisation जनाउँछ।"],["Which receptor senses stretch and helps regulate arterial pressure rapidly?","Stretch महसुस गरी arterial pressure छिटो नियन्त्रणमा सहयोग गर्ने receptor कुन हो?",["Baroreceptor","Photoreceptor","Chemoreceptor in retina","Taste receptor"],0,"Baroreceptors in the carotid sinus and aortic arch detect arterial stretch.","Carotid sinus र aortic arch का baroreceptor ले arterial stretch महसुस गर्छन्।"],["Which hormone system helps regulate long-term blood pressure and sodium balance?","दीर्घकालीन blood pressure र sodium balance कुन hormone system ले नियन्त्रण गर्छ?",["Renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system","Insulin-glucagon system","Melatonin cycle","Calcitonin pathway"],0,"RAAS promotes sodium retention and supports blood pressure regulation.","RAAS ले sodium retention बढाएर blood pressure नियन्त्रणमा सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Which lung volume remains after maximal forced expiration?","अधिकतम जोर लगाएर सास फालेपछि पनि बाँकी रहने lung volume कुन हो?",["Residual volume","Tidal volume","Inspiratory reserve volume","Vital capacity"],0,"Residual volume remains in the lungs after maximal expiration.","अधिकतम expiration पछि पनि फोक्सोमा बाँकी रहने हावा residual volume हो।"],["Vital capacity is best described as:","Vital capacity लाई कसरी परिभाषित गरिन्छ?",["Maximum air exhaled after maximal inspiration","Air remaining after normal expiration","Air moved in quiet breathing","Air in anatomical dead space only"],0,"Vital capacity is the maximum volume exhaled after a maximal inspiration.","अधिकतम inspiration पछि बाहिर निकाल्न सकिने अधिकतम हावा vital capacity हो।"],["Surfactant primarily reduces:","Surfactant ले मुख्यतः के घटाउँछ?",["Alveolar surface tension","Blood viscosity","Airway cartilage","Haemoglobin affinity"],0,"Pulmonary surfactant reduces alveolar surface tension and helps prevent collapse.","Pulmonary surfactant ले alveolar surface tension घटाएर collapse रोक्न मद्दत गर्छ।"],["The main site of gas exchange in the lungs is the:","फोक्सोमा gas exchange को मुख्य स्थान कुन हो?",["Alveoli","Trachea","Main bronchi","Pleural cavity"],0,"Alveoli provide a large thin surface for gas diffusion.","Alveoli ले gas diffusion का लागि ठूलो र पातलो सतह दिन्छ।"],["Ventilation refers to:","Ventilation भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?",["Movement of air into and out of the lungs","Blood flow through the lungs","Oxygen binding to haemoglobin","Cellular use of oxygen"],0,"Ventilation is bulk movement of air between atmosphere and alveoli.","Ventilation भनेको वातावरण र alveoli बीच हावा आवतजावत हो।"],["Perfusion in the lung refers to:","फोक्सोमा perfusion भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?",["Blood flow through pulmonary capillaries","Air movement through bronchi","Movement of mucus","Chest wall movement"],0,"Pulmonary perfusion is blood flow through the pulmonary circulation.","Pulmonary perfusion भनेको फोक्सोको रक्तनली हुँदै रगत बग्नु हो।"],["Which structure prevents food entering the larynx during swallowing?","निल्दा खाना larynx मा पस्न नदिने संरचना कुन हो?",["Epiglottis","Uvula","Vocal ligament","Nasal septum"],0,"The epiglottis helps protect the airway during swallowing.","Epiglottis ले निल्दा airway सुरक्षित राख्न सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Which organ stores and concentrates bile?","Bile भण्डारण र गाढा बनाउने अंग कुन हो?",["Gallbladder","Pancreas","Spleen","Appendix"],0,"The gallbladder stores and concentrates bile produced by the liver.","Gallbladder ले liver मा बनेको bile भण्डारण र गाढा बनाउँछ।"],["Intrinsic factor is required for absorption of:","Intrinsic factor कुन vitamin को absorption का लागि चाहिन्छ?",["Vitamin B12","Vitamin C","Vitamin K","Vitamin B1"],0,"Intrinsic factor from gastric parietal cells is needed for vitamin B12 absorption in the terminal ileum.","पेटका parietal cell बाट निस्कने intrinsic factor ले terminal ileum मा B12 absorption गराउँछ।"],["Which part of the gastrointestinal tract absorbs most water from remaining intestinal contents and forms stool?","बाँकी intestinal contents बाट पानी सोस्दै stool बनाउने मुख्य भाग कुन हो?",["Large intestine","Oesophagus","Stomach","Duodenum only"],0,"The colon absorbs water and electrolytes and compacts faeces.","Colon ले पानी र electrolyte सोसेर दिसा गाढा बनाउँछ।"],["The endocrine part of the pancreas is formed by:","Pancreas को endocrine भाग केबाट बनेको हुन्छ?",["Islets of Langerhans","Acinar ducts","Bile canaliculi","Nephrons"],0,"Pancreatic islets contain endocrine cells that secrete insulin, glucagon and other hormones.","Pancreatic islet का endocrine cell ले insulin, glucagon लगायत hormone निकाल्छन्।"],["Which hormone increases blood glucose during fasting?","उपवासमा blood glucose बढाउने hormone कुन हो?",["Glucagon","Insulin","Calcitonin","Oxytocin"],0,"Glucagon stimulates hepatic glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis.","Glucagon ले liver मा glycogenolysis र gluconeogenesis बढाउँछ।"],["Aldosterone mainly increases renal reabsorption of:","Aldosterone ले मिर्गौलामा मुख्यतः कुन पदार्थको reabsorption बढाउँछ?",["Sodium","Glucose only","Urea only","Bilirubin"],0,"Aldosterone increases sodium reabsorption and potassium secretion in the distal nephron.","Aldosterone ले distal nephron मा sodium reabsorption र potassium secretion बढाउँछ।"],["ADH primarily increases:","ADH ले मुख्यतः के बढाउँछ?",["Water reabsorption in collecting ducts","Glucose filtration","Calcium loss in stool","Bile secretion"],0,"ADH increases water permeability in collecting ducts, concentrating urine.","ADH ले collecting duct मा पानी reabsorption बढाएर पिसाब गाढा बनाउँछ।"],["Which kidney structure filters plasma to form the initial filtrate?","Initial filtrate बनाउन plasma filter गर्ने kidney structure कुन हो?",["Glomerulus","Loop of Henle only","Collecting duct","Ureter"],0,"Glomerular capillaries filter plasma into Bowman's space.","Glomerular capillary ले plasma filter गरी Bowman's space मा पठाउँछ।"],["Which organ produces most circulating thyroid hormone?","Circulating thyroid hormone मुख्यतः कुन अंगले बनाउँछ?",["Thyroid gland","Adrenal medulla","Pituitary posterior lobe","Pancreas"],0,"The thyroid gland produces mainly T4 and some T3.","Thyroid gland ले मुख्यतः T4 र केही T3 बनाउँछ।"],["Which pituitary hormone stimulates the thyroid gland?","Thyroid gland लाई stimulate गर्ने pituitary hormone कुन हो?",["TSH","ACTH","Prolactin","ADH"],0,"Thyroid-stimulating hormone from the anterior pituitary stimulates thyroid hormone synthesis and release.","Anterior pituitary को TSH ले thyroid hormone synthesis र release बढाउँछ।"],["Cortisol is produced by the:","Cortisol कहाँ उत्पादन हुन्छ?",["Adrenal cortex","Adrenal medulla","Thyroid follicles","Pancreatic beta cells"],0,"Cortisol is a glucocorticoid produced by the adrenal cortex.","Cortisol adrenal cortex ले बनाउने glucocorticoid हो।"],["The neurotransmitter released at most parasympathetic postganglionic endings is:","धेरैजसो parasympathetic postganglionic ending मा कुन neurotransmitter निस्कन्छ?",["Acetylcholine","Noradrenaline","Dopamine only","Serotonin only"],0,"Parasympathetic postganglionic neurons usually release acetylcholine.","Parasympathetic postganglionic neuron ले सामान्यतया acetylcholine निकाल्छ।"],["The neurotransmitter released by most sympathetic postganglionic neurons is:","धेरैजसो sympathetic postganglionic neuron ले कुन neurotransmitter निकाल्छ?",["Noradrenaline","Acetylcholine only","GABA","Histamine"],0,"Most sympathetic postganglionic neurons release noradrenaline; important exceptions exist, such as sweat glands.","धेरै sympathetic postganglionic neuron ले noradrenaline निकाल्छन्; sweat gland जस्ता अपवाद हुन्छन्।"],["Which part of the brain helps coordinate balance and posture?","सन्तुलन र posture मिलाउन brain को कुन भागले सहयोग गर्छ?",["Cerebellum","Medulla only","Hypothalamus","Occipital cortex"],0,"The cerebellum coordinates movement, balance and posture.","Cerebellum ले movement, balance र posture समन्वय गर्छ।"],["The medulla oblongata contains centres important for:","Medulla oblongata मा कुन महत्त्वपूर्ण केन्द्र हुन्छन्?",["Respiration and cardiovascular regulation","Vision and hearing interpretation only","Voluntary speech only","Smell only"],0,"The medulla contains vital autonomic centres involved in breathing and cardiovascular control.","Medulla मा श्वासप्रश्वास र cardiovascular नियन्त्रणका vital autonomic centre हुन्छन्।"],["Which cranial nerve carries visual information?","दृष्टि सूचना बोक्ने cranial nerve कुन हो?",["Optic nerve (II)","Oculomotor nerve (III)","Trigeminal nerve (V)","Facial nerve (VII)"],0,"The optic nerve is cranial nerve II and carries visual signals from the retina.","Optic nerve cranial nerve II हो र retina बाट दृश्य सूचना लैजान्छ।"],["The receptor cells for hearing are located in the:","सुन्ने receptor cell कहाँ हुन्छन्?",["Organ of Corti","Retina","Olfactory epithelium","Semicircular canal cupula only"],0,"Hair cells in the organ of Corti transduce sound vibrations into neural signals.","Organ of Corti का hair cell ले sound vibration लाई neural signal मा बदल्छन्।"],["The retina contains photoreceptors called:","Retina मा हुने photoreceptor लाई के भनिन्छ?",["Rods and cones","Osteocytes and osteoblasts","Nephrons","Alveoli"],0,"Rods support dim-light vision; cones support colour and high-acuity vision.","Rod ले कम प्रकाशमा र cone ले रंग तथा स्पष्ट दृष्टिमा सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Which structure is primarily responsible for balance sensing during angular head movement?","टाउको घुम्दा angular movement को balance महसुस गर्ने संरचना कुन हो?",["Semicircular canals","Cochlea","Tympanic membrane","Eustachian tube"],0,"The semicircular canals detect angular acceleration of the head.","Semicircular canal ले टाउकोको angular acceleration महसुस गर्छ।"],["Which embryonic germ layer gives rise to the nervous system?","Nervous system कुन embryonic germ layer बाट विकास हुन्छ?",["Ectoderm","Mesoderm","Endoderm","Trophoblast only"],0,"The neural tube develops from ectoderm and forms the central nervous system.","Neural tube ectoderm बाट बनेर CNS विकास गर्छ।"],["Which germ layer gives rise to much of the muscle and connective tissue?","धेरै muscle र connective tissue कुन germ layer बाट बन्छ?",["Mesoderm","Ectoderm","Endoderm","Amnion"],0,"Mesoderm gives rise to muscle, bone, connective tissue and much of the cardiovascular system.","Mesoderm बाट muscle, bone, connective tissue र धेरै cardiovascular system बन्छ।"],["Which germ layer forms the epithelial lining of much of the gastrointestinal tract?","धेरै gastrointestinal tract को epithelial lining कुन germ layer बाट बन्छ?",["Endoderm","Ectoderm","Mesoderm","Neural crest only"],0,"Endoderm forms much of the epithelial lining of the digestive and respiratory tracts.","Endoderm ले digestive र respiratory tract को धेरै epithelial lining बनाउँछ।"],["The hormone that maintains the corpus luteum in early pregnancy is:","प्रारम्भिक गर्भावस्थामा corpus luteum कायम राख्ने hormone कुन हो?",["Human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG)","TSH","Insulin","Aldosterone"],0,"Embryonic trophoblast produces hCG, which supports the corpus luteum in early pregnancy.","Embryonic trophoblast ले hCG बनाउँछ र प्रारम्भिक गर्भावस्थामा corpus luteum कायम राख्छ।"],["Which phase of the menstrual cycle is dominated by progesterone after ovulation?","Ovulation पछि progesterone प्रमुख हुने menstrual cycle को चरण कुन हो?",["Luteal phase","Follicular phase","Menstrual phase only","Prepubertal phase"],0,"The corpus luteum secretes progesterone during the luteal phase.","Luteal phase मा corpus luteum ले progesterone निकाल्छ।"],["Which structure connects the developing fetus to the placenta?","विकास हुँदै गरेको fetus लाई placenta सँग जोड्ने संरचना कुन हो?",["Umbilical cord","Fallopian tube","Cervix","Amniotic sac wall only"],0,"The umbilical cord contains vessels connecting fetal circulation with the placenta.","Umbilical cord का vessel ले fetal circulation लाई placenta सँग जोड्छन्।"]]);
 for(const r of anatomyBatch) Q.push([r[0],r[1],r[2],r[3],r[4],r[5],"Human Anatomy & Physiology"]);

 // Biochemistry, Haematology, Blood Banking & Microbiology – NHPC 2021 study batch.
 notes.push(...[["Carbohydrates","Carbohydrates provide about 4 kcal/g. Monosaccharides include glucose, fructose and galactose; disaccharides include sucrose, lactose and maltose; polysaccharides include starch and glycogen.","Carbohydrate ले करिब ४ kcal/g ऊर्जा दिन्छ। Glucose, fructose र galactose monosaccharide हुन्; starch र glycogen polysaccharide हुन्।"],["Protein","Proteins are polymers of amino acids joined by peptide bonds. They support tissue repair, enzymes, transport, immunity and fluid balance; 1 g provides about 4 kcal.","Protein amino acid बाट बनेको हुन्छ र peptide bond ले जोडिन्छ। Tissue repair, enzyme, transport, immunity र fluid balance मा काम गर्छ; १ g ले करिब ४ kcal दिन्छ।"],["Lipids","Triglycerides are the major storage form of fat. Lipids provide about 9 kcal/g, form cell membranes and aid absorption of fat-soluble vitamins A, D, E and K.","Triglyceride शरीरमा बोसो भण्डारणको मुख्य रूप हो। Lipid ले करिब ९ kcal/g दिन्छ, cell membrane बनाउँछ र A, D, E, K अवशोषणमा सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Enzymes","Enzymes are biological catalysts that lower activation energy. Their activity is affected by temperature, pH, substrate concentration and inhibitors.","Enzyme जैविक catalyst हो जसले activation energy घटाउँछ। तापक्रम, pH, substrate र inhibitor ले यसको काममा असर गर्छ।"],["Carbohydrate digestion","Salivary and pancreatic amylase digest starch. Brush-border enzymes complete digestion into monosaccharides, which are absorbed through the intestine.","Salivary र pancreatic amylase ले starch पचाउँछन्। Intestinal brush-border enzyme ले monosaccharide बनाउँछन् र आन्द्राबाट अवशोषण हुन्छ।"],["Protein digestion","Pepsin begins protein digestion in the stomach. Pancreatic proteases and intestinal peptidases produce amino acids and small peptides for absorption.","पेटमा pepsin ले protein digestion सुरु गर्छ। Pancreatic protease र intestinal peptidase ले amino acid तथा साना peptide बनाउँछन्।"],["Fat digestion","Bile salts emulsify dietary fat; pancreatic lipase breaks triglycerides into absorbable products. Most lipid absorption occurs in the small intestine.","Bile salt ले बोसोलाई emulsify गर्छ; pancreatic lipase ले triglyceride पचाउँछ। बोसोको धेरैजसो अवशोषण सानो आन्द्रामा हुन्छ।"],["Glycolysis","Glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm and converts glucose to pyruvate, producing a net 2 ATP and 2 NADH per glucose molecule.","Glycolysis cytoplasm मा हुन्छ र glucose लाई pyruvate मा बदल्छ। प्रति glucose net २ ATP र २ NADH बन्छ।"],["Glycogen","Glycogenesis stores glucose as glycogen, mainly in liver and skeletal muscle. Glycogenolysis breaks glycogen down when glucose is needed.","Glycogenesis ले glucose लाई glycogen का रूपमा liver र muscle मा भण्डारण गर्छ। आवश्यक पर्दा glycogenolysis ले glycogen फुटाउँछ।"],["Insulin and glucagon","Insulin lowers blood glucose by promoting uptake and storage. Glucagon raises blood glucose mainly by stimulating hepatic glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis.","Insulin ले glucose uptake र storage बढाएर रगतको sugar घटाउँछ। Glucagon ले liver मा glycogenolysis र gluconeogenesis बढाएर sugar बढाउँछ।"],["Ketone bodies","Ketone bodies are produced by the liver from fatty-acid-derived acetyl-CoA, especially during prolonged fasting or insulin deficiency.","लामो उपवास वा insulin कमी हुँदा liver ले fatty acid बाट ketone body बनाउँछ।"],["Cholesterol","Cholesterol is a membrane component and precursor for steroid hormones, bile acids and vitamin D. It is transported in lipoproteins.","Cholesterol cell membrane को अंश हो र steroid hormone, bile acid तथा vitamin D को precursor हो। Lipoprotein ले बोकेर लैजान्छ।"],["Vitamins A and D","Vitamin A supports vision and epithelial integrity; deficiency may cause night blindness. Vitamin D supports calcium and phosphate absorption; deficiency causes rickets in children.","Vitamin A दृष्टि र epithelial tissue का लागि आवश्यक हुन्छ; कमीले night blindness हुन सक्छ। Vitamin D ले calcium/phosphate अवशोषण बढाउँछ; कमीले बालबालिकामा rickets हुन्छ।"],["Vitamins E and K","Vitamin E acts mainly as an antioxidant. Vitamin K is required for hepatic synthesis of several clotting factors, including II, VII, IX and X.","Vitamin E antioxidant हो। Vitamin K ले liver मा clotting factor II, VII, IX र X बनाउन सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Vitamin B12 and folate","Vitamin B12 and folate are required for DNA synthesis and normal red-cell production. Deficiency can cause megaloblastic anaemia; B12 deficiency may also cause neurological signs.","Vitamin B12 र folate DNA synthesis तथा RBC उत्पादनका लागि चाहिन्छ। कमीले megaloblastic anaemia हुन्छ; B12 कमीमा neurological समस्या पनि हुन सक्छ।"],["Iron metabolism","Iron is needed for haemoglobin synthesis. Most body iron is in haemoglobin; ferritin is a major storage form and transferrin transports iron in plasma.","Iron haemoglobin बनाउन चाहिन्छ। धेरै iron haemoglobin मा हुन्छ; ferritin भण्डारण र transferrin plasma मा transport गर्ने protein हो।"],["Calcium","Calcium is essential for bone, muscle contraction, nerve transmission and coagulation. Parathyroid hormone raises serum calcium.","Calcium हड्डी, muscle contraction, nerve transmission र coagulation का लागि आवश्यक हुन्छ। Parathyroid hormone ले serum calcium बढाउँछ।"],["Electrolytes","Sodium is the major extracellular cation; potassium is the major intracellular cation. Their gradients are essential for membrane potentials.","Sodium मुख्य extracellular cation हो र potassium मुख्य intracellular cation हो। यी gradient ले membrane potential कायम गर्छन्।"],["Acid–base balance","Normal arterial blood pH is approximately 7.35–7.45. Lungs regulate carbon dioxide rapidly; kidneys regulate bicarbonate and hydrogen ion over a longer period.","सामान्य arterial pH करिब 7.35–7.45 हुन्छ। फोक्सोले CO2 छिटो र kidney ले bicarbonate तथा hydrogen ion लामो अवधिमा नियन्त्रण गर्छ।"],["Metabolic acidosis","Metabolic acidosis is a primary fall in bicarbonate. Causes include lactic acidosis, ketoacidosis, renal failure and bicarbonate loss; respiratory compensation lowers PaCO2.","Metabolic acidosis मा bicarbonate प्राथमिक रूपमा घट्छ। Lactic acidosis, ketoacidosis, renal failure र bicarbonate loss कारण हुन्; compensation मा PaCO2 घट्छ।"],["Metabolic alkalosis","Metabolic alkalosis is a primary rise in bicarbonate, commonly associated with vomiting, gastric suction or diuretic use.","Metabolic alkalosis मा bicarbonate बढ्छ। Vomiting, gastric suction वा diuretic प्रयोग सामान्य कारण हुन्।"],["Liver function tests","Common liver-related tests include bilirubin, ALT, AST, ALP, GGT, albumin and prothrombin time. Interpret results with clinical findings.","Liver सम्बन्धी जाँचमा bilirubin, ALT, AST, ALP, GGT, albumin र prothrombin time पर्छन्। नतिजा बिरामीको अवस्थासँग मिलाएर बुझ्नुपर्छ।"],["Renal function tests","Serum creatinine, urea, estimated GFR and urinalysis help assess renal function. Creatinine is influenced by muscle mass and renal clearance.","Serum creatinine, urea, eGFR र urine test ले kidney function मूल्याङ्कन गर्छन्। Creatinine मा muscle mass र renal clearance को असर पर्छ।"],["Haemoglobin and haematocrit","Haemoglobin estimates oxygen-carrying pigment concentration; haematocrit is the proportion of blood volume occupied by red cells.","Haemoglobin ले oxygen बोक्ने pigment को मात्रा देखाउँछ; haematocrit ले रगतमा RBC ले ओगटेको volume को अनुपात देखाउँछ।"],["Red-cell indices","MCV reflects average red-cell volume, MCH average haemoglobin amount per cell, and MCHC average haemoglobin concentration in red cells.","MCV ले RBC को औसत आकार, MCH ले प्रति cell haemoglobin मात्रा र MCHC ले RBC भित्रको haemoglobin concentration देखाउँछ।"],["ESR","ESR measures the distance red cells settle in a vertical tube over one hour. It is a nonspecific marker influenced by inflammation, anaemia and other factors.","ESR ले एक घण्टामा tube भित्र RBC कति तल बस्छ मापन गर्छ। यो inflammation लगायत धेरै कारणले बदलिने nonspecific test हो।"],["Coagulation tests","PT/INR assesses the extrinsic and common pathways; aPTT assesses intrinsic and common pathways. Results must be interpreted with medication and clinical context.","PT/INR ले extrinsic र common pathway तथा aPTT ले intrinsic र common pathway जाँच्छ। औषधि र clinical अवस्था पनि विचार गर्नुपर्छ।"],["ABO blood groups","ABO type depends on A and B antigens on red cells and naturally occurring antibodies in plasma. Correct identification is essential before transfusion.","ABO group RBC मा A/B antigen र plasma मा हुने antibody मा आधारित हुन्छ। Transfusion अघि सही group पहिचान अनिवार्य छ।"],["Rh system","The D antigen is the most clinically important Rh antigen. Rh-negative pregnant patients may need anti-D prophylaxis according to clinical guidelines.","Rh system मा D antigen सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छ। Rh-negative गर्भवतीलाई guideline अनुसार anti-D prophylaxis आवश्यक पर्न सक्छ।"],["Crossmatching","Crossmatching checks donor-recipient compatibility before transfusion. It does not replace correct patient identification, sample labelling or bedside checks.","Crossmatching ले transfusion अघि donor र recipient compatibility जाँच्छ। यसले सही patient identification, sample labelling र bedside check लाई प्रतिस्थापन गर्दैन।"],["Blood components","Packed red cells improve oxygen-carrying capacity; platelets treat selected platelet deficiencies; plasma provides coagulation factors; cryoprecipitate is rich in fibrinogen.","Packed RBC ले oxygen carrying क्षमता बढाउँछ; platelet ले platelet कमीमा, plasma ले clotting factor कमीमा र cryoprecipitate ले fibrinogen दिन्छ।"],["Transfusion reaction","Stop a suspected transfusion reaction immediately, maintain IV access with compatible fluid per protocol, verify identity and notify the responsible clinical team and blood bank.","Transfusion reaction शंका भए तुरुन्त transfusion रोक्नुहोस्, protocol अनुसार IV access कायम राख्नुहोस्, पहिचान जाँचेर clinical team र blood bank लाई खबर गर्नुहोस्।"],["Bacteria","Bacteria are prokaryotes without a membrane-bound nucleus. They may be classified by shape, staining, oxygen requirement and other characteristics.","Bacteria prokaryote हुन् र membrane-bound nucleus हुँदैन। आकार, staining र oxygen आवश्यकता अनुसार वर्गीकरण गरिन्छ।"],["Culture media","Culture media provide nutrients for microbial growth. Selective media inhibit some organisms; differential media help distinguish organisms by visible reactions.","Culture media ले microorganism बढ्न पोषण दिन्छ। Selective media ले केही जीव रोक्छ; differential media ले देखिने reaction बाट छुट्याउन सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Gram stain","Gram-positive bacteria retain crystal violet and appear purple; Gram-negative bacteria take the counterstain and appear pink/red.","Gram-positive bacteria crystal violet राखेर बैजनी देखिन्छन्; Gram-negative counterstain लिएर गुलाबी/रातो देखिन्छन्।"],["Sterilisation and disinfection","Sterilisation destroys all forms of microbial life, including bacterial spores. Disinfection reduces or eliminates many pathogens on inanimate objects but may not destroy spores.","Sterilisation ले bacterial spore सहित सबै microbial life नष्ट गर्छ। Disinfection ले वस्तुमा भएका धेरै pathogen घटाउँछ तर spore नष्ट नहुन सक्छ।"],["Autoclave","Autoclaving uses saturated steam under pressure. A commonly used cycle is 121°C at about 15 psi for a validated holding time; follow device and load instructions.","Autoclave मा pressure सहित saturated steam प्रयोग हुन्छ। 121°C र करिब 15 psi सामान्य cycle हो; वास्तविक समय load र device validation अनुसार हुनुपर्छ।"],["Viruses and fungi","Viruses require living host cells for replication. Fungi are eukaryotes and include yeasts and moulds.","Virus बढ्न living host cell चाहिन्छ। Fungi eukaryote हुन्; yeast र mould यसमा पर्छन्।"],["Immunity","Innate immunity is rapid and nonspecific; adaptive immunity is antigen-specific and includes B-cell antibody responses and T-cell-mediated responses.","Innate immunity छिटो र nonspecific हुन्छ; adaptive immunity antigen-specific हुन्छ र B-cell antibody तथा T-cell response समेट्छ।"],["Biomedical waste","Segregate healthcare waste at the point of generation using the current national colour-coding and waste-management rules. Never recap contaminated needles by hand.","Healthcare waste उत्पादन भएको ठाउँमै हालको राष्ट्रिय colour coding अनुसार छुट्याउनुपर्छ। दूषित needle हातले recap गर्नु हुँदैन।"]]);
 const biochemBatch=[["What is the main storage form of carbohydrate in humans?","मानव शरीरमा carbohydrate भण्डारण हुने मुख्य रूप कुन हो?",["Glycogen","Cellulose","Lactose","Chitin"],"Liver and muscle store glucose mainly as glycogen.","Liver र muscle ले glucose मुख्यतः glycogen का रूपमा भण्डारण गर्छन्।"],["Which nutrient provides the highest energy per gram?","प्रति ग्राम सबैभन्दा बढी ऊर्जा कुन nutrient ले दिन्छ?",["Fat","Protein","Carbohydrate","Water"],"Fat provides about 9 kcal/g, compared with about 4 kcal/g for protein and carbohydrate.","Fat ले करिब ९ kcal/g दिन्छ; protein र carbohydrate ले करिब ४ kcal/g दिन्छन्।"],["Which enzyme begins starch digestion in the mouth?","मुखमा starch पचाउन सुरु गर्ने enzyme कुन हो?",["Salivary amylase","Pepsin","Trypsin","Lipase"],"Salivary amylase initiates starch digestion in the oral cavity.","Salivary amylase ले मुखमै starch digestion सुरु गर्छ।"],["Where does glycolysis occur?","Glycolysis कहाँ हुन्छ?",["Cytoplasm","Mitochondrial matrix","Nucleus","Lysosome"],"Glycolysis takes place in the cytoplasm.","Glycolysis cytoplasm मा हुन्छ।"],["What is the net ATP yield of anaerobic glycolysis per glucose?","Anaerobic glycolysis मा प्रति glucose net कति ATP बन्छ?",["2 ATP","4 ATP","30 ATP","36 ATP"],"Anaerobic glycolysis yields a net two ATP per glucose.","Anaerobic glycolysis बाट प्रति glucose net २ ATP प्राप्त हुन्छ।"],["Which hormone lowers blood glucose?","रगतको glucose घटाउने hormone कुन हो?",["Insulin","Glucagon","Cortisol","Adrenaline"],"Insulin promotes glucose uptake and storage, lowering blood glucose.","Insulin ले glucose uptake र storage बढाएर blood glucose घटाउँछ।"],["Which organ is the main site of urea synthesis?","Urea synthesis को मुख्य अंग कुन हो?",["Liver","Lung","Spleen","Skin"],"The liver converts toxic ammonia to urea through the urea cycle.","Liver ले urea cycle मार्फत ammonia लाई urea मा बदल्छ।"],["Which lipoprotein is commonly called good cholesterol carrier?","सामान्यतया good cholesterol carrier कुन lipoprotein लाई भनिन्छ?",["HDL","LDL","VLDL","Chylomicron"],"HDL participates in reverse cholesterol transport.","HDL ले reverse cholesterol transport मा भूमिका खेल्छ।"],["Which vitamin deficiency causes night blindness?","कुन vitamin को कमीले night blindness हुन्छ?",["Vitamin A","Vitamin C","Vitamin K","Vitamin B1"],"Vitamin A is essential for retinal photopigment function.","Vitamin A retinal photopigment का लागि आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["Which vitamin is essential for normal clotting-factor synthesis?","सामान्य clotting factor synthesis का लागि कुन vitamin आवश्यक हुन्छ?",["Vitamin K","Vitamin E","Vitamin C","Vitamin B6"],"Vitamin K is needed for gamma-carboxylation of several clotting factors.","Vitamin K धेरै clotting factor को gamma-carboxylation का लागि चाहिन्छ।"],["Deficiency of vitamin C causes which disease?","Vitamin C को कमीले कुन रोग हुन्छ?",["Scurvy","Rickets","Pellagra","Beriberi"],"Vitamin C deficiency causes scurvy, with impaired collagen formation.","Vitamin C कमीले collagen निर्माणमा समस्या भई scurvy हुन्छ।"],["Which vitamin deficiency is associated with megaloblastic anaemia?","Megaloblastic anaemia कुन vitamin को कमीमा देखिन्छ?",["Folate","Vitamin D","Vitamin E","Vitamin K"],"Folate deficiency impairs DNA synthesis and can cause megaloblastic anaemia.","Folate कमीले DNA synthesis बिगारेर megaloblastic anaemia गराउन सक्छ।"],["Which vitamin deficiency can cause neurological signs with megaloblastic anaemia?","Megaloblastic anaemia सँग neurological sign कुन vitamin कमीमा देखिन सक्छ?",["Vitamin B12","Vitamin C","Vitamin A","Vitamin K"],"Vitamin B12 deficiency can cause both megaloblastic anaemia and neurological dysfunction.","Vitamin B12 कमीले megaloblastic anaemia र neurological समस्या दुवै हुन सक्छ।"],["Which plasma protein transports iron?","Plasma मा iron बोक्ने protein कुन हो?",["Transferrin","Albumin","Fibrinogen","Globulin"],"Transferrin transports iron in plasma; ferritin stores it.","Transferrin ले plasma मा iron बोक्छ; ferritin ले भण्डारण गर्छ।"],["Which is the major extracellular cation?","मुख्य extracellular cation कुन हो?",["Sodium","Potassium","Magnesium","Phosphate"],"Sodium is the major cation in extracellular fluid.","Sodium extracellular fluid को मुख्य cation हो।"],["Which is the major intracellular cation?","मुख्य intracellular cation कुन हो?",["Potassium","Sodium","Chloride","Calcium"],"Potassium is the major intracellular cation.","Potassium intracellular fluid को मुख्य cation हो।"],["What is the normal arterial blood pH range?","सामान्य arterial blood pH कति हो?",["7.35–7.45","6.8–7.0","7.8–8.0","8.1–8.3"],"Normal arterial pH is tightly regulated around 7.35–7.45.","सामान्य arterial pH करिब 7.35–7.45 मा नियन्त्रण हुन्छ।"],["Which system provides rapid compensation for metabolic acid–base disorders?","Metabolic acid–base disorder मा छिटो compensation कुन system ले गर्छ?",["Respiratory system","Skeletal system","Integumentary system","Reproductive system"],"Ventilation changes PaCO2 rapidly to compensate for metabolic disturbances.","Ventilation परिवर्तन गरेर respiratory system ले PaCO2 छिटो बदल्छ।"],["A primary decrease in bicarbonate indicates which disorder?","Bicarbonate प्राथमिक रूपमा घटेमा कुन disorder हुन्छ?",["Metabolic acidosis","Metabolic alkalosis","Respiratory acidosis","Respiratory alkalosis"],"A fall in bicarbonate is the primary change in metabolic acidosis.","Bicarbonate घट्नु metabolic acidosis को प्राथमिक परिवर्तन हो।"],["Repeated vomiting most commonly predisposes to which acid–base disorder?","बारम्बार बान्ता हुँदा कुन acid–base disorder हुने सम्भावना बढी हुन्छ?",["Metabolic alkalosis","Metabolic acidosis","Respiratory acidosis","Respiratory alkalosis"],"Loss of gastric hydrochloric acid can cause metabolic alkalosis.","पेटको hydrochloric acid हराउँदा metabolic alkalosis हुन सक्छ।"],["Which enzyme is commonly used as a marker of hepatocellular injury?","Hepatocellular injury को marker का रूपमा कुन enzyme प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["ALT","Amylase","CK-MB","ALP only"],"ALT is relatively specific for hepatocellular injury, though interpretation needs context.","ALT hepatocellular injury मा उपयोगी हुन्छ, तर clinical context आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["Which test is commonly used to assess glomerular filtration?","Glomerular filtration मूल्याङ्कन गर्न कुन test उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["eGFR","Bleeding time","Serum amylase","ESR"],"Estimated GFR is used to assess kidney filtration function.","eGFR ले kidney को filtration function मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ।"],["Which red-cell index reflects average cell volume?","RBC को औसत आकार कुन index ले देखाउँछ?",["MCV","MCH","MCHC","RDW only"],"MCV is the mean corpuscular volume.","MCV भनेको mean corpuscular volume हो।"],["Which red-cell index reflects haemoglobin concentration within red cells?","RBC भित्रको haemoglobin concentration कुन index ले देखाउँछ?",["MCHC","MCV","ESR","PCV"],"MCHC estimates the average haemoglobin concentration in packed red cells.","MCHC ले packed RBC भित्रको औसत haemoglobin concentration देखाउँछ।"],["What does haematocrit measure?","Haematocrit ले के मापन गर्छ?",["Proportion of blood volume occupied by red cells","Platelet count","Plasma glucose","White-cell differential"],"Haematocrit is the fraction of blood volume occupied by red blood cells.","Haematocrit ले रगतको कति भाग RBC ले ओगटेको छ देखाउँछ।"],["ESR is usually reported as the distance red cells settle over what period?","ESR मा RBC बसेको दूरी सामान्यतया कति समयको आधारमा रिपोर्ट गरिन्छ?",["One hour","One minute","24 hours","Ten seconds"],"The Westergren ESR is commonly read after one hour.","Westergren ESR सामान्यतया एक घण्टापछि पढिन्छ।"],["Which test evaluates the extrinsic and common coagulation pathways?","Extrinsic र common coagulation pathway जाँच्ने test कुन हो?",["PT/INR","aPTT","Bleeding time","D-dimer only"],"PT/INR assesses the extrinsic and common pathways.","PT/INR ले extrinsic र common pathway मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ।"],["Which test evaluates the intrinsic and common coagulation pathways?","Intrinsic र common coagulation pathway जाँच्ने test कुन हो?",["aPTT","PT/INR","ESR","Reticulocyte count"],"aPTT assesses the intrinsic and common pathways.","aPTT ले intrinsic र common pathway जाँच्छ।"],["Which anticoagulant is commonly used for a full blood count sample?","Full blood count sample मा सामान्यतया कुन anticoagulant प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["EDTA","Sodium fluoride","Plain clot activator","Citrate for all tests"],"EDTA preserves cellular morphology and is commonly used for CBC specimens.","EDTA ले blood cell morphology जोगाउँछ र CBC मा प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],["Which anticoagulant is commonly used for coagulation testing?","Coagulation test का लागि कुन anticoagulant प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Sodium citrate","EDTA","Heparin for PT","Fluoride oxalate"],"Citrate binds calcium reversibly and is used for coagulation assays.","Citrate ले calcium लाई reversible रूपमा बाँध्छ र coagulation test मा प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],["Which ABO group has A antigen on red cells?","RBC मा A antigen हुने ABO group कुन हो?",["Group A","Group B","Group O","Group AB only"],"Group A red cells express A antigen and plasma usually contains anti-B.","Group A RBC मा A antigen हुन्छ र plasma मा सामान्यतया anti-B हुन्छ।"],["Which ABO group has both A and B antigens?","A र B दुवै antigen हुने ABO group कुन हो?",["Group AB","Group O","Group A","Group B"],"Group AB red cells express both A and B antigens.","Group AB RBC मा A र B दुवै antigen हुन्छन्।"],["Which ABO group has neither A nor B antigen on red cells?","RBC मा A वा B कुनै antigen नहुने group कुन हो?",["Group O","Group AB","Group A","Group B"],"Group O red cells lack A and B antigens.","Group O RBC मा A र B antigen हुँदैन।"],["Which Rh antigen is most clinically significant?","Rh system मा clinically सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण antigen कुन हो?",["D antigen","C antigen only","E antigen only","Lewis antigen"],"The D antigen is the principal antigen used to define Rh-positive status.","D antigen ले Rh-positive status निर्धारण गर्न मुख्य भूमिका खेल्छ।"],["What is the main purpose of crossmatching?","Crossmatching को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["Check donor-recipient compatibility","Measure haemoglobin","Count platelets","Detect urine glucose"],"Crossmatching checks compatibility before a blood component is issued for transfusion.","Transfusion अघि donor र recipient को compatibility जाँच्नु crossmatching को उद्देश्य हो।"],["Which blood component is primarily used to increase oxygen-carrying capacity?","Oxygen बोक्ने क्षमता बढाउन मुख्यतः कुन blood component दिइन्छ?",["Packed red blood cells","Platelet concentrate","Cryoprecipitate","Albumin"],"Packed red cells increase haemoglobin and oxygen-carrying capacity.","Packed RBC ले haemoglobin र oxygen carrying capacity बढाउँछ।"],["Which component is rich in fibrinogen?","Fibrinogen धेरै हुने blood component कुन हो?",["Cryoprecipitate","Packed red cells","Washed red cells","Platelet-poor plasma"],"Cryoprecipitate is concentrated in fibrinogen and selected clotting proteins.","Cryoprecipitate मा fibrinogen र केही clotting protein धेरै हुन्छ।"],["What is the first action when an acute transfusion reaction is suspected?","Acute transfusion reaction शंका हुँदा पहिलो काम के हो?",["Stop the transfusion","Increase the transfusion rate","Discard the blood bag immediately without reporting","Give the next unit"],"Stop the transfusion immediately and follow the institutional reaction protocol.","Transfusion तुरुन्त रोक्नुहोस् र संस्थाको reaction protocol पालना गर्नुहोस्।"],["Bacteria are classified as which type of cell?","Bacteria कुन प्रकारको cell हुन्?",["Prokaryotic","Eukaryotic","Acellular virus","Multicellular animal"],"Bacteria are prokaryotes and lack a membrane-bound nucleus.","Bacteria prokaryote हुन् र membrane-bound nucleus हुँदैन।"],["Which stain differentiates Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria?","Gram-positive र Gram-negative छुट्याउने stain कुन हो?",["Gram stain","Ziehl–Neelsen only","India ink","Wright stain"],"Gram staining differentiates bacteria by cell-wall properties and staining response.","Gram stain ले cell-wall विशेषता र staining response का आधारमा bacteria छुट्याउँछ।"],["Gram-positive bacteria typically appear what colour after Gram staining?","Gram stain पछि Gram-positive bacteria सामान्यतया कुन रङ देखिन्छन्?",["Purple","Pink","Green","Colourless"],"Gram-positive organisms retain crystal violet and appear purple.","Gram-positive ले crystal violet राख्ने भएकाले बैजनी देखिन्छन्।"],["Which organism requires living host cells for replication?","Replication का लागि living host cell चाहिने organism कुन हो?",["Virus","Most bacteria","Yeast","Protozoa"],"Viruses are obligate intracellular agents and require host-cell machinery.","Virus obligate intracellular agent हो र host cell चाहिन्छ।"],["Which method uses saturated steam under pressure?","Pressure सहित saturated steam प्रयोग गर्ने विधि कुन हो?",["Autoclaving","Dry wiping","Filtration of air only","Pasteurisation only"],"Autoclaving uses pressurised saturated steam to achieve sterilisation.","Autoclaving ले pressure सहित saturated steam प्रयोग गरेर sterilisation गर्छ।"],["What does sterilisation achieve?","Sterilisation ले के गर्छ?",["Destroys all forms of microbial life including spores","Removes visible dirt only","Kills only enveloped viruses","Reduces odour"],"Sterilisation destroys all forms of microbial life, including bacterial spores.","Sterilisation ले bacterial spore सहित सबै microbial life नष्ट गर्छ।"],["What is the key difference between selective and differential media?","Selective र differential media बीच मुख्य फरक के हो?",["Selective inhibits some microbes; differential distinguishes visible reactions","Both are identical","Differential sterilises instruments","Selective is used only for viruses"],"Selective media suppress selected organisms; differential media show distinguishable biochemical reactions.","Selective media ले केही जीवको वृद्धि रोक्छ; differential media ले biochemical reaction छुट्याउँछ।"],["Which immune response is antigen-specific and develops immunological memory?","Antigen-specific र immunological memory हुने immune response कुन हो?",["Adaptive immunity","Innate immunity","Physical barrier only","Inflammation only"],"Adaptive immunity is specific and can generate memory through B and T lymphocytes.","Adaptive immunity specific हुन्छ र B तथा T lymphocyte मार्फत memory बनाउन सक्छ।"],["Which immunoglobulin is usually the first produced in a primary immune response?","Primary immune response मा सुरुमा बन्ने immunoglobulin कुन हो?",["IgM","IgG","IgA","IgE"],"IgM is generally the first antibody produced in a primary response.","Primary response मा सामान्यतया IgM पहिलो antibody हो।"],["Where should healthcare waste be segregated?","Healthcare waste कहाँ छुट्याउनुपर्छ?",["At the point of generation","At the end of the week","After mixing all waste","Only at the landfill"],"Segregation at the point of generation reduces exposure and supports safe disposal.","उत्पादन भएकै ठाउँमा छुट्याउँदा exposure घट्छ र सुरक्षित disposal सम्भव हुन्छ।"],["Which practice is safest for a used contaminated needle?","प्रयोग भइसकेको दूषित needle का लागि सुरक्षित अभ्यास कुन हो?",["Discard immediately into an approved sharps container","Recap with both hands","Bend it by hand","Put it in general waste"],"Dispose of used needles directly into an approved puncture-resistant sharps container; avoid hand recapping.","प्रयोग भएको needle सिधै approved sharps container मा हाल्नुहोस्; हातले recap नगर्नुहोस्।"]];
const biochemMore=[["Which enzyme converts starch into maltose and smaller oligosaccharides?","Starch लाई maltose र साना oligosaccharide मा बदल्ने enzyme कुन हो?",["Amylase","Pepsin","Lipase","Nuclease"],"Amylase hydrolyses internal alpha-1,4 glycosidic bonds in starch.","Amylase ले starch को alpha-1,4 glycosidic bond तोड्छ।"],["Lactose is composed of which two monosaccharides?","Lactose कुन दुई monosaccharide बाट बनेको हुन्छ?",["Glucose and galactose","Glucose and fructose","Fructose and galactose","Two glucose molecules"],"Lactose is a disaccharide of glucose and galactose.","Lactose glucose र galactose मिलेर बनेको disaccharide हो।"],["Which sugar is commonly known as fruit sugar?","Fruit sugar भनेर कुन sugar लाई चिनिन्छ?",["Fructose","Glucose","Lactose","Maltose"],"Fructose is naturally abundant in fruits and honey.","Fructose फलफूल र महमा पाइने sugar हो।"],["Which pathway produces glucose from non-carbohydrate precursors?","Non-carbohydrate precursor बाट glucose बनाउने pathway कुन हो?",["Gluconeogenesis","Glycolysis","Glycogenesis","Pentose phosphate pathway only"],"Gluconeogenesis forms glucose from substrates such as lactate, glycerol and glucogenic amino acids.","Gluconeogenesis ले lactate, glycerol र glucogenic amino acid बाट glucose बनाउँछ।"],["Which organ is the major site of ketone-body production?","Ketone body उत्पादनको मुख्य अंग कुन हो?",["Liver","Skeletal muscle","Brain","Pancreas"],"The liver produces ketone bodies from fatty-acid-derived acetyl-CoA.","Liver ले fatty acid बाट बनेको acetyl-CoA प्रयोग गरी ketone body बनाउँछ।"],["Which plasma protein contributes most to colloid oncotic pressure?","Colloid oncotic pressure मा सबैभन्दा बढी योगदान दिने plasma protein कुन हो?",["Albumin","Fibrinogen","Haemoglobin","Transferrin"],"Albumin is the most abundant plasma protein and a major determinant of oncotic pressure.","Albumin सबैभन्दा धेरै पाइने plasma protein हो र oncotic pressure कायम राख्न महत्त्वपूर्ण छ।"],["Which amino acid is the precursor for nitric oxide synthesis?","Nitric oxide synthesis को precursor amino acid कुन हो?",["Arginine","Glycine","Valine","Methionine"],"Nitric oxide synthase converts L-arginine into nitric oxide and citrulline.","Nitric oxide synthase ले L-arginine बाट nitric oxide र citrulline बनाउँछ।"],["Which vitamin is required for collagen hydroxylation?","Collagen hydroxylation का लागि कुन vitamin चाहिन्छ?",["Vitamin C","Vitamin A","Vitamin D","Vitamin K"],"Vitamin C is a cofactor for prolyl and lysyl hydroxylases in collagen synthesis.","Vitamin C collagen synthesis मा prolyl र lysyl hydroxylase को cofactor हो।"],["Which vitamin deficiency is classically associated with beriberi?","Beriberi कुन vitamin को कमीमा हुन्छ?",["Thiamine (B1)","Riboflavin (B2)","Niacin (B3)","Pyridoxine (B6)"],"Thiamine deficiency causes beriberi and may cause Wernicke encephalopathy.","Thiamine कमीले beriberi र Wernicke encephalopathy हुन सक्छ।"],["Pellagra results from deficiency of which vitamin?","Pellagra कुन vitamin को कमीले हुन्छ?",["Niacin (B3)","Thiamine (B1)","Biotin (B7)","Cobalamin (B12)"],"Niacin deficiency causes pellagra, classically associated with dermatitis, diarrhoea and dementia.","Niacin कमीले pellagra हुन्छ; dermatitis, diarrhoea र dementia यसको classic लक्षण हुन्।"],["Which mineral is a central component of haemoglobin?","Haemoglobin को केन्द्रिय अंश कुन mineral हो?",["Iron","Iodine","Zinc","Calcium"],"Iron in the haem group binds oxygen reversibly.","Haem group को iron ले oxygen लाई reversible रूपमा बाँध्छ।"],["Iodine is essential for synthesis of which hormones?","Iodine कुन hormone बनाउन आवश्यक हुन्छ?",["Thyroid hormones T3 and T4","Insulin and glucagon","Cortisol and aldosterone","Adrenaline and noradrenaline"],"Iodine is incorporated into thyroid hormone molecules T3 and T4.","Iodine thyroid hormone T3 र T4 को अंश हो।"],["Which mineral is required for normal thyroid hormone synthesis?","सामान्य thyroid hormone synthesis का लागि कुन mineral आवश्यक हुन्छ?",["Iodine","Iron only","Sodium only","Copper only"],"Iodine is an essential substrate for thyroid hormone production.","Iodine thyroid hormone उत्पादनका लागि अनिवार्य substrate हो।"],["What is basal metabolic rate (BMR)?","Basal metabolic rate (BMR) भनेको के हो?",["Energy used at rest under basal conditions","Energy used only during exercise","Total energy in one meal","Energy stored as fat only"],"BMR is the energy expenditure needed to maintain vital functions at rest under defined basal conditions.","BMR भनेको निश्चित basal अवस्थामा आराम गर्दा vital function चलाउन चाहिने ऊर्जा हो।"],["Which macronutrient provides approximately 4 kcal per gram?","कुन macronutrient ले प्रति ग्राम करिब ४ kcal दिन्छ?",["Protein","Fat","Alcohol","Water"],"Protein provides about 4 kcal per gram; carbohydrate also provides about 4 kcal/g.","Protein ले करिब ४ kcal/g दिन्छ; carbohydrate ले पनि करिब ४ kcal/g दिन्छ।"],["Which nutrient is essential for building and repairing body tissues?","शरीरका tissue निर्माण र मर्मतका लागि कुन nutrient आवश्यक हुन्छ?",["Protein","Water only","Cholesterol only","Sodium"],"Proteins supply amino acids for tissue growth, maintenance and repair.","Protein ले tissue वृद्धि, संरक्षण र मर्मतका लागि amino acid दिन्छ।"],["Which lipoprotein transports most dietary triglyceride from the intestine?","आन्द्राबाट dietary triglyceride मुख्यतः कुन lipoprotein ले लैजान्छ?",["Chylomicron","HDL","LDL","Albumin"],"Chylomicrons transport dietary triglycerides from intestinal cells through lymph and blood.","Chylomicron ले आन्द्राबाट dietary triglyceride lymph र blood हुँदै लैजान्छ।"],["Which organ stores the largest amount of glycogen in absolute terms?","कुल मात्राको हिसाबले सबैभन्दा धेरै glycogen कुन अंगमा भण्डारण हुन्छ?",["Skeletal muscle","Liver","Kidney","Heart"],"Total skeletal-muscle mass means muscle stores more glycogen overall, although liver has a higher concentration.","कुल muscle mass धेरै भएकाले शरीरमा समग्र glycogen muscle मा बढी हुन्छ; concentration भने liver मा बढी हुन सक्छ।"],["Which test is commonly used to assess long-term average glycaemia?","लामो अवधिको औसत blood glucose मूल्याङ्कन गर्न कुन test प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["HbA1c","Random urine ketone only","Serum sodium","Bleeding time"],"HbA1c reflects average glycaemia over roughly the preceding two to three months, interpreted with clinical context.","HbA1c ले करिब पछिल्ला २–३ महिनाको औसत glucose अवस्था देखाउँछ; clinical context आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["Which sample is commonly used for fasting plasma glucose measurement?","Fasting plasma glucose मापन गर्न सामान्यतया कुन sample प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Venous plasma after fasting","Saliva after meals","Hair sample","Sputum"],"Fasting plasma glucose is measured in a blood sample after the required fasting period.","आवश्यक fasting अवधि पूरा भएपछि लिइएको blood sample को plasma मा glucose मापन गरिन्छ।"],["Which substance is commonly measured to assess pancreatic exocrine injury in acute pancreatitis?","Acute pancreatitis मा pancreatic injury मूल्याङ्कन गर्न कुन पदार्थ मापन गरिन्छ?",["Lipase","Troponin","TSH","Bilirubin only"],"Serum lipase is commonly used in the assessment of acute pancreatitis.","Acute pancreatitis मूल्याङ्कनमा serum lipase प्रायः प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],["Which bilirubin fraction is water-soluble and conjugated in the liver?","Liver मा conjugate भएर water-soluble बन्ने bilirubin कुन हो?",["Direct bilirubin","Unconjugated bilirubin","Albumin-bound haem","Urobilinogen only"],"Conjugated bilirubin is water-soluble and is commonly measured as direct bilirubin.","Conjugated bilirubin पानीमा घुलनशील हुन्छ र direct bilirubin भनेर मापन गरिन्छ।"],["Which plasma electrolyte is the major extracellular anion?","मुख्य extracellular anion कुन electrolyte हो?",["Chloride","Potassium","Calcium","Magnesium"],"Chloride is the major extracellular anion and helps maintain electroneutrality and acid–base balance.","Chloride मुख्य extracellular anion हो र electroneutrality तथा acid–base balance मा सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Which electrolyte abnormality can cause dangerous cardiac arrhythmias?","कुन electrolyte असन्तुलनले खतरनाक cardiac arrhythmia गराउन सक्छ?",["Potassium disturbance","Mild chloride change only","Small phosphate variation only","Normal sodium"],"Both hypokalaemia and hyperkalaemia can cause serious cardiac rhythm disturbances.","Hypokalaemia र hyperkalaemia दुवैले गम्भीर cardiac rhythm समस्या गराउन सक्छन्।"],["Which buffer system is especially important in extracellular fluid?","Extracellular fluid मा विशेष महत्त्वपूर्ण buffer system कुन हो?",["Bicarbonate buffer","Phosphate buffer only","Ammonia buffer only","Haemoglobin only"],"The bicarbonate–carbonic acid system is the major extracellular buffer system.","Bicarbonate–carbonic acid system मुख्य extracellular buffer हो।"],["Respiratory acidosis is primarily caused by retention of which substance?","Respiratory acidosis मुख्यतः कुन पदार्थ जम्मा हुँदा हुन्छ?",["Carbon dioxide","Bicarbonate","Oxygen","Sodium"],"Alveolar hypoventilation causes carbon dioxide retention and raises PaCO2.","Alveolar hypoventilation ले carbon dioxide जम्मा गराएर PaCO2 बढाउँछ।"],["In respiratory alkalosis, arterial PaCO2 is usually:","Respiratory alkalosis मा arterial PaCO2 सामान्यतया कस्तो हुन्छ?",["Decreased","Increased","Always unchanged","Zero"],"Excessive alveolar ventilation lowers PaCO2, producing respiratory alkalosis.","अत्यधिक ventilation ले PaCO2 घटाउँछ र respiratory alkalosis हुन्छ।"],["Which blood cell is primarily responsible for oxygen transport?","Oxygen transport को मुख्य जिम्मेवार blood cell कुन हो?",["Red blood cell","Platelet","Neutrophil","Lymphocyte"],"Red blood cells contain haemoglobin, which transports most oxygen in blood.","RBC मा haemoglobin हुन्छ जसले रगतको अधिकांश oxygen बोक्छ।"],["Which white blood cell is usually the most abundant in normal adult peripheral blood?","सामान्य वयस्कको peripheral blood मा सबैभन्दा धेरै पाइने WBC कुन हो?",["Neutrophil","Basophil","Eosinophil","Monocyte"],"Neutrophils are usually the most abundant circulating white blood cells in adults.","वयस्कको circulating WBC मध्ये neutrophil सामान्यतया सबैभन्दा धेरै हुन्छ।"],["Which blood component is essential for primary haemostasis?","Primary haemostasis का लागि कुन blood component आवश्यक हुन्छ?",["Platelets","Red cells","Albumin","Eosinophils"],"Platelets adhere, activate and aggregate to form the initial platelet plug.","Platelet ले adhere, activate र aggregate भएर प्रारम्भिक platelet plug बनाउँछन्।"],["Which cell type is responsible for antibody production after differentiation?","Differentiation पछि antibody उत्पादन गर्ने cell कुन हो?",["Plasma cell","Neutrophil","Erythrocyte","Platelet"],"Activated B lymphocytes can differentiate into plasma cells that secrete antibodies.","Activated B lymphocyte plasma cell मा बदलिन्छ र antibody निकाल्छ।"],["What is reticulocyte count used to assess?","Reticulocyte count के मूल्याङ्कन गर्न प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Bone-marrow red-cell production response","Platelet function","Clotting factor activity","Serum sodium"],"Reticulocytes are immature red cells; their count helps assess marrow response to anaemia or blood loss.","Reticulocyte immature RBC हुन्; count ले anaemia वा blood loss मा bone marrow को response देखाउँछ।"],["Which test estimates the time taken for a clot to form in the traditional method?","परम्परागत विधिमा clot बन्न लाग्ने समय कुन test ले अनुमान गर्छ?",["Clotting time","Haematocrit","ESR","Blood grouping"],"Clotting time is a historical global screening test and has limited sensitivity compared with modern coagulation assays.","Clotting time पुरानो screening test हो र आधुनिक coagulation assay भन्दा कम संवेदनशील हुन्छ।"],["Which anticoagulant is used in blood collection bags for stored donor blood?","Donor blood भण्डारण गर्ने blood bag मा कुन anticoagulant-preservative प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Citrate-phosphate-dextrose (CPD) or approved additive systems","EDTA only","Plain water","Potassium oxalate only"],"Blood collection systems use approved anticoagulant-preservative solutions such as CPD-based formulations.","Blood bag मा CPD जस्ता स्वीकृत anticoagulant-preservative solution प्रयोग हुन्छन्।"],["What is the purpose of donor screening before blood collection?","रक्तदान अघि donor screening को उद्देश्य के हो?",["Protect donor and recipient safety","Increase blood viscosity","Determine recipient's blood group only","Replace crossmatching"],"Donor assessment helps protect donor health and reduce transfusion-transmitted infection risk.","Donor screening ले donor को स्वास्थ्य जोगाउँछ र transfusion बाट सर्ने संक्रमणको जोखिम घटाउँछ।"],["Which infection is routinely screened in donated blood according to national regulations?","राष्ट्रिय नियमअनुसार donated blood मा कुन संक्रमण screening गरिन्छ?",["HIV","Common cold virus only","Seasonal allergy","Hypertension"],"Blood services screen for specified transfusion-transmissible infections, commonly including HIV, hepatitis B/C and syphilis according to national rules.","Blood service ले राष्ट्रिय नियमअनुसार HIV, hepatitis B/C र syphilis लगायत transfusion-transmissible infection जाँच्छ।"],["Which blood component is most appropriate for severe thrombocytopenia with bleeding, when indicated?","Bleeding सहित गम्भीर thrombocytopenia मा आवश्यक परे कुन component उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Platelet component","Packed red cells only","Cryoprecipitate only","Albumin"],"Platelet transfusion may be indicated for severe thrombocytopenia with clinically significant bleeding, following guidelines.","गम्भीर thrombocytopenia र clinically significant bleeding मा guideline अनुसार platelet दिन सकिन्छ।"],["Which reaction is classically associated with ABO-incompatible red-cell transfusion?","ABO incompatible RBC transfusion सँग कुन reaction विशेष रूपमा सम्बन्धित छ?",["Acute intravascular haemolysis","Mild iron deficiency","Delayed wound healing only","Vitamin deficiency"],"ABO-incompatible red cells can trigger complement-mediated acute intravascular haemolysis.","ABO incompatible RBC ले complement-mediated acute intravascular haemolysis गराउन सक्छ।"],["Which microorganism is a fungus commonly associated with oral thrush?","Oral thrush सँग सम्बन्धित fungus कुन हो?",["Candida albicans","Escherichia coli","Plasmodium falciparum","Mycobacterium tuberculosis"],"Candida albicans is a yeast that can cause oral candidiasis, especially with predisposing factors.","Candida albicans yeast हो र जोखिम कारक हुँदा oral candidiasis गराउन सक्छ।"],["Which organism causes malaria?","Malaria कुन organism ले गराउँछ?",["Plasmodium species","Candida species","Staphylococcus species","Influenza virus"],"Malaria is caused by Plasmodium parasites transmitted by infected female Anopheles mosquitoes.","Malaria Plasmodium parasite ले गराउँछ र संक्रमित female Anopheles लामखुट्टेबाट सर्छ।"],["Which bacterium is classically associated with tuberculosis?","Tuberculosis सँग सम्बन्धित bacteria कुन हो?",["Mycobacterium tuberculosis","Streptococcus pyogenes","Vibrio cholerae","Clostridium tetani"],"Tuberculosis is caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis, an acid-fast bacillus.","Tuberculosis Mycobacterium tuberculosis नामको acid-fast bacillus ले गराउँछ।"],["Which stain is used to demonstrate acid-fast bacilli in a sputum smear?","Sputum smear मा acid-fast bacilli देखाउन कुन stain प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Ziehl–Neelsen stain","Gram stain only","Albert stain","Leishman stain"],"Ziehl–Neelsen staining is a classic method for demonstrating acid-fast bacilli.","Ziehl–Neelsen stain acid-fast bacilli देखाउने परम्परागत विधि हो।"],["Which culture medium is commonly used for Mycobacterium tuberculosis?","Mycobacterium tuberculosis culture गर्न कुन medium प्रयोग गरिन्छ?",["Lowenstein–Jensen medium","MacConkey agar","Sabouraud agar","Blood agar only"],"Lowenstein–Jensen is an egg-based medium used for mycobacterial culture.","Lowenstein–Jensen mycobacteria culture गर्न प्रयोग हुने egg-based medium हो।"],["Which organism is commonly used as an indicator for testing steam sterilisation efficacy?","Steam sterilisation को प्रभावकारिता जाँच्न कुन biological indicator प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Geobacillus stearothermophilus spores","E. coli vegetative cells","Candida yeast cells","Influenza virus"],"Highly resistant Geobacillus stearothermophilus spores are used as biological indicators for steam sterilisation.","Steam sterilisation जाँच्न प्रतिरोधी Geobacillus stearothermophilus spore biological indicator का रूपमा प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],["What is the most important routine measure to prevent healthcare-associated infection?","Healthcare-associated infection रोक्न सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण नियमित उपाय कुन हो?",["Correct hand hygiene","Routine antibiotic use for everyone","Recapping needles","Reusing disposable gloves"],"Hand hygiene at appropriate moments is a core infection-prevention measure.","उचित समयमा हात सफा गर्नु infection prevention को आधारभूत उपाय हो।"],["Which type of immunity is transferred from mother to infant through breast milk antibodies?","आमाको दूधका antibody बाट शिशुमा कुन प्रकारको immunity सर्छ?",["Passive immunity","Active immunity","Autoimmunity","Cellular rejection"],"Maternal secretory IgA in breast milk provides passive mucosal protection to the infant.","आमाको दूधमा रहेको secretory IgA ले शिशुलाई passive mucosal protection दिन्छ।"],["Which immunoglobulin is predominant in mucosal secretions?","Mucosal secretion मा मुख्य रूपमा पाइने immunoglobulin कुन हो?",["IgA","IgM","IgE","IgD"],"Secretory IgA is the major antibody in many mucosal secretions.","Secretory IgA धेरै mucosal secretion मा प्रमुख antibody हो।"],["Which microorganism is typically grown on Sabouraud dextrose agar?","Sabouraud dextrose agar मा सामान्यतया कुन microorganism बढाइन्छ?",["Fungi","Mycobacteria only","Viruses only","Red blood cells"],"Sabouraud dextrose agar is commonly used for fungal culture.","Sabouraud dextrose agar fungal culture का लागि प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],["What is the main purpose of a negative control in a laboratory assay?","Laboratory assay मा negative control को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["Detect background signal or contamination","Prove every sample is positive","Replace calibration","Increase test sensitivity automatically"],"A negative control helps identify background signal, contamination or nonspecific reactions.","Negative control ले background signal, contamination वा nonspecific reaction पहिचान गर्न मद्दत गर्छ।"],["Why should a blood specimen be correctly labelled at the bedside?","Bedside मै blood specimen सही label गर्नु किन आवश्यक छ?",["To prevent patient-identification and transfusion errors","To increase haemoglobin","To sterilise the sample","To avoid all laboratory testing"],"Correct bedside identification and labelling are critical safeguards against wrong-blood-in-tube and transfusion errors.","Bedside पहिचान र labeling ले गलत बिरामीको रगत नमुना तथा transfusion error रोक्न मद्दत गर्छ।"],["Which sample handling practice helps preserve blood-gas results?","Blood gas नतिजा सही राख्न कुन sample handling अभ्यास उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Collect anaerobically in a suitable heparinised syringe and analyse promptly","Leave sample open to air for an hour","Use an unlabelled plain container","Shake vigorously and delay analysis"],"Blood gases require an appropriate heparinised sample, minimal air contamination and prompt analysis per laboratory protocol.","Blood gas का लागि heparinised syringe, हावा नछिर्ने गरी collection र छिटो analysis आवश्यक हुन्छ।"]];
 biochemBatch.push(...biochemMore);
 for(let i=0;i<biochemBatch.length;i++){const r=biochemBatch[i],opts=r[2].slice(),correct=opts[0],answer=(i*3+1)%4;opts[0]=opts[answer];opts[answer]=correct;Q.push([r[0],r[1],opts,answer,r[3],r[4],"Biochemistry, Haematology, Blood Banking & Microbiology"]);}

 // Clinical Pathology module – first reviewed batch.
 notes.push(...[["Clinical pathology","Laboratory study of blood, urine, CSF and body fluids supports diagnosis, monitoring and treatment.","Blood, urine, CSF र body fluid को laboratory जाँचले diagnosis, monitoring र treatment मा सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Pre-analytical phase","Includes preparation, patient identification, collection, labelling, transport and storage; errors are common in this phase.","तयारी, patient identification, collection, labelling, transport र storage यसमा पर्छन्; यस चरणमा गल्ती धेरै हुन्छन्।"],["Patient identification","Use two approved identifiers and match the request form with the specimen at collection; bed number alone is insufficient.","Sample लिँदा दुईवटा स्वीकृत identifier प्रयोग गरी request form सँग मिलाउनुहोस्; bed number मात्र पर्याप्त हुँदैन।"],["Specimen labelling","Label immediately after collection in the patient's presence according to institutional policy.","संस्थाको नियमअनुसार बिरामीकै उपस्थितिमा sample लिएलगत्तै label गर्नुहोस्।"],["Specimen transport","Use leak-proof labelled containers and appropriate temperature and biohazard precautions; transport promptly.","Leak-proof labelled container र उचित तापक्रम/सुरक्षा अपनाएर छिटो पठाउनुहोस्।"],["Specimen rejection","Unlabelled, leaking, clotted, insufficient or unsuitable specimens may be rejected under laboratory policy.","Unlabelled, चुहिने, clot भएको, अपर्याप्त वा अनुपयुक्त sample अस्वीकार हुन सक्छ।"],["Haemolysis","Rupture of red cells releases intracellular contents into plasma or serum and may alter potassium, LDH and AST.","RBC फुटेर भित्रका पदार्थ plasma वा serum मा निस्कनु haemolysis हो; potassium, LDH र AST बदलिन सक्छ।"],["Serum and plasma","Serum is obtained after clotting and lacks most fibrinogen; plasma is obtained from anticoagulated blood and retains clotting factors.","Serum रगत जमाएपछि प्राप्त हुन्छ र fibrinogen हुँदैन; plasma anticoagulated blood बाट प्राप्त भई clotting factor राख्छ।"],["Urinalysis","Routine urinalysis includes physical inspection, reagent-strip chemistry and microscopy when indicated.","Routine urinalysis मा physical जाँच, reagent-strip chemical जाँच र आवश्यक परे microscopy पर्छ।"],["Urine specific gravity","Estimates urine concentration and renal concentrating ability; interpret with hydration and clinical status.","Urine concentration र kidney concentrating क्षमता अनुमान गर्छ; hydration र clinical अवस्थासँग बुझ्नुपर्छ।"],["Urine protein","Persistent proteinuria may indicate renal disease and requires clinical assessment and quantification.","लगातार proteinuria ले kidney रोग संकेत गर्न सक्छ; clinical assessment र quantification चाहिन्छ।"],["Urine microscopy","Sediment may contain RBCs, WBCs, epithelial cells, casts, crystals, bacteria and yeast.","Urine sediment मा RBC, WBC, epithelial cell, cast, crystal, bacteria र yeast हुन सक्छ।"],["Urinary casts","Casts form within renal tubules from a protein matrix and can help localise renal pathology.","Cast kidney tubule भित्र protein matrix बाट बन्छ र renal pathology बुझ्न सहयोग गर्छ।"],["CSF examination","CSF is collected by trained clinicians through lumbar puncture using aseptic technique; tests include cells, protein, glucose and microbiology.","प्रशिक्षित clinician ले aseptic lumbar puncture बाट CSF लिन्छन्; cell, protein, glucose र microbiology जाँचिन्छ।"],["CSF in bacterial meningitis","Often shows neutrophilic pleocytosis, raised protein and reduced glucose, but patterns vary.","Bacterial meningitis मा neutrophil र protein बढ्ने, glucose घट्ने हुन सक्छ; pattern फरक हुन सक्छ।"],["Sputum","A good sputum sample is deep-cough respiratory secretion rather than saliva; it supports microscopy and culture.","राम्रो sputum गहिरो खोकीबाट आएको secretion हो, थुक मात्र होइन; microscopy र culture मा प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],["Stool examination","May include macroscopic inspection, occult blood, ova/parasite microscopy, culture or antigen testing.","Stool मा macroscopic जाँच, occult blood, ova/parasite microscopy, culture वा antigen test हुन सक्छ।"],["Body fluids","Pleural, ascitic and synovial fluids may be tested for appearance, cell count, protein, glucose, crystals and culture.","Pleural, ascitic र synovial fluid मा appearance, cell count, protein, glucose, crystal र culture जाँचिन्छ।"],["Cardiac troponin","Troponin is the preferred biomarker of myocardial injury; interpret serial results with timing and clinical findings.","Troponin myocardial injury को प्रमुख biomarker हो; serial result, समय र clinical finding सँग बुझ्नुपर्छ।"],["ABG and pulse oximetry","ABG evaluates PaO2, PaCO2 and pH; pulse oximetry estimates oxygen saturation but not PaCO2 or pH.","ABG ले PaO2, PaCO2 र pH जाँच्छ; pulse oximetry ले oxygen saturation अनुमान गर्छ, PaCO2 वा pH होइन।"]]);
 const clinicalBatch=[["Which phase includes specimen collection and labelling?","Sample collection र labelling कुन चरणमा पर्छ?",["Pre-analytical","Analytical","Post-analytical","Audit"],"Collection and labelling occur before analysis.","Collection र labelling analysis अघि हुन्छ।"],["Safest patient identification before sampling?","Sample अघि सुरक्षित patient identification कुन हो?",["Two approved identifiers","Bed number only","Room number only","Guess"],"Two identifiers reduce wrong-patient errors.","दुई identifier ले गलत बिरामीको sample जोखिम घटाउँछ।"],["When should a specimen be labelled?","Sample कहिले label गर्नुपर्छ?",["Immediately at bedside","At end of shift","Before identification","After results"],"Immediate bedside labelling prevents mix-ups.","तुरुन्त bedside labelling गर्दा sample साटिँदैन।"],["Which specimen may be rejected?","कुन sample अस्वीकार हुन सक्छ?",["Unlabelled sample","Adequate labelled sample","Correctly transported sample","Valid sample"],"An unlabelled sample cannot be safely attributed to a patient.","Unlabelled sample बिरामीसँग सुरक्षित रूपमा जोड्न सकिँदैन।"],["Haemolysis means:","Haemolysis भनेको के हो?",["Rupture of red cells","Clot formation","Platelet production","WBC division"],"RBC rupture releases intracellular contents into plasma.","RBC फुट्दा भित्रका पदार्थ plasma मा निस्कन्छन्।"],["Which result can rise falsely with haemolysis?","Haemolysis हुँदा कुन result गलत बढ्न सक्छ?",["Potassium","Chloride only","Sodium only","Bicarbonate only"],"RBC contain potassium that leaks into the sample.","RBC भित्रको potassium cell फुट्दा sample मा निस्कन्छ।"],["Serum is obtained:","Serum कसरी प्राप्त हुन्छ?",["After blood clots","After adding EDTA","From urine","From saliva"],"Serum is the fluid remaining after clot formation.","रगत जमिसकेपछि बाँकी तरल serum हो।"],["Routine urinalysis commonly includes:","Routine urinalysis मा के पर्छ?",["Physical, chemical and microscopic assessment","ECG","Blood culture only","Spirometry"],"Urinalysis combines physical and chemical tests with microscopy when indicated.","Urinalysis मा physical, chemical र आवश्यक परे microscopy पर्छ।"],["Urine specific gravity estimates:","Urine specific gravity ले के अनुमान गर्छ?",["Urine concentration","Blood group","Platelet function","Lung capacity"],"It estimates how concentrated urine is.","यसले urine कति concentrated छ अनुमान गर्छ।"],["Persistent proteinuria may indicate:","लगातार proteinuria ले के संकेत गर्छ?",["Renal disease","Normal in everyone","Lung disease only","Blood group"],"Persistent urine protein requires assessment for kidney disease.","लगातार urine protein आए kidney रोगको मूल्याङ्कन चाहिन्छ।"],["Nitrite-positive urine may suggest:","Urine nitrite positive हुँदा के शंका हुन्छ?",["Nitrate-reducing bacteria","Virus only","Kidney stone always","No infection"],"Some urinary bacteria convert nitrate to nitrite.","केही urinary bacteria ले nitrate लाई nitrite मा बदल्छन्।"],["Leukocyte esterase indicates:","Leukocyte esterase ले के संकेत गर्छ?",["White blood cells","Glucose","Bilirubin","Albumin only"],"It is associated with white cells in urine.","यो urine मा WBC उपस्थितिसँग सम्बन्धित हुन्छ।"],["Clean-catch midstream urine helps reduce:","Clean-catch midstream urine ले के घटाउँछ?",["Contamination","GFR","Urine volume","Blood pressure"],"It reduces contamination from skin and distal urethral flora.","यसले बाहिरी flora बाट contamination घटाउँछ।"],["CSF is commonly collected by:","CSF सामान्यतया कसरी लिइन्छ?",["Lumbar puncture","Venepuncture","Catheterisation","Skin swab"],"Trained clinicians collect CSF by lumbar puncture.","प्रशिक्षित clinician ले lumbar puncture बाट CSF लिन्छन्।"],["Bacterial meningitis CSF often shows:","Bacterial meningitis को CSF मा के देखिन्छ?",["Neutrophils up, protein up, glucose down","Glucose high always","No cells","Only eosinophils"],"This is a classic pattern, though results can vary.","यो classic pattern हो तर नतिजा फरक हुन सक्छ।"],["Why process CSF urgently?","CSF किन तुरुन्त process गर्नुपर्छ?",["Avoid diagnostic delay","Change its colour","Sterilise it","Increase glucose"],"Prompt processing supports timely cell counts and microbiology.","छिटो process गर्दा cell count र microbiology समयमै हुन्छ।"],["A good sputum specimen should be:","राम्रो sputum sample कस्तो हुनुपर्छ?",["Deep-cough secretion","Saliva only","Water","Nasal mucus"],"Deep-cough sputum represents lower respiratory secretions better.","गहिरो खोकीको sputum ले lower respiratory secretion देखाउँछ।"],["Ova and parasite examination uses:","Ova र parasite जाँच्न कुन नमुना प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Stool","Serum","Hair","Pleural fluid"],"Stool microscopy can identify parasite eggs and cysts.","Stool microscopy बाट parasite का अण्डा र cyst देखिन्छन्।"],["Faecal occult blood detects:","Faecal occult blood ले के पत्ता लगाउँछ?",["Hidden blood in stool","Visible worms only","Bile salts","Stool pH"],"It detects blood not visible to the naked eye.","यसले आँखाले नदेखिने दिसाको रगत पत्ता लगाउँछ।"],["Pleural effusion analysis tests:","Pleural effusion मा कुन fluid जाँचिन्छ?",["Pleural fluid","CSF","Synovial fluid","Saliva"],"Pleural fluid analysis helps classify effusions and investigate causes.","Pleural fluid जाँचले effusion को प्रकार र कारण बुझाउँछ।"],["Synovial fluid crystals help diagnose:","Synovial fluid crystal ले कुन रोग पहिचानमा मद्दत गर्छ?",["Gout","Pneumonia","Hepatitis","Meningitis"],"Monosodium urate crystals support gout diagnosis.","Monosodium urate crystal ले gout diagnosis समर्थन गर्छ।"],["Preferred biomarker for myocardial injury?","Myocardial injury को प्रमुख biomarker कुन हो?",["Cardiac troponin","Albumin","ESR","Urine ketone"],"Cardiac troponin is the preferred biomarker.","Cardiac troponin प्रमुख biomarker हो।"],["Pulse oximetry does not measure directly:","Pulse oximetry ले प्रत्यक्ष के मापन गर्दैन?",["PaCO2","Oxygen saturation","Pulse estimate","Saturation trend"],"It estimates oxygen saturation, not carbon dioxide tension or pH.","यसले oxygen saturation अनुमान गर्छ, PaCO2 वा pH मापन गर्दैन।"],["Which test measures PaO2, PaCO2 and pH?","PaO2, PaCO2 र pH कुन test ले मापन गर्छ?",["Arterial blood gas","Urine microscopy","Stool culture","Lipid profile"],"ABG evaluates oxygenation, ventilation and acid-base status.","ABG ले oxygenation, ventilation र acid-base अवस्था जाँच्छ।"],["Which test detects bloodstream infection?","Bloodstream infection कुन test ले पत्ता लगाउँछ?",["Blood culture","Urine specific gravity","Haematocrit","ECG"],"Blood culture detects bacteraemia or fungaemia.","Blood culture ले bacteraemia वा fungaemia पत्ता लगाउँछ।"]];
 for(let i=0;i<clinicalBatch.length;i++){const r=clinicalBatch[i],opts=r[2].slice(),correct=opts[0],answer=(i*3+2)%4;opts[0]=opts[answer];opts[answer]=correct;Q.push([r[0],r[1],opts,answer,r[3],r[4],"Clinical Pathology"]);}

 const clinicalMore=[["Which part of the laboratory workflow includes result validation and reporting?","Result validation र reporting laboratory को कुन चरणमा पर्छ?",["Post-analytical","Pre-analytical","Analytical","Collection"],"Post-analytical work includes validation, reporting and communication of critical values.","Post-analytical चरणमा result validation, reporting र critical value जानकारी पर्छ।"],["A clotted EDTA sample for CBC should generally be:","CBC का लागि EDTA sample clot भएको छ भने सामान्यतया के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Reject and recollect","Report without comment","Use for blood culture","Dilute with water"],"Clotting traps cells and can invalidate the cell count; recollection is usually needed.","Clot हुँदा cell फस्छन् र count गलत हुन सक्छ; पुनः sample चाहिन्छ।"],["Which urine finding defines haematuria?","Haematuria कुन urine finding हो?",["Red blood cells in urine","Glucose in urine","Ketones in urine","Bilirubin in urine"],"Haematuria means red blood cells are present in urine.","Haematuria भनेको urine मा RBC हुनु हो।"],["Pyuria means:","Pyuria भनेको के हो?",["White blood cells or pus cells in urine","Glucose in urine","Protein in blood","Ketones in blood"],"Pyuria is the presence of white cells in urine.","Pyuria भनेको urine मा WBC वा pus cell हुनु हो।"],["Which test helps quantify albuminuria in chronic kidney disease assessment?","Chronic kidney disease मा albuminuria को मात्रा जाँच्ने test कुन हो?",["Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio","Bleeding time","Serum amylase","Pulse oximetry"],"Urine ACR detects and quantifies albuminuria.","Urine ACR ले albuminuria पत्ता लगाएर मात्रा देखाउँछ।"],["Which CSF pattern is more typical of viral meningitis?","Viral meningitis मा कुन CSF pattern बढी देखिन्छ?",["Lymphocyte predominance with usually preserved glucose","Neutrophils with very low glucose in every case","No white cells always","Only red cells"],"Viral meningitis often has lymphocytic predominance and relatively preserved glucose, with exceptions.","Viral meningitis मा प्रायः lymphocyte बढी र glucose तुलनात्मक रूपमा सामान्य हुन्छ।"],["Which test is used to identify bacteria and guide antibiotic choice?","Bacteria पहिचान र antibiotic छनोटमा सहयोग गर्ने test कुन हो?",["Culture and susceptibility testing","Specific gravity","Haematocrit","ECG"],"Culture identifies organisms and susceptibility testing guides antimicrobial selection.","Culture ले organism पहिचान गर्छ र susceptibility ले antibiotic छनोटमा सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Which sample is collected for suspected pulmonary tuberculosis testing?","Pulmonary tuberculosis शंका हुँदा कुन sample लिइन्छ?",["Sputum","Hair","Saliva after rinsing only","Urine only"],"Respiratory sputum is commonly collected for TB microscopy and molecular testing.","TB जाँचका लागि respiratory sputum सामान्यतया लिइन्छ।"],["Which stain is used for acid-fast bacilli in sputum?","Sputum मा acid-fast bacilli देखाउन कुन stain प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Ziehl–Neelsen","Gram","Wright","India ink"],"Ziehl–Neelsen staining demonstrates acid-fast bacilli.","Ziehl–Neelsen stain ले acid-fast bacilli देखाउँछ।"],["Which medium is classically used to culture Mycobacterium tuberculosis?","Mycobacterium tuberculosis culture गर्न कुन medium प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Lowenstein–Jensen","MacConkey","Sabouraud","Chocolate agar only"],"Lowenstein–Jensen is an egg-based medium for mycobacteria.","Lowenstein–Jensen mycobacteria का लागि egg-based medium हो।"],["Which culture is used to investigate infectious diarrhoea due to bacterial pathogens?","Bacterial pathogen का कारण भएको infectious diarrhoea जाँच्न कुन culture गरिन्छ?",["Stool culture","Blood film only","Urine culture only","CSF culture only"],"Stool culture can identify selected bacterial enteric pathogens.","Stool culture ले केही bacterial enteric pathogen पहिचान गर्छ।"],["Which test can detect hidden blood in stool?","दिसामा लुकेको रगत पत्ता लगाउने test कुन हो?",["Faecal occult blood test","Urine dipstick","PT/INR","Serum sodium"],"Faecal occult blood testing detects blood not visible to the eye.","Faecal occult blood test ले आँखाले नदेखिने रगत पत्ता लगाउँछ।"],["Which fluid analysis is relevant in suspected septic arthritis?","Septic arthritis शंका हुँदा कुन fluid analysis महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छ?",["Synovial fluid","Pleural fluid","CSF only","Ascitic fluid only"],"Synovial fluid cell count, microscopy and culture help investigate septic arthritis.","Synovial fluid cell count, microscopy र culture ले septic arthritis जाँच्न सहयोग गर्छ।"],["Which ascitic fluid parameter is central to assessing spontaneous bacterial peritonitis?","Spontaneous bacterial peritonitis मूल्याङ्कनमा ascitic fluid को कुन parameter मुख्य हुन्छ?",["Polymorphonuclear neutrophil count","Urine specific gravity","Serum troponin","Stool pH"],"Ascitic fluid neutrophil count is central to diagnosis.","Ascitic fluid neutrophil count diagnosis मा मुख्य हुन्छ।"],["A transudative pleural effusion is commonly associated with:","Transudative pleural effusion कुन अवस्थासँग सम्बन्धित हुन्छ?",["Congestive heart failure","Pneumonia","Pleural malignancy","Tuberculosis pleuritis"],"Heart failure commonly produces a transudative effusion.","Heart failure ले प्रायः transudative effusion गराउँछ।"],["An exudative pleural effusion may be caused by:","Exudative pleural effusion को कारण कुन हुन सक्छ?",["Pneumonia","Uncomplicated dehydration","Normal physiology","Simple fasting"],"Pneumonia and malignancy are common causes of exudative effusions.","Pneumonia र malignancy exudative effusion का सामान्य कारण हुन्।"],["Which blood test is commonly used to monitor long-term glucose control?","लामो अवधिको glucose control हेर्न कुन blood test प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["HbA1c","ESR","PT","Serum chloride"],"HbA1c estimates average glycaemic exposure over approximately 2–3 months.","HbA1c ले करिब २–३ महिनाको औसत glucose अवस्था देखाउँछ।"],["Which test is used to assess kidney filtration?","Kidney filtration मूल्याङ्कन गर्न कुन test प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Estimated GFR","Bleeding time","Troponin","Stool culture"],"eGFR estimates glomerular filtration function.","eGFR ले glomerular filtration function अनुमान गर्छ।"],["Which finding is a marker of myocardial injury?","Myocardial injury को marker कुन हो?",["Raised cardiac troponin","Low urine specific gravity","Positive stool occult blood","High urine ketone only"],"Cardiac troponin rises with myocardial injury and must be interpreted clinically.","Myocardial injury हुँदा cardiac troponin बढ्न सक्छ; clinical रूपमा बुझ्नुपर्छ।"],["A critical laboratory value should be:","Critical laboratory value आएमा के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Communicated promptly to the responsible clinician","Ignored until next visit","Deleted","Sent to another patient"],"Critical values require prompt communication and documentation under policy.","Critical value तुरुन्त सम्बन्धित clinician लाई जानकारी र documentation गर्नुपर्छ।"],["Which specimen container is suitable for routine stool collection?","Routine stool collection का लागि कुन container उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Clean, dry, leak-proof container","Open paper","Container with disinfectant","Unwashed jar"],"A clean, dry and leak-proof container limits contamination and leakage.","सफा, सुक्खा र leak-proof container ले contamination र leakage घटाउँछ।"],["Which test is most appropriate for assessing arterial acid-base status?","Arterial acid-base अवस्था जाँच्न कुन test उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Arterial blood gas","Urine microscopy","Stool microscopy","Lipid profile"],"ABG measures pH and respiratory and metabolic parameters.","ABG ले pH र respiratory तथा metabolic parameter जाँच्छ।"],["Which specimen is most suitable for routine urine culture?","Routine urine culture का लागि कुन नमुना उपयुक्त हुन्छ?",["Fresh clean-catch midstream urine","Old urine left open","Urine mixed with water","Urine from floor"],"Fresh clean-catch midstream urine minimises contamination.","Fresh clean-catch midstream urine ले contamination घटाउँछ।"],["Which laboratory phase includes analysis of the specimen on instruments?","Instrument मा sample जाँच्ने काम कुन चरणमा पर्छ?",["Analytical phase","Pre-analytical phase","Post-analytical phase","Patient preparation"],"The analytical phase is the actual testing or measurement process.","Analytical phase मा वास्तविक testing वा measurement हुन्छ।"],["Why must specimens be transported in leak-proof containers?","Sample leak-proof container मा किन पठाउनुपर्छ?",["To prevent exposure and contamination","To increase sample volume","To change test result","To avoid patient identification"],"Leak-proof transport protects staff, patients and the environment from biohazard exposure.","Leak-proof transport ले staff, बिरामी र वातावरणलाई biohazard exposure बाट जोगाउँछ।"]];
 for(let i=0;i<clinicalMore.length;i++){const r=clinicalMore[i],opts=r[2].slice(),correct=opts[0],answer=(i*3+1)%4;opts[0]=opts[answer];opts[answer]=correct;Q.push([r[0],r[1],opts,answer,r[3],r[4],"Clinical Pathology"]);}

 // Clinical Pathology: second expansion batch; 50 additional syllabus-linked questions.
 notes.push(
 ["Clinical pathology: cardiovascular markers","Cardiac troponins are preferred biomarkers of myocardial injury. Serial measurements and symptom timing matter. CK-MB may be useful in selected settings but is less specific. BNP/NT-proBNP support assessment of heart failure; ECG and clinical assessment remain essential.","Cardiac troponin myocardial injury को प्रमुख biomarker हो। Serial measurement र लक्षण सुरु भएको समय महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छ। CK-MB केही अवस्थामा उपयोगी भए पनि कम specific हुन्छ। BNP/NT-proBNP ले heart failure मूल्याङ्कनमा सहयोग गर्छ; ECG र clinical assessment पनि आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],
 ["Clinical pathology: anaemia and haemolysis","Anaemia is classified by morphology (microcytic, normocytic, macrocytic) and mechanism. Iron deficiency commonly causes microcytosis; vitamin B12 or folate deficiency may cause macrocytosis. Reticulocyte count reflects marrow response. Haemolysis may raise indirect bilirubin and LDH and lower haptoglobin.","Anaemia लाई morphology र कारणअनुसार वर्गीकरण गरिन्छ। Iron deficiency मा microcytic र B12/folate कमीमा macrocytic anaemia हुन सक्छ। Reticulocyte count ले bone marrow response देखाउँछ। Haemolysis मा indirect bilirubin र LDH बढ्न तथा haptoglobin घट्न सक्छ।"],
 ["Clinical pathology: coagulation profile","Platelets form the initial haemostatic plug. PT/INR is commonly used to monitor warfarin; aPTT may monitor unfractionated heparin according to protocol. Fibrinogen is converted to fibrin by thrombin. D-dimer reflects breakdown of cross-linked fibrin and is sensitive but non-specific.","Platelet ले प्रारम्भिक haemostatic plug बनाउँछ। Warfarin monitoring मा PT/INR र unfractionated heparin मा protocol अनुसार aPTT प्रयोग हुन सक्छ। Thrombin ले fibrinogen लाई fibrin बनाउँछ। D-dimer fibrin breakdown को सूचक हो तर specific हुँदैन।"],
 ["Clinical pathology: renal and electrolyte tests","Serum creatinine and eGFR help assess kidney filtration; urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio detects kidney damage. Sodium disorders can affect neurological function. Potassium abnormalities can cause dangerous arrhythmias. Interpret electrolytes with renal function, medicines, fluid status and sample quality.","Serum creatinine र eGFR ले kidney filtration बुझ्न मद्दत गर्छ; urine ACR ले kidney damage पत्ता लगाउन सहयोग गर्छ। Sodium गडबडीले स्नायु प्रणालीमा असर गर्छ। Potassium गडबडीले खतरनाक arrhythmia गराउन सक्छ। Electrolyte लाई renal function, औषधि, fluid status र sample quality सँग बुझ्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["Clinical pathology: respiratory and infection tests","ABG assesses pH, PaCO2, PaO2 and bicarbonate. Pulse oximetry estimates oxygen saturation but does not measure ventilation or PaCO2. Sputum Gram stain and culture may guide investigation of bacterial infection; TB testing follows national protocols and may include molecular assays.","ABG ले pH, PaCO2, PaO2 र bicarbonate जाँच्छ। Pulse oximetry ले oxygen saturation अनुमान गर्छ तर ventilation वा PaCO2 मापन गर्दैन। Sputum Gram stain र culture ले bacterial infection जाँच्न मद्दत गर्छ; TB परीक्षण national protocol अनुसार molecular assay सहित हुन सक्छ।"]
 );
 const clinicalExtra=[
 ["Which red-cell index reflects average cell size?","RBC को औसत आकार कुन index ले जनाउँछ?",["MCV","MCHC","Platelet count","ESR"],"MCV is mean corpuscular volume and reflects average red-cell size.","MCV ले RBC को औसत आकार जनाउँछ।"],
 ["Microcytic anaemia is commonly associated with deficiency of:","Microcytic anaemia सामान्यतया कुन तत्वको कमीमा हुन्छ?",["Iron","Vitamin B12","Vitamin D","Vitamin K"],"Iron deficiency is a common cause of microcytic anaemia.","Iron कमी microcytic anaemia को सामान्य कारण हो।"],
 ["Macrocytosis may occur in deficiency of:","Macrocytosis कुन vitamin को कमीमा हुन सक्छ?",["Vitamin B12","Vitamin C only","Sodium","Calcium"],"Vitamin B12 or folate deficiency can cause macrocytosis.","Vitamin B12 वा folate कमीले macrocytosis हुन सक्छ।"],
 ["Reticulocyte count helps assess:","Reticulocyte count ले के मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ?",["Bone marrow red-cell response","Kidney stone size","Liver size","Blood group"],"Reticulocytes indicate marrow response to anaemia or blood loss.","Reticulocyte ले anaemia वा blood loss प्रति marrow response देखाउँछ।"],
 ["Which result is commonly increased in intravascular haemolysis?","Intravascular haemolysis मा कुन परिणाम बढ्न सक्छ?",["LDH","Haptoglobin","Serum albumin always","Platelet lifespan"],"LDH is often increased due to red-cell destruction.","RBC नष्ट हुँदा LDH प्रायः बढ्छ।"],
 ["Which protein may decrease during intravascular haemolysis?","Intravascular haemolysis मा कुन protein घट्न सक्छ?",["Haptoglobin","Fibrinogen always","Troponin","Transferrin always"],"Free haemoglobin binds haptoglobin, reducing circulating haptoglobin.","Free haemoglobin ले haptoglobin बाँध्दा यसको मात्रा घट्न सक्छ।"],
 ["Which test is used to monitor warfarin therapy?","Warfarin therapy monitoring का लागि कुन test प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["PT/INR","Bleeding time only","Serum amylase","Urine ketone"],"PT/INR is used to monitor vitamin K antagonist therapy.","Vitamin K antagonist monitoring मा PT/INR प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],
 ["Which test may be used to monitor unfractionated heparin?","Unfractionated heparin monitoring मा कुन test प्रयोग हुन सक्छ?",["aPTT","HbA1c","ESR","Bilirubin"],"aPTT is commonly used, according to local protocol.","स्थानीय protocol अनुसार aPTT प्रयोग हुन सक्छ।"],
 ["D-dimer is a marker of:","D-dimer केको सूचक हो?",["Cross-linked fibrin breakdown","Glucose metabolism","Kidney filtration","Liver enzyme synthesis"],"D-dimer is produced during degradation of cross-linked fibrin.","Cross-linked fibrin टुक्रिँदा D-dimer बन्छ।"],
 ["Which protein is converted to fibrin during clot formation?","Clot बन्ने क्रममा कुन protein fibrin मा परिवर्तन हुन्छ?",["Fibrinogen","Albumin","Haemoglobin","Myoglobin"],"Thrombin converts fibrinogen into fibrin.","Thrombin ले fibrinogen लाई fibrin बनाउँछ।"],
 ["Which blood component forms the initial platelet plug?","प्रारम्भिक platelet plug कुन blood component ले बनाउँछ?",["Platelets","Erythrocytes","Albumin","Neutrophils"],"Platelets adhere and aggregate at the site of vessel injury.","रक्तनली चोट लागेको ठाउँमा platelet टाँसिएर जम्मा हुन्छन्।"],
 ["Which test estimates average glucose over about three months?","करिब तीन महिनाको औसत glucose देखाउने test कुन हो?",["HbA1c","Random urine protein","PT","Serum potassium"],"HbA1c reflects glycation over the red-cell lifespan.","HbA1c ले RBC को आयु अवधिको औसत glucose अवस्था देखाउँछ।"],
 ["Which electrolyte is especially important for cardiac electrical stability?","मुटुको electrical stability का लागि कुन electrolyte विशेष महत्त्वपूर्ण छ?",["Potassium","Chloride only","Phosphate only","Bicarbonate only"],"Potassium disturbances can cause serious cardiac arrhythmias.","Potassium गडबडीले गम्भीर cardiac arrhythmia गराउन सक्छ।"],
 ["Severe hyponatraemia may primarily cause:","गम्भीर hyponatraemia ले मुख्यतः के गराउन सक्छ?",["Neurological symptoms or seizures","Dental caries","High haemoglobin","Increased vision acuity"],"Low sodium can cause cerebral oedema and neurological symptoms.","Sodium कम हुँदा cerebral oedema र neurological लक्षण हुन सक्छ।"],
 ["Which test best estimates glomerular filtration in routine practice?","Routine practice मा glomerular filtration अनुमान गर्न कुन test उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["eGFR","Bleeding time","Troponin","Serum amylase"],"eGFR estimates filtration using creatinine and patient factors.","eGFR ले creatinine र बिरामीका विवरणबाट filtration अनुमान गर्छ।"],
 ["Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio is used to detect:","Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio के पत्ता लगाउन प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Albuminuria","Haemoglobinopathy","Pneumonia","Meningitis"],"Urine ACR detects and grades albumin loss in urine.","Urine ACR ले पिसाबमा albumin चुहावट पत्ता लगाउँछ र मात्रा वर्गीकरण गर्छ।"],
 ["A positive nitrite test in urine may suggest:","Urine nitrite positive हुँदा के शंका गर्न सकिन्छ?",["Certain bacterial urinary infection","Viral hepatitis","Heart attack","Anaemia"],"Some bacteria convert urinary nitrate to nitrite; a negative test does not exclude infection.","केही bacteria ले nitrate लाई nitrite बनाउँछन्; negative हुँदा पनि infection नकारिँदैन।"],
 ["Leukocyte esterase in urine indicates:","Urine मा leukocyte esterase ले के जनाउँछ?",["White blood cells","Glucose","Bilirubin","Ketones"],"Leukocyte esterase suggests white cells in urine.","Leukocyte esterase ले urine मा WBC हुन सक्ने संकेत गर्छ।"],
 ["Which urine cast is classically associated with glomerular bleeding?","Glomerular bleeding सँग कुन urine cast सम्बन्धित हुन्छ?",["Red-cell cast","Hyaline cast only","Fatty cast only","Waxy cast only"],"Red-cell casts suggest bleeding originating in the nephron, often glomerular.","Red-cell cast ले nephron, प्रायः glomerulus बाट bleeding भएको संकेत गर्छ।"],
 ["Which condition commonly causes nephrotic-range proteinuria?","Nephrotic-range proteinuria कुन अवस्थासँग सम्बन्धित हुन्छ?",["Glomerular disease","Simple dehydration only","Otitis externa","Asthma"],"Nephrotic syndrome involves heavy protein loss due to glomerular injury.","Glomerular क्षतिका कारण nephrotic syndrome मा धेरै protein निस्कन्छ।"],
 ["Which CSF feature may occur in bacterial meningitis?","Bacterial meningitis मा CSF को कुन विशेषता देखिन सक्छ?",["Neutrophil predominance and low glucose","High glucose in every case","No cells in all cases","Only eosinophils"],"Bacterial meningitis often produces neutrophilic pleocytosis and low CSF glucose.","Bacterial meningitis मा प्रायः neutrophil बढ्ने र CSF glucose घट्ने हुन्छ।"],
 ["CSF glucose should be interpreted alongside:","CSF glucose लाई कुन कुरासँग तुलना गरेर बुझ्नुपर्छ?",["Simultaneous blood glucose","Urine colour","Skin temperature","Stool pH"],"A paired blood glucose helps interpret the CSF-to-blood glucose relationship.","एकै समयमा लिइएको blood glucose सँग तुलना गर्दा CSF glucose बुझ्न सजिलो हुन्छ।"],
 ["Which CSF test can support diagnosis of subarachnoid haemorrhage?","Subarachnoid haemorrhage जाँचमा कुन CSF finding सहयोगी हुन सक्छ?",["Xanthochromia","Urine ketones","Sputum eosinophils","Stool occult blood"],"Xanthochromia may be seen after blood breakdown in CSF; clinical and imaging assessment are essential.","CSF मा रगत टुक्रिएपछि xanthochromia देखिन सक्छ; clinical र imaging जाँच पनि आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],
 ["A sputum sample consisting mainly of saliva is:","मुख्यतः र्‍याल भएको sputum sample कस्तो मानिन्छ?",["Poor-quality specimen","Ideal lower-airway specimen","Sterile sample","Blood culture"],"Saliva contamination reduces the usefulness of sputum microscopy and culture.","र्‍याल मिसिँदा sputum microscopy र culture को उपयोगिता घट्छ।"],
 ["Gram-positive bacteria retain which primary stain colour?","Gram-positive bacteria ले primary stain को कुन रङ राख्छ?",["Purple","Pink","Green","Yellow"],"Gram-positive organisms retain crystal violet and appear purple.","Gram-positive जीवले crystal violet राखेर बैजनी देखिन्छन्।"],
 ["Gram-negative bacteria typically appear:","Gram-negative bacteria सामान्यतया कस्तो देखिन्छन्?",["Pink or red","Purple","Black","Colourless always"],"They take the counterstain, commonly appearing pink or red.","Counterstain लिएर प्रायः गुलाबी वा रातो देखिन्छन्।"],
 ["Which medium is selective for many Gram-negative enteric bacilli?","धेरै Gram-negative enteric bacilli का लागि कुन medium selective हुन्छ?",["MacConkey agar","Sabouraud agar","Lowenstein–Jensen","Blood agar only"],"MacConkey agar selects many Gram-negative bacilli and differentiates lactose fermentation.","MacConkey agar ले धेरै Gram-negative bacilli छान्छ र lactose fermentation छुट्याउँछ।"],
 ["Which organism is classically acid-fast?","कुन organism acid-fast हो?",["Mycobacterium tuberculosis","Escherichia coli","Staphylococcus aureus","Candida albicans"],"Mycobacteria have lipid-rich cell walls and are acid-fast.","Mycobacteria को cell wall lipid-rich हुने भएकाले acid-fast हुन्छन्।"],
 ["Which test is commonly used for rapid molecular detection of pulmonary TB?","Pulmonary TB छिटो molecular रूपमा पत्ता लगाउन कुन test प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["WHO-recommended rapid molecular test such as Xpert MTB/RIF","ESR alone","Urine dipstick","Serum sodium"],"Rapid molecular assays detect TB genetic material and may assess rifampicin resistance.","Rapid molecular assay ले TB genetic material र rifampicin resistance जाँच्न सक्छ।"],
 ["Which stool finding may indicate intestinal inflammation?","दिसामा कुन finding ले intestinal inflammation जनाउन सक्छ?",["Faecal calprotectin elevation","Low serum troponin","Urine glucose","Low pulse rate"],"Faecal calprotectin is a marker of intestinal inflammation, not a standalone diagnosis.","Faecal calprotectin intestinal inflammation को marker हो, एक्लै diagnosis होइन।"],
 ["Which parasite stage may be identified by stool microscopy?","Stool microscopy मा parasite को कुन stage देखिन सक्छ?",["Ova and cysts","Platelet plugs","Red-cell casts","Alveoli"],"Stool microscopy may identify ova, cysts, larvae or trophozoites.","Stool microscopy मा ova, cyst, larva वा trophozoite देखिन सक्छ।"],
 ["Which test is used to assess occult gastrointestinal bleeding?","लुकेको gastrointestinal bleeding जाँच्न कुन test प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Faecal immunochemical test or occult blood test","PT only","ABG","Urine culture"],"FIT/FOBT detects blood not visibly apparent in stool.","FIT/FOBT ले दिसामा नदेखिने रगत पत्ता लगाउँछ।"],
 ["Ascitic fluid with elevated neutrophils raises concern for:","Ascitic fluid मा neutrophil बढ्दा कुन रोगको शंका हुन्छ?",["Spontaneous bacterial peritonitis","Asthma","Nephrolithiasis","Otitis media"],"An elevated ascitic neutrophil count is a key criterion for spontaneous bacterial peritonitis.","Ascitic neutrophil बढ्नु spontaneous bacterial peritonitis को मुख्य आधार हो।"],
 ["Synovial fluid crystals can help diagnose:","Synovial fluid crystal ले कुन रोग पहिचानमा मद्दत गर्छ?",["Crystal arthritis such as gout","Pneumonia","Hepatitis A","Pulmonary oedema"],"Monosodium urate crystals support gout; crystal identification must be interpreted clinically.","Monosodium urate crystal ले gout समर्थन गर्छ; clinical अवस्था पनि हेर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["Which fluid analysis is important in suspected pleural infection?","Pleural infection शंका हुँदा कुन fluid analysis महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छ?",["Pleural fluid pH, cell count and culture","Urine ketone only","Serum calcium only","Stool microscopy"],"Pleural pH, cell count, chemistry and culture help assess complicated infection.","Pleural pH, cell count, chemistry र culture ले जटिल infection मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ।"],
 ["Which biomarker is preferred for myocardial injury?","Myocardial injury का लागि कुन biomarker प्राथमिक हो?",["Cardiac troponin","ESR","Serum albumin","Urine protein"],"Cardiac troponin is preferred and interpreted with symptoms, ECG and serial testing.","Cardiac troponin प्राथमिक हो; लक्षण, ECG र serial test सँग व्याख्या गरिन्छ।"],
 ["BNP or NT-proBNP may support assessment of:","BNP वा NT-proBNP ले कुन अवस्थाको मूल्याङ्कनमा सहयोग गर्छ?",["Heart failure","Iron deficiency only","Urinary infection","Meningitis"],"Natriuretic peptides support assessment of suspected heart failure.","Natriuretic peptide ले heart failure शंका मूल्याङ्कनमा सहयोग गर्छ।"],
 ["Pulse oximetry may be misleading in the presence of:","कुन अवस्थामा pulse oximetry गलत हुन सक्छ?",["Poor peripheral perfusion or motion","Normal stable signal","Correct probe placement","Warm well-perfused finger"],"Motion, poor perfusion and some dyshemoglobins can affect readings.","Movement, कम perfusion र केही dyshemoglobin ले reading प्रभावित गर्न सक्छ।"],
 ["Which ABG value primarily reflects respiratory component?","ABG को कुन value ले respiratory component जनाउँछ?",["PaCO2","Serum albumin","Haematocrit","Platelet count"],"PaCO2 reflects alveolar ventilation and the respiratory component of acid-base balance.","PaCO2 ले alveolar ventilation र acid-base को respiratory भाग जनाउँछ।"],
 ["Which ABG value reflects metabolic component most directly?","ABG को कुन value ले metabolic component बढी प्रत्यक्ष जनाउँछ?",["HCO3−","PaO2","Pulse rate","Haemoglobin"],"Bicarbonate is used to assess the metabolic component of acid-base status.","Bicarbonate ले acid-base अवस्थाको metabolic भाग मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ।"],
 ["A low pH with raised PaCO2 suggests:","pH कम र PaCO2 बढेको छ भने के संकेत गर्छ?",["Respiratory acidosis","Respiratory alkalosis","Metabolic alkalosis","Normal acid-base status"],"Raised carbon dioxide with acidemia suggests respiratory acidosis.","CO2 बढेर pH घट्दा respiratory acidosis संकेत हुन्छ।"],
 ["A low pH with low bicarbonate suggests:","pH कम र bicarbonate कम हुँदा के संकेत गर्छ?",["Metabolic acidosis","Metabolic alkalosis","Respiratory alkalosis","Normal status"],"Reduced bicarbonate with acidemia suggests metabolic acidosis.","Bicarbonate घटेर pH कम हुँदा metabolic acidosis संकेत हुन्छ।"],
 ["Which condition can cause respiratory alkalosis?","कुन अवस्थाले respiratory alkalosis गराउन सक्छ?",["Hyperventilation","Hypoventilation","Severe diarrhoea","Renal bicarbonate loss"],"Excessive ventilation lowers PaCO2 and can cause respiratory alkalosis.","धेरै ventilation हुँदा PaCO2 घटेर respiratory alkalosis हुन सक्छ।"],
 ["Severe diarrhoea may cause which acid-base disorder?","गम्भीर पखालाले कुन acid-base disorder गराउन सक्छ?",["Metabolic acidosis","Metabolic alkalosis","Respiratory alkalosis","No possible change"],"Loss of bicarbonate-rich intestinal fluid can cause metabolic acidosis.","Bicarbonate भएको आन्द्राको fluid हराउँदा metabolic acidosis हुन सक्छ।"],
 ["Which sample is required for standard ABG testing?","Standard ABG परीक्षणका लागि कुन sample चाहिन्छ?",["Heparinised arterial blood","Clotted serum","Urine","EDTA stool"],"ABG requires an appropriately collected arterial blood sample, usually in a heparinised syringe.","ABG का लागि heparinised syringe मा उचित रूपमा लिइएको arterial blood चाहिन्छ।"],
 ["Air bubbles in an ABG syringe can:","ABG syringe मा हावाको bubble हुँदा के हुन सक्छ?",["Alter gas measurements","Improve accuracy","Sterilise the sample","Increase haemoglobin"],"Air contamination can change measured blood-gas values; handle and analyse promptly.","हावा मिसिँदा blood gas value बदलिन सक्छ; sample उचित रूपमा छिटो जाँच्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["Which test is most useful to detect bacteraemia?","Bacteraemia पत्ता लगाउन कुन test उपयोगी हुन्छ?",["Blood culture","Urine protein","ECG","Chest circumference"],"Blood culture can detect bacteria in the bloodstream.","Blood culture ले रगतमा bacteria पत्ता लगाउन सक्छ।"],
 ["Blood cultures should ideally be collected:","Blood culture आदर्श रूपमा कहिले लिनुपर्छ?",["Before antibiotics when feasible, without delaying urgent treatment","Only after completing antibiotics","From a used IV bag","After adding antiseptic into the bottle"],"Collect before antimicrobials when feasible, following aseptic technique and clinical urgency.","सम्भव भए antibiotic अघि aseptic technique अपनाएर लिनुपर्छ, तर urgent treatment ढिलाइ गर्नु हुँदैन।"],
 ["Which laboratory result requires immediate critical-value communication?","कुन laboratory result आएमा तुरुन्त critical-value जानकारी दिनुपर्छ?",["A result meeting the laboratory's critical threshold","Any normal result","A routine reference interval","A cancelled test"],"Critical thresholds are locally defined and must be communicated promptly with documentation.","Critical threshold स्थानीय laboratory ले तोक्छ; तुरुन्त जानकारी र documentation गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["Why is internal quality control performed?","Internal quality control किन गरिन्छ?",["To monitor analytical performance","To identify the patient by name","To replace calibration forever","To sterilise specimens"],"Quality control detects analytical shifts or errors before patient results are released.","Quality control ले बिरामीको result दिनुअघि analytical त्रुटि वा परिवर्तन पत्ता लगाउँछ।"],
 ["External quality assessment compares:","External quality assessment ले के तुलना गर्छ?",["A laboratory's performance with peer or reference results","Patient height with weight","Urine colour with stool colour","Only staff attendance"],"EQA evaluates laboratory performance against external comparison or reference material.","EQA ले बाह्य comparison वा reference material सँग laboratory performance मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ।"],
 ["A haemolysed sample may falsely increase which analyte?","Haemolysed sample मा कुन analyte गलत रूपमा बढ्न सक्छ?",["Potassium","Sodium always","Chloride always","Glucose always"],"Red-cell lysis releases intracellular potassium and can falsely elevate the result.","RBC फुट्दा intracellular potassium निस्केर result गलत रूपमा बढ्न सक्छ।"],
 ["Which anticoagulant is commonly used for a CBC sample?","CBC sample का लागि कुन anticoagulant सामान्यतया प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["EDTA","Sodium fluoride only","Plain tube only","Heparin always"],"EDTA preserves cellular morphology for routine blood counts.","EDTA ले routine blood count का लागि cell morphology जोगाउँछ।"],
 ["Which anticoagulant is commonly used for coagulation tests?","Coagulation test का लागि कुन anticoagulant प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Sodium citrate","EDTA","Oxalate only","No additive in all cases"],"Citrate binds calcium reversibly and is used at a specified blood-to-anticoagulant ratio.","Citrate ले calcium लाई reversible रूपमा बाँध्छ र निश्चित अनुपातमा प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],
 ["An underfilled citrate tube may:","Citrate tube कम भरिएको छ भने के हुन सक्छ?",["Prolong clotting times inaccurately","Always shorten PT","Improve sample quality","Increase platelet production"],"Excess citrate relative to plasma can prolong coagulation results falsely.","Plasma को तुलनामा citrate बढी हुँदा clotting time गलत रूपमा बढ्न सक्छ।"],
 ["Which blood group is the universal red-cell donor in emergency practice when group is unknown, subject to protocol?","Blood group थाहा नभएको emergency मा protocol अनुसार कुन RBC group प्रयोग हुन सक्छ?",["O negative","AB positive","A positive","B negative"],"O negative red cells may be used for emergency release under transfusion policy; compatibility testing follows.","Emergency release मा protocol अनुसार O negative RBC प्रयोग हुन सक्छ; पछि compatibility प्रक्रिया पालना हुन्छ।"],
 ["Which blood group is the universal plasma donor?","Universal plasma donor कुन blood group हो?",["AB","O","A","B"],"AB plasma lacks anti-A and anti-B antibodies in the usual ABO system.","सामान्य ABO प्रणालीमा AB plasma मा anti-A र anti-B हुँदैन।"],
 ["A suspected acute transfusion reaction requires first:","Acute transfusion reaction शंका हुँदा सबैभन्दा पहिले के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Stop the transfusion","Increase the transfusion rate","Discard the blood bag without reporting","Give the next unit immediately"],"Stop transfusion immediately and follow the institutional reaction protocol.","तुरुन्त transfusion रोक्ने र संस्थाको reaction protocol पालना गर्ने।"],
 ["Which finding may indicate an acute haemolytic transfusion reaction?","Acute haemolytic transfusion reaction को संकेत कुन हुन सक्छ?",["Fever, back pain and hypotension","Improved appetite","Mild thirst only","Hair loss"],"Acute haemolysis can cause fever, pain, hypotension, haemoglobinuria and shock.","Acute haemolysis मा ज्वरो, दुखाइ, hypotension, haemoglobinuria र shock हुन सक्छ।"],
 ["Which laboratory discipline studies tissues and cells for disease diagnosis?","रोग निदानका लागि tissue र cell अध्ययन गर्ने discipline कुन हो?",["Histopathology and cytology","Clinical chemistry only","Blood banking only","Parasitology only"],"Histopathology examines tissue architecture; cytology examines cells.","Histopathology ले tissue structure र cytology ले cell अध्ययन गर्छ।"],
 ["A biopsy specimen should be placed in the correct:","Biopsy sample कुन कुरामा सही रूपमा राख्नुपर्छ?",["Fixative and labelled container according to test","Open dry paper","Unlabelled water cup","Used disinfectant"],"Correct fixation and labelling preserve tissue and maintain traceability; some tests require fresh tissue.","सही fixation र labelling ले tissue जोगाउँछ; केही परीक्षणमा fresh tissue चाहिन्छ।"]
 ];
 for(let i=0;i<clinicalExtra.length;i++){const r=clinicalExtra[i],opts=r[2].slice(),correct=opts[0],answer=(i*3+2)%4;opts[0]=opts[answer];opts[answer]=correct;Q.push([r[0],r[1],opts,answer,r[3],r[4],"Clinical Pathology"]);}


 // Applied Pharmacology: foundational bilingual notes and first 50-question batch.
 notes.push(
 ["Applied pharmacology: scope and safe practice","Pharmacology studies drugs and their effects. Anaesthesia personnel must understand indications, contraindications, interactions, adverse effects, monitoring and institutional protocols. Prescribing and administration must remain within professional authorization.","Pharmacology ले औषधि र त्यसको प्रभाव अध्ययन गर्छ। Anaesthesia team ले indication, contraindication, interaction, adverse effect, monitoring र hospital protocol बुझ्नुपर्छ। औषधि prescribe/दिने काम आफ्नो अधिकार र जिम्मेवारीभित्र मात्र गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["Pharmacokinetics: ADME","Pharmacokinetics describes absorption, distribution, metabolism and excretion. Bioavailability is the fraction of an administered dose reaching systemic circulation unchanged. First-pass metabolism can reduce oral drug availability.","Pharmacokinetics मा absorption, distribution, metabolism र excretion (ADME) पर्छ। Bioavailability भनेको दिएको dose मध्ये unchanged रूपमा systemic circulation पुग्ने अंश हो। First-pass metabolism ले oral औषधिको उपलब्धता घटाउन सक्छ।"],
 ["Pharmacodynamics and receptors","Pharmacodynamics describes what a drug does to the body. Agonists activate receptors; antagonists block receptor activation. Potency and efficacy are different concepts: potency concerns dose, efficacy concerns maximum effect.","Pharmacodynamics ले औषधिले शरीरमा गर्ने प्रभाव बताउँछ। Agonist ले receptor सक्रिय गर्छ; antagonist ले रोक्छ। Potency र efficacy फरक हुन्: potency dose सँग र efficacy अधिकतम प्रभावसँग सम्बन्धित हुन्छ।"],
 ["Dose, half-life and therapeutic index","Half-life is the time required for plasma concentration to fall by half during elimination. A narrow therapeutic index means close monitoring may be needed. Loading and maintenance doses have different purposes and must be prescribed appropriately.","Half-life भनेको elimination हुँदा plasma concentration आधा हुन लाग्ने समय हो। Narrow therapeutic index भएका औषधिमा नजिकबाट monitoring आवश्यक पर्न सक्छ। Loading dose र maintenance dose का उद्देश्य फरक हुन्छन्।"],
 ["Autonomic pharmacology","Sympathetic effects are mediated by alpha and beta adrenergic receptors; parasympathetic effects mainly by muscarinic receptors. Drug effects depend on receptor selectivity, dose and patient condition.","Sympathetic प्रभाव alpha र beta adrenergic receptor बाट तथा parasympathetic प्रभाव मुख्यतः muscarinic receptor बाट हुन्छ। औषधिको प्रभाव receptor selectivity, dose र बिरामीको अवस्थाले निर्धारण गर्छ।"],
 ["Adrenergic agonists and emergency use","Epinephrine stimulates alpha and beta receptors and is a key medicine for anaphylaxis and cardiac arrest under current protocols. Norepinephrine is a potent vasopressor commonly used in distributive shock with close haemodynamic monitoring.","Epinephrine ले alpha र beta receptor उत्तेजित गर्छ र guideline अनुसार anaphylaxis तथा cardiac arrest मा महत्त्वपूर्ण औषधि हो। Norepinephrine शक्तिशाली vasopressor हो, distributive shock मा नजिकबाट haemodynamic monitoring सहित प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],
 ["Beta blockers","Beta blockers reduce beta-adrenergic effects. Depending on selectivity, they may reduce heart rate, contractility and blood pressure. Potential concerns include bradycardia, hypotension and bronchospasm with non-selective agents.","Beta blocker ले beta-adrenergic प्रभाव घटाउँछ। औषधिअनुसार heart rate, contractility र BP घट्न सक्छ। Bradycardia, hypotension तथा non-selective औषधिमा bronchospasm सम्भावित जोखिम हुन्।"],
 ["Calcium-channel blockers","Dihydropyridines mainly cause vascular smooth-muscle relaxation; non-dihydropyridines such as verapamil and diltiazem also slow AV nodal conduction. Hypotension and peripheral oedema can occur.","Dihydropyridine ले मुख्यतः रक्तनलीको smooth muscle relax गर्छ; verapamil र diltiazem ले AV nodal conduction पनि घटाउँछन्। Hypotension र peripheral oedema हुन सक्छ।"],
 ["Antiarrhythmic medicines","Antiarrhythmic drugs are grouped by their effects on ion channels and receptors. Selection depends on the rhythm, haemodynamic status, ECG, comorbidities and current resuscitation/cardiology guidance.","Antiarrhythmic औषधि ion channel र receptor मा हुने प्रभावअनुसार वर्गीकृत हुन्छन्। छनोट rhythm, haemodynamic अवस्था, ECG, सह-रोग र हालको guideline अनुसार हुन्छ।"],
 ["Nitrates and anti-anginal therapy","Nitrates such as nitroglycerin reduce preload mainly through venodilation and can relieve angina. They may cause headache and hypotension and are unsafe with phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitors because of severe hypotension risk.","Nitroglycerin जस्ता nitrate ले venodilation मार्फत preload घटाएर angina कम गर्न सक्छ। टाउको दुख्ने र hypotension हुन सक्छ; PDE-5 inhibitor सँग गम्भीर hypotension को जोखिमले प्रयोग गर्नु हुँदैन।"],
 ["Anticoagulants and thrombolytics","Anticoagulants reduce clot formation or extension; thrombolytics promote clot breakdown. They increase bleeding risk. Indications, contraindications, timing and laboratory monitoring depend on the specific agent and protocol.","Anticoagulant ले clot बन्ने वा बढ्ने प्रक्रिया घटाउँछ; thrombolytic ले बनेको clot फुटाउन सहयोग गर्छ। Bleeding risk बढ्छ। औषधिअनुसार indication, contraindication, समय र laboratory monitoring फरक हुन्छ।"],
 ["Anaesthetic agents","Propofol produces hypnosis but provides no reliable analgesia and may cause hypotension and respiratory depression. Ketamine provides dissociative anaesthesia with analgesia and may increase heart rate and blood pressure; individual responses vary.","Propofol ले hypnosis गराउँछ तर भरपर्दो analgesia दिँदैन; hypotension र respiratory depression हुन सक्छ। Ketamine ले dissociative anaesthesia र analgesia दिन्छ, heart rate/BP बढाउन सक्छ; व्यक्तिअनुसार प्रभाव फरक हुन्छ।"],
 ["Opioids and analgesia","Opioids act mainly at opioid receptors to provide analgesia. Important adverse effects include respiratory depression, sedation, nausea, constipation and dependence. Monitor ventilation and level of consciousness.","Opioid ले opioid receptor मार्फत analgesia दिन्छ। Respiratory depression, sedation, वाकवाकी, कब्जियत र dependence प्रमुख adverse effect हुन्। Ventilation र चेतनाको स्तर निगरानी गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["Neuromuscular blocking agents","Neuromuscular blockers cause skeletal muscle paralysis; they do not provide unconsciousness or analgesia. Adequate anaesthesia, airway control and quantitative neuromuscular monitoring are essential. Reversal is agent- and situation-dependent.","Neuromuscular blocker ले skeletal muscle paralysis गराउँछ; बेहोस वा pain relief गराउँदैन। पर्याप्त anaesthesia, airway control र quantitative monitoring आवश्यक हुन्छ। Reversal औषधि र अवस्थाअनुसार हुन्छ।"],
 ["Local anaesthetics and toxicity","Local anaesthetics block voltage-gated sodium channels. Systemic toxicity may cause circumoral numbness, tinnitus, seizures and cardiovascular instability. Prevention includes dose calculation, aspiration when appropriate, incremental injection and readiness to manage toxicity.","Local anaesthetic ले voltage-gated sodium channel block गर्छ। Systemic toxicity मा मुख वरिपरि झमझम, कान बज्ने, seizure र cardiovascular instability हुन सक्छ। Dose गणना, उपयुक्त aspiration, बिस्तारै injection र toxicity व्यवस्थापनको तयारी आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],
 ["Antiemetics, antihistamines and corticosteroids","Antiemetics act on pathways such as serotonin, dopamine or histamine receptors. Antihistamines block histamine receptors and may cause sedation. Corticosteroids reduce inflammation but can cause hyperglycaemia and increase infection risk with prolonged use.","Antiemetic ले serotonin, dopamine वा histamine pathway मा काम गर्छ। Antihistamine ले histamine receptor block गर्छ र निद्रा लाग्न सक्छ। Corticosteroid ले inflammation घटाउँछ तर glucose बढाउन र लामो प्रयोगमा infection risk बढाउन सक्छ।"],
 ["Diuretics and electrolyte balance","Loop diuretics increase sodium and water excretion and may lower potassium. Potassium-sparing diuretics can cause hyperkalaemia. Monitor renal function, fluid status and electrolytes when clinically indicated.","Loop diuretic ले sodium र पानीको निष्कासन बढाउँछ र potassium घटाउन सक्छ। Potassium-sparing diuretic ले hyperkalaemia गराउन सक्छ। आवश्यकताअनुसार renal function, fluid status र electrolyte जाँच्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["Antimicrobials and stewardship","Antibiotics treat susceptible bacterial infections, not viral illnesses. Choice depends on likely organism, infection site, allergy, renal/hepatic function, local resistance and culture results. Avoid unnecessary use and follow antimicrobial stewardship.","Antibiotic ले संवेदनशील bacterial infection उपचार गर्छ, viral रोग होइन। औषधि छनोट organism, infection site, allergy, kidney/liver function, स्थानीय resistance र culture अनुसार हुन्छ। अनावश्यक प्रयोग नगरी antimicrobial stewardship पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["IV fluids and electrolyte preparations","Crystalloids distribute through extracellular fluid; isotonic saline and balanced solutions are common examples. Fluid choice and volume depend on indication, losses, cardiac/renal function and reassessment. Potassium must never be given as an IV push.","Crystalloid extracellular fluid मा फैलिन्छ; normal saline र balanced solution उदाहरण हुन्। Fluid को प्रकार र मात्रा indication, loss, मुटु/मिर्गौलाको अवस्था र पुनर्मूल्याङ्कनमा निर्भर हुन्छ। Potassium कहिल्यै IV push दिनु हुँदैन।"],
 ["Medication safety and calculations","Use the medication rights, verify patient identity, allergy, drug, concentration, dose, route, timing and documentation. Check calculations independently for high-alert medicines. Never guess a dose; use the current prescription and institutional reference.","औषधि दिँदा patient identity, allergy, drug, concentration, dose, route, समय र documentation जाँच्नुपर्छ। High-alert औषधिमा गणना दोहोर्‍याएर जाँच्नुहोस्। Dose अनुमान नगरी हालको prescription र hospital reference पालना गर्नुहोस्।"]
 );
