 // Anaesthesia Technology expanded notes and first 50-question practice batch.
 notes.push(...[["31. Anaesthesia gas supply and cylinder safety","Medical gas cylinders are identified by the approved label and colour system used locally; never rely on colour alone. Secure cylinders upright, protect valves, check pressure and connections, and use the correct regulator. Pipeline supply, reserve cylinders and alarms must be understood. Oxygen supports combustion, so keep oil and grease away from oxygen equipment.","Medical gas cylinder लाई label र स्थानीय स्वीकृत colour system बाट चिनिन्छ; रङ मात्रमा भर पर्नु हुँदैन। Cylinder सुरक्षित राख्ने, pressure र connection जाँच्ने र सही regulator प्रयोग गर्ने। Oxygen ले आगो फैलाउन सहयोग गर्छ, त्यसैले oil/grease टाढा राख्नुपर्छ।"],["32. Flowmeters, vaporizers and oxygen failure protection","Flowmeters control gas flow and must be read correctly. Vaporizers are agent-specific, correctly filled and securely seated; check for leaks and interlock function. Oxygen failure protection and low-pressure alarms reduce risk but do not replace continuous vigilance. Never bypass a safety system or use a machine with an unresolved fault.","Flowmeter ले gas flow नियन्त्रण गर्छ। Vaporizer agent अनुसार सही भर्ने, जडान गर्ने र leak/interlock जाँच्ने। Oxygen failure protection र alarm उपयोगी भए पनि निरन्तर निगरानीको विकल्प होइन। सुरक्षा प्रणाली bypass गर्नु हुँदैन।"],["33. Breathing circuits and carbon dioxide absorption","Breathing systems may be circle, Mapleson or other designs. Understand fresh-gas flow, resistance, dead space, valves, reservoir bag and scavenging. In circle systems, carbon dioxide absorbent removes exhaled CO2; exhaustion, channeling or desiccation may cause rebreathing or abnormal reactions. Check canister seating and circuit integrity.","Breathing system circle, Mapleson आदि हुन सक्छ। Fresh gas flow, resistance, dead space, valve, reservoir bag र scavenging बुझ्नुपर्छ। Circle system मा CO2 absorbent ले निस्केको CO2 हटाउँछ; absorbent सकिएमा वा बिग्रिएमा rebreathing हुन सक्छ।"],["34. Capnography and interpretation","A normal capnogram has an inspiratory baseline near zero, an expiratory upstroke, alveolar plateau and inspiratory downstroke. End-tidal CO2 is influenced by ventilation, metabolism and pulmonary blood flow. A sudden loss of waveform may indicate disconnection, oesophageal intubation, complete obstruction or circulatory collapse; assess the patient and equipment immediately.","Capnogram मा baseline, expiratory upstroke, alveolar plateau र inspiratory downstroke हुन्छ। EtCO2 ventilation, metabolism र pulmonary blood flow बाट प्रभावित हुन्छ। Waveform अचानक हराएमा disconnection, गलत tube, obstruction वा circulation collapse हुन सक्छ।"],["35. Pulse oximetry limitations","Pulse oximetry estimates oxygen saturation, not ventilation or carbon dioxide. Motion, poor perfusion, cold extremities, nail products, dyshemoglobinaemia and device limitations can affect accuracy. Interpret the trend with waveform quality and clinical assessment; a reassuring saturation does not exclude hypoventilation when supplemental oxygen is used.","Pulse oximeter ले oxygen saturation अनुमान गर्छ, ventilation वा CO2 होइन। Movement, कमजोर perfusion, चिसो हातखुट्टा, nail product र device limitation ले accuracy घटाउन सक्छ। बिरामीको अवस्था र waveform सँगै हेर्नुपर्छ।"],["36. Non-invasive and invasive blood pressure monitoring","Cuff size and position affect non-invasive BP accuracy. An arterial line provides continuous beat-to-beat pressure and permits blood sampling but requires aseptic insertion, secure fixation, zeroing and leveling at the appropriate reference point. Check the waveform and transducer system; recognise damping and artefact.","Cuff को size र position ले NIBP accuracy असर गर्छ। Arterial line ले निरन्तर BP र blood sampling दिन्छ तर aseptic insertion, fixation, zeroing र सही level आवश्यक हुन्छ। Waveform र transducer जाँच्नुपर्छ।"],["37. ECG monitoring in theatre","ECG monitoring helps identify rate, rhythm and ischaemic changes but does not replace clinical assessment or a diagnostic 12-lead ECG when indicated. Ensure electrode contact and appropriate lead selection. Electrical interference, poor contact and movement may create artefacts. Report new arrhythmia or significant ST change promptly.","ECG ले heart rate, rhythm र ischaemic परिवर्तन पहिचान गर्न मद्दत गर्छ तर clinical assessment को विकल्प होइन। Electrode राम्रोसँग टाँस्ने र उपयुक्त lead छान्ने। नयाँ arrhythmia वा ST परिवर्तन तुरुन्त जानकारी दिनुपर्छ।"],["38. Temperature monitoring and prevention of hypothermia","Anaesthesia impairs thermoregulation and exposes patients to heat loss. Monitor temperature when indicated, minimise unnecessary exposure, warm fluids and use approved active warming devices. Hypothermia may contribute to coagulopathy, delayed drug metabolism, shivering and delayed recovery. Avoid burns and follow device instructions.","Anaesthesia ले शरीरको तापक्रम नियन्त्रण कमजोर बनाउँछ। आवश्यकताअनुसार temperature निगरानी, अनावश्यक exposure कम, fluid warming र approved warming device प्रयोग गर्नुपर्छ। Hypothermia ले bleeding, औषधि असर लम्बिने र recovery ढिलो गराउन सक्छ।"],["39. Fluid therapy and perioperative balance","Assess the patient's status, procedure, losses, comorbidities and laboratory results before fluid decisions. Crystalloids, colloids and blood components have different indications and risks. Monitor input, output, haemodynamics, electrolytes and signs of overload. Fluid choice and volume are individualised by the anaesthesia team.","Fluid निर्णयअघि बिरामीको अवस्था, surgery, loss, comorbidity र lab result हेर्नुपर्छ। Crystalloid, colloid र blood component का उपयोग र जोखिम फरक हुन्छन्। Input-output, BP, electrolyte र fluid overload निगरानी गर्नुपर्छ।"],["40. Blood transfusion safety","Confirm patient identity, prescription, component, compatibility documentation and expiry according to local policy. Use approved blood administration equipment and monitoring. If a reaction is suspected, stop the transfusion, maintain appropriate access, assess the patient and urgently notify the responsible team and blood bank; follow the institutional reaction protocol.","Blood transfusion अघि बिरामीको पहिचान, prescription, component, compatibility र expiry जाँच्नुपर्छ। Reaction शंका भए transfusion रोक्ने, बिरामी जाँच्ने र जिम्मेवार टोली तथा blood bank लाई तुरुन्त खबर गरी protocol पालना गर्ने।"],["41. Pre-anaesthetic airway assessment","Assessment includes history of difficult airway, mouth opening, dentition, jaw movement, neck mobility, facial features and relevant airway tests. No single bedside test predicts every difficult airway. Review aspiration risk, oxygenation reserve and available rescue devices. A documented plan should include help and backup strategies.","Airway assessment मा पहिलेको difficult airway, मुख खोल्ने क्षमता, दाँत, jaw, घाँटी चल्ने क्षमता र अन्य संकेत हेर्छ। कुनै एक test ले सबै difficult airway पहिचान गर्दैन। Rescue device, सहयोग र backup योजना तयार हुनुपर्छ।"],["42. Difficult airway and failed intubation readiness","Prepare suction, oxygenation devices, supraglottic airway, appropriate tubes, videolaryngoscope if available and emergency front-of-neck access pathway according to training and local algorithm. Prioritise oxygenation, call for help early, limit repeated attempts and communicate clearly. Follow the current difficult-airway guideline.","Suction, oxygenation device, supraglottic airway, tube र उपलब्ध भए videolaryngoscope तयार राख्ने। Oxygenation प्राथमिकता दिने, चाँडै सहयोग बोलाउने, बारम्बार असफल प्रयास नगर्ने र current difficult-airway guideline पालना गर्ने।"],["43. Aspiration risk and prevention","Aspiration risk assessment considers fasting status, emergency surgery, reflux, obstruction, pregnancy, obesity, delayed gastric emptying and other patient factors. Use current fasting guidance and an individualised airway plan. Suction must be available. Cricoid pressure and rapid sequence techniques are context-dependent and must follow trained-team protocols.","Aspiration risk मा fasting, emergency surgery, reflux, obstruction, pregnancy, obesity र gastric emptying जस्ता कुरा विचार गरिन्छ। Current fasting guideline र व्यक्तिगत airway योजना अपनाउने। Suction तयार राख्ने; rapid sequence technique प्रशिक्षित टोलीले protocol अनुसार गर्ने।"],["44. Anaesthesia in diabetes and endocrine disorders","Review glycaemic control, medicines, fasting, renal function and risk of hypoglycaemia or hyperglycaemia. Perioperative glucose monitoring and insulin/oral medicine plans must follow current institutional guidance. Thyroid disease can alter cardiovascular and metabolic responses; assess control and associated complications before surgery.","Diabetes मा glucose control, औषधि, fasting, kidney function र hypo/hyperglycaemia जोखिम हेर्नुपर्छ। Perioperative glucose र औषधि योजना guideline अनुसार हुन्छ। Thyroid रोगले cardiovascular तथा metabolic response बदल्न सक्छ।"],["45. Anaesthesia in cardiac and respiratory disease","Assess functional capacity, symptoms, current treatment, recent exacerbations, oxygenation and relevant investigations. Optimise reversible problems and plan monitoring, ventilation and postoperative support with the responsible team. Avoid assuming that all patients with the same diagnosis have the same anaesthetic risk.","Cardiac/respiratory रोगमा functional capacity, लक्षण, औषधि, पछिल्लो exacerbation, oxygenation र आवश्यक जाँच हेर्नुपर्छ। सुधार गर्न सकिने समस्या सुधारेर monitoring, ventilation र postoperative support योजना बनाइन्छ।"],["46. Renal and hepatic impairment","Renal impairment can alter drug clearance, fluid balance, potassium and acid-base status. Liver disease may affect metabolism, coagulation, albumin and glucose regulation. Review relevant tests and medicines; select and adjust drugs under anaesthesia-team direction. Avoid nephrotoxic or hepatotoxic exposure where possible.","Kidney रोगले drug clearance, fluid, potassium र acid-base असर गर्छ। Liver रोगले metabolism, coagulation, albumin र glucose नियन्त्रण असर गर्न सक्छ। जाँच र औषधि समीक्षा गरी अधिकृत टोलीको निर्देशनमा औषधि मिलाउनुपर्छ।"],["47. Obstetric anaesthesia and pre-eclampsia","Obstetric anaesthesia requires maternal and fetal considerations. Pre-eclampsia may involve hypertension, endothelial dysfunction, thrombocytopenia, organ dysfunction and risk of seizures. Assess severity, airway oedema, platelet/coagulation information when indicated and urgency. Management is multidisciplinary and follows obstetric anaesthesia protocols.","Obstetric anaesthesia मा आमा र भ्रूण दुवैको अवस्था विचार गर्नुपर्छ। Pre-eclampsia मा hypertension, platelet कमी, अंग समस्या र seizure जोखिम हुन सक्छ। गम्भीरता र आवश्यक जाँच हेरी multidisciplinary protocol अपनाइन्छ।"],["48. Paediatric and neonatal considerations","Children have age-related differences in airway anatomy, oxygen consumption, heat loss, circulating volume and drug handling. Use appropriate equipment sizes and weight-based calculations checked independently. Prevent hypothermia and monitor closely. Neonatal resuscitation follows current neonatal life-support algorithms and trained-provider roles.","बालबालिकामा airway, oxygen खपत, तापक्रम गुम्ने, blood volume र drug handling उमेरअनुसार फरक हुन्छ। सही size का उपकरण र तौलअनुसार double-check गरिएको dose चाहिन्छ। नवजात resuscitation current guideline अनुसार प्रशिक्षित टोलीले गर्छ।"],["49. Postoperative complications and escalation","Early postoperative problems include airway obstruction, hypoventilation, hypoxia, hypotension, hypertension, arrhythmia, pain, nausea, bleeding, hypothermia and delayed emergence. Use structured assessment, monitor trends, call for help early and communicate using a clear handover format. Never dismiss deterioration as routine recovery.","Postoperative समस्या airway obstruction, hypoventilation, hypoxia, BP/rhythm परिवर्तन, दुखाइ, वाकवाकी, bleeding, hypothermia र ढिलो होस आउनु हुन्। व्यवस्थित मूल्याङ्कन, trend monitoring र समयमै सहयोग आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["50. Infection prevention and equipment reprocessing","Use hand hygiene, standard precautions, appropriate PPE and aseptic technique. Reusable airway and anaesthesia equipment must be cleaned, disinfected or sterilised according to manufacturer instructions, device classification and infection-control policy. Single-use items must not be reused. Maintain traceability and report damaged equipment.","Hand hygiene, standard precaution, PPE र aseptic technique अपनाउने। Reusable airway/anaesthesia उपकरण manufacturer निर्देशन र infection-control policy अनुसार सफा, disinfect वा sterilise गर्ने। Single-use सामान पुनःप्रयोग नगर्ने।"]]);
 notes.push(...[["51. General anaesthesia: induction, maintenance and emergence","General anaesthesia is commonly described in phases: induction, maintenance and emergence. Induction establishes unconsciousness and appropriate conditions for airway management; maintenance sustains anaesthesia while monitoring physiology and surgical requirements; emergence involves planned return of consciousness, protective reflexes and adequate ventilation. The technique and agents are selected by the qualified anaesthesia team according to the patient and procedure.","General anaesthesia लाई induction, maintenance र emergence चरणमा बुझिन्छ। Induction मा बेहोसी र airway management का लागि उपयुक्त अवस्था बनाइन्छ; maintenance मा anaesthesia कायम राख्दै physiology निगरानी गरिन्छ; emergence मा होस, protective reflex र पर्याप्त सास फर्किएको मूल्याङ्कन गरिन्छ। औषधि र विधि बिरामी तथा शल्यक्रियाअनुसार अधिकृत anaesthesia team ले छनोट गर्छ।"],["52. Pre-anaesthetic assessment and optimisation","Pre-anaesthetic assessment reviews the presenting condition, previous anaesthesia, allergies, current medicines, fasting status, airway, cardiopulmonary function and relevant investigations. Risk is individualised and modifiable problems are addressed where possible. The plan, monitoring, postoperative destination and contingency arrangements should be discussed and documented by the responsible clinician.","Pre-anaesthetic assessment मा मुख्य रोग, पहिलेको anaesthesia अनुभव, allergy, चलिरहेका औषधि, fasting, airway, मुटु–फोक्सोको अवस्था र आवश्यक जाँच हेरिन्छ। जोखिम बिरामीअनुसार मूल्याङ्कन गरी सुधार्न मिल्ने समस्या सम्बोधन गरिन्छ। योजना, monitoring, postoperative स्थान र वैकल्पिक तयारीबारे छलफल तथा अभिलेख राखिन्छ।"],["53. Fasting and aspiration prevention","Fasting guidance depends on the patient's age, condition, urgency and the type of intake; clear fluids, breast milk, formula and solid food have different recommended intervals in current guidelines. Emergency patients or those with delayed gastric emptying need individual assessment. Do not apply a single fasting interval to every patient; follow current institutional guidance.","Fasting को समय उमेर, स्वास्थ्य, emergency अवस्था र खाएको/पिएको पदार्थअनुसार फरक हुन्छ। Clear fluid, breast milk, formula र ठोस खानाका interval एउटै हुँदैनन्। Emergency वा gastric emptying ढिलो हुने बिरामीको छुट्टै मूल्याङ्कन आवश्यक हुन्छ। सबैलाई एउटै fasting समय लागू नगरी हालको संस्थागत guideline पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],["54. Airway assessment: Mallampati and mouth opening","Airway assessment includes mouth opening, mandibular movement, dentition, neck movement, thyromental distance and features that may predict difficult ventilation or intubation. Mallampati classification is one component, not a stand-alone prediction tool. Previous airway records and the clinical context are important.","Airway assessment मा मुख खोल्ने क्षमता, जबडाको movement, दाँत, घाँटीको movement, thyromental distance र ventilation/intubation कठिन हुन सक्ने संकेत हेरिन्छ। Mallampati classification एउटा भाग मात्र हो; यसले एक्लै कठिन airway निश्चित गर्दैन। पहिलेको airway record र clinical context पनि महत्वपूर्ण हुन्छ।"],["55. Endotracheal tube size, depth and cuff pressure","Endotracheal tube size and insertion depth are selected using patient characteristics and verified clinically and with waveform capnography. Tube position can change with head movement. Cuff pressure should be checked with an appropriate manometer and kept within the locally recommended range; excessive pressure can injure tracheal mucosa, while inadequate sealing can permit leakage.","ETT को size र depth बिरामीको विशेषताअनुसार छनोट गरी clinical assessment र waveform capnography बाट पुष्टि गरिन्छ। टाउकोको position बदलिँदा tube position पनि बदलिन सक्छ। Cuff pressure manometer ले जाँचेर संस्थागत सिफारिसको सीमाभित्र राखिन्छ; धेरै pressure ले trachea मा चोट र कम pressure ले leak हुन सक्छ।"],["56. Laryngoscope and airway equipment checks","Before use, check the laryngoscope handle, blade attachment, light or video display, battery charge and availability of alternative blades. Confirm that suction, oxygen source, masks, airway adjuncts, tubes, stylet or bougie and rescue airway devices are accessible. Equipment checks should follow a standard checklist and local policy.","प्रयोगअघि laryngoscope handle, blade जोडाइ, light/video display र battery जाँचिन्छ। Suction, oxygen source, mask, airway adjunct, tube, stylet/bougie र rescue airway उपकरण उपलब्ध छन् कि छैनन् हेर्नुपर्छ। उपकरण जाँच standard checklist र स्थानीय policy अनुसार गर्नुपर्छ।"],["57. Anaesthesia breathing systems: circle system","A circle breathing system uses inspiratory and expiratory limbs, unidirectional valves, a carbon dioxide absorber and a reservoir bag or ventilator. Correct assembly, leak testing, valve function and absorber condition are essential. Rebreathing is safe only when carbon dioxide is effectively removed and the system is functioning as intended.","Circle breathing system मा inspiratory/expiratory limb, one-way valve, CO2 absorber र reservoir bag वा ventilator हुन्छ। सही assembly, leak test, valve function र absorber अवस्था जाँच्नुपर्छ। CO2 प्रभावकारी रूपमा हटेको र system ठीक काम गरेको अवस्थामा मात्र rebreathing सुरक्षित हुन्छ।"],["58. Carbon dioxide absorbents","Soda lime and other approved absorbents remove carbon dioxide from exhaled gas in circle systems. Exhaustion, channeling, drying or inappropriate handling can reduce performance or create hazards. Follow manufacturer instructions for colour indicators, replacement, storage and disposal; do not rely on colour alone.","Circle system मा soda lime जस्ता absorbent ले निस्केको gas बाट CO2 हटाउँछन्। Absorbent सकिनु, channeling हुनु, सुक्नु वा गलत handling ले काम घटाउन वा जोखिम बढाउन सक्छ। Colour indicator मात्रमा निर्भर नभई manufacturer निर्देशनअनुसार replacement, storage र disposal गर्नुपर्छ।"],["59. Ventilation modes: volume and pressure control","In volume-controlled ventilation, a set tidal volume is delivered while airway pressure varies with compliance and resistance. In pressure-controlled ventilation, inspiratory pressure is set and delivered tidal volume varies with mechanics and leaks. Mode selection and settings require clinical assessment, monitoring and adjustment by trained personnel.","Volume-controlled ventilation मा तोकिएको tidal volume दिइन्छ तर airway pressure compliance र resistance अनुसार बदलिन्छ। Pressure-controlled ventilation मा inspiratory pressure तोकिन्छ र tidal volume mechanics तथा leak अनुसार बदलिन्छ। Mode र setting तालिमप्राप्त टोलीले clinical अवस्था हेरेर मिलाउँछ।"],["60. Lung compliance and airway resistance","Compliance describes the change in lung volume for a given pressure change; reduced compliance means stiffer respiratory system. Airway resistance reflects opposition to gas flow and rises with narrowing, secretions, kinking or obstruction. Pressure waveforms and patient assessment help distinguish these problems.","Compliance भनेको pressure परिवर्तन हुँदा lung volume कति बदलिन्छ भन्ने हो; कम compliance हुँदा फोक्सो/श्वास प्रणाली कडा हुन्छ। Airway resistance ले gas flow मा हुने अवरोध जनाउँछ र airway साँघुरिँदा, secretion हुँदा वा tube kink/obstruction हुँदा बढ्छ। Pressure waveform र बिरामीको अवस्था मिलाएर कारण छुट्याइन्छ।"],["61. Oxygen delivery devices and flow principles","Oxygen delivery devices include nasal cannulae, simple masks, Venturi masks and reservoir masks. Delivered oxygen concentration varies with device design, flow, fit and the patient's breathing pattern. Oxygen is a prescribed therapy; monitor the response and use the target saturation range appropriate to the clinical condition and local protocol.","Oxygen delivery device मा nasal cannula, simple mask, Venturi mask र reservoir mask पर्छन्। दिइने oxygen concentration device, flow, mask fit र बिरामीको सासअनुसार फरक हुन्छ। Oxygen prescribed therapy हो; बिरामीको अवस्था र स्थानीय protocol अनुसार target saturation राखेर response निगरानी गर्नुपर्छ।"],["62. Capnography: phases and waveform","A normal capnogram has an inspiratory baseline, expiratory upstroke, alveolar plateau and inspiratory downstroke. End-tidal CO2 is measured near the end of expiration and usually approximates, but is not identical to, arterial CO2. Changes in waveform shape or value can reflect ventilation, circulation, metabolism or equipment problems.","सामान्य capnogram मा inspiratory baseline, expiratory upstroke, alveolar plateau र inspiratory downstroke हुन्छ। End-tidal CO2 expiration को अन्त्यतिर मापन हुन्छ र सामान्यतया arterial CO2 को नजिक हुन्छ तर ठ्याक्कै उस्तै हुँदैन। Waveform वा value परिवर्तनले ventilation, circulation, metabolism वा equipment समस्या देखाउन सक्छ।"],["63. Arterial blood gas: acid-base interpretation","ABG interpretation begins with pH, then PaCO2 and bicarbonate to identify respiratory or metabolic disturbance. Oxygenation is assessed using PaO2 in the context of inspired oxygen and clinical status. Compensation and mixed disorders require systematic interpretation; correlate results with the patient and sampling conditions.","ABG बुझ्दा पहिले pH, त्यसपछि PaCO2 र bicarbonate हेरेर respiratory वा metabolic समस्या छुट्याइन्छ। Oxygenation लाई दिइएको oxygen concentration र clinical अवस्थासँग मिलाएर PaO2 बाट मूल्याङ्कन गरिन्छ। Compensation वा mixed disorder व्यवस्थित रूपमा विश्लेषण गरी बिरामी र sample लिने अवस्थासँग मिलाउनुपर्छ।"],["64. Perioperative fluid balance and urine output","Fluid assessment considers oral and intravenous intake, blood loss, urine output, drains, insensible losses and the patient's cardiac and renal function. Both fluid deficit and overload can be harmful. Record input and output accurately and escalate unexpected changes; fluid prescriptions are individualised by the responsible clinician.","Fluid assessment मा मुखबाट/IV बाट गएको fluid, रगत बगेको मात्रा, urine output, drain, insensible loss तथा मुटु र मिर्गौलाको अवस्था हेरिन्छ। Fluid कम वा धेरै दुवै हानिकारक हुन सक्छ। Input-output सही लेख्ने र असामान्य परिवर्तन तुरुन्त जानकारी गराउने; fluid prescription जिम्मेवार clinician ले बिरामीअनुसार गर्छ।"],["65. Blood components and transfusion observation","Red cells, platelets, plasma and cryoprecipitate have different indications and risks. Verify patient identity, component details, compatibility documentation and consent according to policy. Observe for fever, chills, rash, dyspnoea, pain or haemodynamic change; suspected reaction requires immediate escalation and management under the transfusion protocol.","Red cells, platelets, plasma र cryoprecipitate का प्रयोग र जोखिम फरक हुन्छन्। Policy अनुसार बिरामीको पहिचान, component विवरण, compatibility र consent पुष्टि गर्नुपर्छ। ज्वरो, काम्ने, rash, सास गाह्रो, दुखाइ वा haemodynamic परिवर्तन हेर्नुपर्छ; reaction शंका भए तुरुन्त जानकारी दिई transfusion protocol पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],["66. Temperature management and warming","Anaesthesia impairs normal thermoregulation and can increase heat loss. Monitor temperature when indicated, minimise unnecessary exposure and use approved warming methods and warmed fluids when appropriate. Hypothermia may contribute to shivering, delayed drug metabolism, coagulopathy and slower recovery.","Anaesthesia ले सामान्य thermoregulation कमजोर पारेर शरीरको ताप गुम्ने जोखिम बढाउँछ। आवश्यकताअनुसार temperature निगरानी गर्ने, अनावश्यक exposure घटाउने र उपयुक्त warming device तथा warmed fluid प्रयोग गर्ने। Hypothermia ले shivering, औषधि metabolism ढिलो, coagulation समस्या र recovery ढिलो गराउन सक्छ।"],["67. Postoperative respiratory complications","Postoperative respiratory problems include airway obstruction, hypoventilation, hypoxaemia, atelectasis, bronchospasm and aspiration. Risk is influenced by residual anaesthetic or neuromuscular effects, pain, obesity, sleep-disordered breathing and underlying lung disease. Early recognition, monitoring and escalation are essential.","Postoperative respiratory समस्या airway obstruction, hypoventilation, hypoxaemia, atelectasis, bronchospasm र aspiration हुन सक्छन्। बाँकी anaesthetic/muscle relaxant असर, दुखाइ, obesity, sleep-disordered breathing र फोक्सोको रोगले जोखिम बढाउँछन्। छिटो पहिचान, monitoring र escalation आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["68. Postoperative nausea, vomiting and aspiration risk","PONV risk depends on patient factors, procedure and anaesthetic technique. Prevention may use risk reduction and prescribed antiemetics. Persistent vomiting can cause dehydration, electrolyte disturbance and aspiration, especially when airway reflexes are impaired. Document symptoms and response to treatment.","PONV को जोखिम बिरामी, शल्यक्रिया र anaesthesia विधिमा निर्भर हुन्छ। जोखिम घटाउने उपाय र prescribed antiemetic प्रयोग हुन सक्छ। लगातार बान्ताले dehydration, electrolyte समस्या र airway reflex कमजोर हुँदा aspiration गराउन सक्छ। लक्षण र उपचारको response अभिलेख राख्नुपर्छ।"],["69. Recovery scoring and handover","Recovery assessment commonly considers consciousness, airway patency, breathing, circulation, activity, oxygenation, pain, nausea and temperature according to local criteria. A structured handover communicates procedure, anaesthetic course, airway, medicines, fluids, blood loss, concerns and pending tasks. A score supports but does not replace clinical judgement.","Recovery assessment मा स्थानीय criteria अनुसार होस, airway, सास, circulation, activity, oxygenation, दुखाइ, वाकवाकी र तापक्रम हेरिन्छ। Structured handover मा procedure, anaesthesia course, airway, औषधि, fluid, blood loss, समस्या र बाँकी काम जानकारी दिइन्छ। Score ले clinical judgement लाई प्रतिस्थापन गर्दैन।"],["70. Anaesthesia equipment maintenance and incident reporting","Equipment must be checked before use, maintained according to manufacturer schedules and removed from service when faulty. Record faults, label unsafe devices and notify the appropriate technical or clinical lead. Near misses and incidents should be reported through the institutional system to support learning and prevent recurrence.","उपकरण प्रयोगअघि जाँच्ने र manufacturer schedule अनुसार maintenance गर्ने। खराब उपकरण प्रयोगबाट हटाई चिन्ह लगाएर सम्बन्धित technical/clinical जिम्मेवार व्यक्तिलाई जानकारी दिने। Near miss र incident संस्थाको reporting system मा लेख्दा सिकाइ र पुनः घटना रोक्न मद्दत हुन्छ।"]]);
 notes.push(...[["71. Premedication: aims and safety","Premedication may reduce anxiety, provide analgesia, reduce secretions or aspiration risk, and support a planned anaesthetic technique. Drug choice depends on age, comorbidities, airway and respiratory risk, current medicines and procedure. Sedatives can depress ventilation and impair protective reflexes; monitoring and an appropriate plan are essential. Premedication is prescribed by the responsible clinician, not given routinely to every patient.","Premedication ले anxiety घटाउन, दुखाइ नियन्त्रण, secretion वा aspiration risk घटाउन र anaesthesia plan मा सहयोग गर्न सक्छ। औषधि छनोट गर्दा उमेर, सह-रोग, airway, सासको जोखिम, चलिरहेका औषधि र procedure हेर्नुपर्छ। Sedative ले ventilation र protective reflex घटाउन सक्छ; त्यसैले monitoring र योजना आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["72. Minimum alveolar concentration (MAC)","MAC is the alveolar concentration of an inhaled anaesthetic that prevents movement in response to a surgical stimulus in 50% of subjects under defined conditions. It is a measure of potency: lower MAC generally indicates greater potency. MAC varies with age, temperature, pregnancy and other physiological or drug factors; it is not a direct measure of an individual patient's awareness.","MAC भनेको निश्चित अवस्थामा surgical stimulus हुँदा ५०% व्यक्तिमा movement रोक्ने inhaled anaesthetic को alveolar concentration हो। कम MAC हुनु सामान्यतया बढी potency को संकेत हो। उमेर, तापक्रम, गर्भावस्था र औषधिले MAC बदल्न सक्छ; यो एक्लै बिरामीको awareness मापन होइन।"],["73. Volatile anaesthetic agents","Halothane, isoflurane and sevoflurane are volatile inhalational agents with different pharmacological properties and safety profiles. Uptake and washout are influenced by blood-gas solubility, ventilation, cardiac output and concentration. Agent selection and delivery require a calibrated vaporizer, gas monitoring and appropriate clinical supervision; nitrous oxide is an inhaled adjunct, not a complete sole anaesthetic for most major procedures.","Halothane, isoflurane र sevoflurane का pharmacological गुण र safety profile फरक हुन्छन्। शरीरमा जाने र बाहिरिने गति blood-gas solubility, ventilation, cardiac output र concentration बाट प्रभावित हुन्छ। सही calibrated vaporizer, gas monitoring र clinical supervision आवश्यक हुन्छ; nitrous oxide प्रायः adjunct का रूपमा प्रयोग हुन्छ।"],["74. Intravenous induction agents","Thiopentone, propofol and ketamine are intravenous anaesthetic agents with distinct effects. Propofol commonly causes dose-related cardiovascular and respiratory depression; ketamine often preserves sympathetic tone and may provide analgesia; thiopentone is a barbiturate induction agent. Selection depends on patient condition, contraindications, availability and clinician judgement. Airway and resuscitation equipment must be ready.","Thiopentone, propofol र ketamine फरक प्रभाव भएका IV anaesthetic हुन्। Propofol ले dose अनुसार BP र respiration घटाउन सक्छ; ketamine ले धेरै अवस्थामा sympathetic tone जोगाउन र analgesia दिन सक्छ; thiopentone barbiturate हो। छनोट बिरामीको अवस्था, contraindication र clinician को निर्णयमा निर्भर हुन्छ। Airway तथा resuscitation उपकरण तयार हुनुपर्छ।"],["75. Opioids used in anaesthesia","Morphine, pethidine, fentanyl, buprenorphine and tramadol are opioids with differing potency, duration and pharmacology. Important class risks include respiratory depression, sedation, nausea, constipation and dependence. Combine careful assessment with prescribed dosing, monitoring and reassessment. Opioid effects may be potentiated by other sedatives.","Morphine, pethidine, fentanyl, buprenorphine र tramadol फरक potency र duration भएका opioid हुन्। मुख्य जोखिममा respiratory depression, sedation, nausea, constipation र dependence पर्छन्। Prescription अनुसार मात्रा, monitoring र पुनः मूल्याङ्कन आवश्यक हुन्छ। अन्य sedative सँग जोखिम बढ्न सक्छ।"],["76. Neuromuscular blocking agents","Suxamethonium is a depolarising neuromuscular blocker; pancuronium, vecuronium, atracurium and rocuronium are non-depolarising agents. These drugs cause paralysis but do not provide unconsciousness or analgesia. Adequate anaesthesia, ventilation, quantitative or appropriate neuromuscular monitoring and a planned reversal strategy are essential.","Suxamethonium depolarising neuromuscular blocker हो; pancuronium, vecuronium, atracurium र rocuronium non-depolarising हुन्। यी औषधिले paralysis गराउँछन् तर बेहोसी वा दुखाइ नियन्त्रण गर्दैनन्। पर्याप्त anaesthesia, ventilation, neuromuscular monitoring र reversal योजना अनिवार्य हुन्छ।"],["77. Reversal of neuromuscular blockade","Neostigmine with an appropriate antimuscarinic may reverse suitable non-depolarising blockade; sugammadex reverses rocuronium or vecuronium where available and indicated. Choice depends on the agent, depth of block, monitoring and patient factors. Do not rely only on elapsed time or clinical impression; confirm adequate recovery using an appropriate neuromuscular assessment.","उपयुक्त non-depolarising blockade मा neostigmine सँग antimuscarinic प्रयोग हुन सक्छ; उपलब्ध र उपयुक्त अवस्थामा sugammadex ले rocuronium वा vecuronium reverse गर्छ। औषधि, blockade को गहिराइ, monitoring र बिरामीको अवस्थाअनुसार छनोट हुन्छ। समय बितेको वा बाहिरी अनुमान मात्रमा भर नपरी recovery पुष्टि गर्नुपर्छ।"],["78. Neuromuscular transmission and nerve stimulators","Neuromuscular transmission involves acetylcholine release at the motor nerve terminal, binding at nicotinic receptors and muscle depolarisation. Peripheral nerve stimulators deliver controlled stimuli and help assess blockade. Train-of-four response and other patterns are interpreted with the clinical context; quantitative monitoring is preferred where available to reduce residual paralysis.","Neuromuscular transmission मा motor nerve बाट acetylcholine निस्केर nicotinic receptor मा बाँधिन्छ र muscle depolarisation हुन्छ। Peripheral nerve stimulator ले नियन्त्रित stimulus दिएर blockade मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ। Train-of-four response clinical अवस्थासँग मिलाएर बुझिन्छ; उपलब्ध भए quantitative monitoring ले बाँकी paralysis जोखिम घटाउन मद्दत गर्छ।"],["79. Local anaesthetic agents and toxicity awareness","Local anaesthetics block voltage-gated sodium channels and temporarily interrupt nerve conduction. Common agents include lidocaine, bupivacaine and ropivacaine; onset, duration and toxicity differ. Accidental intravascular injection or excessive systemic exposure can cause neurological and cardiovascular toxicity. Use the prescribed dose, appropriate technique, monitoring and the institution's local anaesthetic systemic toxicity protocol.","Local anaesthetic ले voltage-gated sodium channel रोक्दै nerve conduction अस्थायी रूपमा बन्द गर्छ। Lidocaine, bupivacaine र ropivacaine का onset, duration र toxicity फरक हुन्छन्। रगतको नलीमा गल्तीले जानु वा बढी systemic exposure हुँदा neurological र cardiovascular toxicity हुन सक्छ। Prescribed dose, सही technique, monitoring र संस्थाको toxicity protocol पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],["80. Emergency medicines: role and safe handling","The syllabus names atropine, epinephrine, isoprenaline, ephedrine, aminophylline, hydrocortisone, sodium bicarbonate, dopamine, norepinephrine and dobutamine. These medicines have different indications, mechanisms and risks. Learn their classes, clinical roles, concentration labels, storage and checking requirements. Administration, dose and preparation must follow current protocol and authorised prescriber direction; never rely on memory alone in an emergency.","Syllabus मा atropine, epinephrine, isoprenaline, ephedrine, aminophylline, hydrocortisone, sodium bicarbonate, dopamine, norepinephrine र dobutamine उल्लेख छन्। यी औषधिको काम, mechanism र जोखिम फरक हुन्छ। Class, प्रयोग, concentration label, storage र checking सिक्नुपर्छ। Dose र preparation सधैँ हालको protocol तथा अधिकृत prescriber को निर्देशनअनुसार गर्नुपर्छ।"],["81. Intravenous cannulation and venepuncture","Select an appropriate vein and cannula based on therapy, patient anatomy and urgency. Use hand hygiene, skin antisepsis, aseptic non-touch technique, suitable vein stabilisation and safe sharps disposal. Confirm patency and inspect for pain, swelling, leakage or inflammation. Difficult access should be escalated early and repeated attempts minimised according to policy.","IV cannulation गर्दा उपचार, बिरामीको anatomy र urgency अनुसार vein तथा cannula छनोट गरिन्छ। Hand hygiene, skin antisepsis, aseptic non-touch technique र सुरक्षित sharps disposal आवश्यक हुन्छ। Patency पुष्टि गरी दुखाइ, सुन्निने, leak वा inflammation हेर्नुपर्छ। कठिन access भए चाँडै सहयोग माग्ने र बारम्बार प्रयास घटाउने।"],["82. Patient protection and positioning injuries","Protect eyes from pressure and chemical exposure, support limbs in neutral alignment and pad pressure points. Avoid excessive stretch or compression of peripheral nerves and vessels. Secure monitoring cables and devices without constriction; check skin and contact points during prolonged procedures. Document positioning and any pre-existing injury.","आँखालाई pressure र chemical exposure बाट जोगाउने, हातखुट्टा neutral position मा राख्ने र pressure point मा padding गर्ने। Peripheral nerve तथा blood vessel मा अत्यधिक तन्काइ वा दबाब नपरोस्। Monitoring cable र device ले कसिलो नबनाओस्; लामो procedure मा छाला र contact point जाँच्ने।"],["83. Extubation and transfer readiness","Extubation is planned after assessing consciousness, airway protection, ventilation, oxygenation, neuromuscular recovery, haemodynamic stability and procedure-specific risks. Suctioning, cuff management and airway support are performed by trained personnel according to the plan. A difficult-airway or high-risk patient may need a staged strategy and appropriate postoperative destination.","Extubation अघि होस, airway protection, ventilation, oxygenation, neuromuscular recovery, haemodynamic stability र procedure-specific जोखिम मूल्याङ्कन गरिन्छ। Suction, cuff management र airway support तालिमप्राप्त व्यक्तिले योजनाअनुसार गर्छन्। कठिन airway वा high-risk बिरामीलाई staged strategy र उपयुक्त postoperative स्थान चाहिन सक्छ।"],["84. Recovery-room cardiovascular and neurological problems","Recovery may be complicated by hypotension, hypertension, tachycardia, bradycardia, pallor, sweating, restlessness or seizures. Assess airway, breathing, circulation, consciousness, pain, temperature, bleeding, fluid status and medication effects. Escalate promptly, document trends and follow local emergency pathways rather than assuming a single cause.","Recovery मा hypotension, hypertension, tachycardia, bradycardia, pallor, पसिना, restlessness वा seizure हुन सक्छ। Airway, breathing, circulation, होस, दुखाइ, तापक्रम, bleeding, fluid र औषधिको असर मूल्याङ्कन गर्नुपर्छ। एउटै कारण ठानेर नबस्ने; तुरुन्त escalation, trend अभिलेख र स्थानीय emergency pathway पालना गर्ने।"],["85. Pulmonary function tests and perioperative relevance","Spirometry commonly reports FEV1, FVC and the FEV1/FVC ratio. Obstructive patterns reduce expiratory flow and often lower the ratio; restrictive patterns reduce lung volumes, with confirmation requiring appropriate lung-volume assessment. Test quality, symptoms and clinical context matter; pulmonary function tests are not interpreted in isolation.","Spirometry मा FEV1, FVC र FEV1/FVC ratio मापन हुन्छ। Obstructive pattern मा expiratory flow घट्छ र ratio प्रायः कम हुन्छ; restrictive pattern मा lung volume घट्छ र पुष्टि गर्न उपयुक्त lung-volume assessment चाहिन्छ। Test quality, लक्षण र clinical context महत्वपूर्ण हुन्छन्।"],["86. Ventilator humidification and aerosol therapy","Humidification adds moisture to inspired gas and helps protect airway mucosa when normal upper-airway conditioning is bypassed. Heated humidifiers and heat-moisture exchangers have different indications and limitations. Aerosol therapy delivers medication as particles to the respiratory tract; device selection and circuit placement affect delivery. Follow infection-control and manufacturer instructions.","Humidification ले inspired gas मा moisture थपेर माथिल्लो airway को सामान्य काम bypass हुँदा mucosa जोगाउँछ। Heated humidifier र heat-moisture exchanger का प्रयोग तथा सीमा फरक हुन्छन्। Aerosol therapy ले औषधि साना कणका रूपमा श्वासमार्गमा पुर्‍याउँछ; device र circuit placement ले delivery असर गर्छ।"],["87. Newborn resuscitation principles","Newborn resuscitation differs from adult resuscitation and prioritises effective ventilation when a newborn does not establish breathing. Preparation includes warmth, airway positioning, appropriate-sized equipment and a trained team. Assessment and interventions follow the current neonatal resuscitation guideline; adult algorithms and drug doses must not be substituted.","नवजात शिशुको resuscitation वयस्कभन्दा फरक हुन्छ र सास सुरु नभए प्रभावकारी ventilation प्राथमिक हुन्छ। तयारीमा न्यानो राख्ने, airway position मिलाउने, सही size का उपकरण र तालिमप्राप्त टोली चाहिन्छ। हालको neonatal resuscitation guideline पालना गर्नुपर्छ; adult algorithm वा dose प्रयोग गर्नु हुँदैन।"],["88. Anaesthesia for thoracic surgery","Thoracic surgery may require lung isolation and one-lung ventilation to provide surgical access. Double-lumen tubes or bronchial blockers are selected and positioned by trained clinicians, with confirmation using appropriate methods including bronchoscopy when indicated. Oxygenation, ventilation, airway pressures and haemodynamics require close monitoring.","Thoracic surgery मा surgical access का लागि lung isolation र one-lung ventilation आवश्यक हुन सक्छ। Double-lumen tube वा bronchial blocker तालिमप्राप्त clinician ले छनोट र position गर्छन्; आवश्यकताअनुसार bronchoscopy बाट पुष्टि गरिन्छ। Oxygenation, ventilation, airway pressure र haemodynamics नजिकबाट निगरानी गर्नुपर्छ।"],["89. Anaesthesia for cardiac surgery and cardiopulmonary bypass","Cardiac surgery requires coordinated anaesthesia, perfusion and surgical teams. Cardiopulmonary bypass temporarily supports circulation and gas exchange using a pump-oxygenator; anticoagulation, temperature, blood gases, electrolytes and organ perfusion are closely managed. The anaesthesia technologist must understand equipment checks, monitoring interfaces and communication within the specialist team.","Cardiac surgery मा anaesthesia, perfusion र surgical team बीच समन्वय आवश्यक हुन्छ। Cardiopulmonary bypass मा pump-oxygenator ले अस्थायी रूपमा circulation र gas exchange सहयोग गर्छ। Anticoagulation, तापक्रम, blood gas, electrolyte र organ perfusion निगरानी गरिन्छ। उपकरण जाँच र specialist team सँग communication बुझ्नुपर्छ।"],["90. Shock, low cardiac output and cardiac arrest","Shock is inadequate tissue perfusion and may be hypovolaemic, distributive, cardiogenic or obstructive. Low cardiac output can result from reduced preload, impaired contractility, abnormal afterload or rhythm disturbance. Recognition uses clinical signs, trends and appropriate monitoring. Cardiac arrest requires immediate activation of the emergency response and current resuscitation algorithms by trained responders.","Shock भनेको tissue मा पर्याप्त रक्तप्रवाह नपुग्नु हो; hypovolaemic, distributive, cardiogenic वा obstructive हुन सक्छ। Low cardiac output preload कम, contractility कमजोर, afterload वा rhythm समस्या हुँदा हुन सक्छ। Clinical संकेत र monitoring बाट पहिचान गरिन्छ। Cardiac arrest मा तुरुन्त emergency response बोलाई तालिमप्राप्त टोलीले हालको resuscitation algorithm पालना गर्छ।"]]);
 const anaesthesiaBatch1=[["Which device confirms tracheal tube placement most reliably during ongoing anaesthesia?","Anaesthesia चलिरहेको बेला tracheal tube सही ठाउँमा छ भन्ने सबैभन्दा भरपर्दो निरन्तर संकेत कुन हो?",["Sustained waveform capnography","Chest movement alone","Auscultation once","Tube misting"],"Sustained waveform capnography is the key confirmation method, interpreted with clinical assessment.","निरन्तर waveform capnography मुख्य पुष्टि विधि हो; clinical assessment पनि आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["Pulse oximetry primarily measures:","Pulse oximeter ले मुख्यतः के मापन गर्छ?",["Peripheral oxygen saturation","Carbon dioxide level","Tidal volume","Blood pressure"],"It estimates peripheral oxygen saturation, not ventilation.","यसले oxygen saturation अनुमान गर्छ, ventilation होइन।"],["Capnography measures:","Capnography ले के मापन गर्छ?",["Exhaled carbon dioxide","Arterial oxygen pressure directly","Haemoglobin","Core temperature"],"Capnography displays exhaled CO2 over time.","यसले समयअनुसार निस्केको CO2 देखाउँछ।"],["A sudden loss of capnography waveform may indicate:","Capnography waveform अचानक हराउँदा के संकेत हुन सक्छ?",["Circuit disconnection","Normal ventilation always","Improved perfusion","Fever"],"Disconnection, tube displacement, obstruction or circulatory collapse must be considered.","Disconnection, tube displacement, obstruction वा circulation collapse विचार गर्नुपर्छ।"],["The purpose of a scavenging system is to:","Scavenging system को उद्देश्य के हो?",["Remove waste anaesthetic gases","Deliver oxygen to patient","Measure BP","Warm IV fluid"],"It removes waste anaesthetic gases from the working environment.","यसले काम गर्ने वातावरणबाट waste anaesthetic gas हटाउँछ।"],["A vaporizer should be:","Vaporizer कस्तो हुनुपर्छ?",["Correct agent, filled and securely seated","Filled with any volatile agent","Used despite leakage","Disconnected from machine"],"Agent-specific filling and correct seating prevent delivery errors and leaks.","सही agent र सुरक्षित जडानले औषधि गल्ती तथा leak रोक्छ।"],["Which gas supports combustion?","कुन gas ले आगो बल्न सहयोग गर्छ?",["Oxygen","Nitrogen","Carbon dioxide","Helium"],"Oxygen supports combustion; keep oils and flames away.","Oxygen ले आगो बल्न सहयोग गर्छ; तेल र आगो टाढा राख्नुपर्छ।"],["A low-pressure oxygen alarm should prompt:","Low-pressure oxygen alarm आएमा के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Immediate assessment of supply and patient safety","Ignore if SpO2 is normal","Disable alarm","Increase volatile agent"],"Check the supply, backup source and patient while following the emergency checklist.","Supply, backup र बिरामी जाँचेर emergency checklist पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],["In a circle breathing system, soda lime is used to:","Circle breathing system मा soda lime किन प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Absorb carbon dioxide","Absorb oxygen","Generate nitrous oxide","Measure humidity"],"CO2 absorbent permits rebreathing of appropriately conditioned gases.","CO2 absorbent ले उपयुक्त gas पुनःश्वास लिन सम्भव बनाउँछ।"],["A capnogram plateau mainly represents:","Capnogram को plateau ले मुख्यतः के जनाउँछ?",["Alveolar gas phase","Inspiratory baseline","Oxygen cylinder pressure","ECG rhythm"],"The alveolar plateau reflects exhaled alveolar gas.","Alveolar plateau ले निस्कँदै गरेको alveolar gas जनाउँछ।"],["Poor peripheral perfusion can affect:","कम peripheral perfusion ले कुन monitor असर गर्न सक्छ?",["Pulse oximeter accuracy","Vaporizer concentration directly","ECG paper speed","Cylinder colour"],"Low perfusion can weaken the pulse oximeter signal and reduce reliability.","कम perfusion ले pulse oximeter signal कमजोर बनाउँछ।"],["An arterial line provides:","Arterial line ले के सुविधा दिन्छ?",["Continuous invasive blood pressure","Non-invasive oxygen saturation only","Anaesthetic gas concentration","Urine output"],"It provides continuous beat-to-beat arterial pressure monitoring.","यसले निरन्तर beat-to-beat arterial BP दिन्छ।"],["The transducer for invasive pressure monitoring should be:","Invasive pressure monitoring को transducer के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Zeroed and levelled correctly","Placed below the floor","Left uncalibrated","Disconnected during reading"],"Correct zeroing and leveling are essential for accurate readings.","सही zeroing र leveling ले सही reading दिन्छ।"],["Which monitor assesses cardiac electrical activity?","मुटुको electrical activity कुन monitor ले हेर्छ?",["ECG","Pulse oximeter","Capnograph","Temperature probe"],"ECG displays cardiac electrical activity and rhythm.","ECG ले मुटुको electrical activity र rhythm देखाउँछ।"],["A common cause of ECG artefact is:","ECG artefact को सामान्य कारण कुन हो?",["Poor electrode contact","Correct skin preparation","Stable patient","Proper cable connection"],"Poor contact and movement can create artefacts.","Electrode सम्पर्क कमजोर र movement ले artefact बनाउँछ।"],["Anaesthesia increases risk of hypothermia partly because it:","Anaesthesia ले hypothermia जोखिम किन बढाउँछ?",["Impairs thermoregulation","Increases shivering control","Stops heat loss","Always raises metabolism"],"Anaesthesia impairs normal temperature regulation and promotes heat loss.","Anaesthesia ले तापक्रम नियन्त्रण कमजोर पारेर heat loss बढाउँछ।"],["An appropriately sized BP cuff is important because:","सही size को BP cuff किन आवश्यक छ?",["Wrong size can distort BP reading","It measures oxygen","It prevents arrhythmia","It sterilises skin"],"Cuff size affects accuracy of non-invasive BP measurement.","Cuff size ले NIBP reading को accuracy असर गर्छ।"],["Which is a key component of a preoperative check?","Preoperative check को मुख्य भाग कुन हो?",["Identity, procedure and consent","Only patient's height","Only room temperature","Only instrument colour"],"Correct identity, planned procedure and informed consent are essential.","पहिचान, planned procedure र informed consent आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["A difficult-airway plan should include:","Difficult-airway plan मा के समावेश हुनुपर्छ?",["Backup oxygenation and rescue strategy","Only repeated direct laryngoscopy","No suction","No help call"],"Rescue devices, oxygenation plan and early help are essential.","Rescue device, oxygenation योजना र समयमै सहयोग आवश्यक हुन्छ।"],["Repeated failed intubation attempts increase risk of:","बारम्बार असफल intubation प्रयासले कुन जोखिम बढाउँछ?",["Airway trauma and hypoxia","Improved oxygenation","Reduced swelling","Better mask seal"],"Repeated attempts can cause trauma, bleeding and worsening oxygenation.","धेरै प्रयासले चोट, bleeding र oxygen कमी बढाउन सक्छ।"],["Aspiration risk is increased by:","Aspiration जोखिम कुन अवस्थामा बढ्न सक्छ?",["Delayed gastric emptying","Empty stomach always","Normal airway reflexes","No reflux"],"Delayed gastric emptying and reflux increase aspiration risk.","ढिलो gastric emptying र reflux ले aspiration जोखिम बढाउँछ।"],["Which device provides a supraglottic airway?","Supraglottic airway device कुन हो?",["Laryngeal mask airway","Peripheral IV cannula","Arterial catheter","Nasogastric feeding bag"],"A laryngeal mask airway sits above the glottis.","Laryngeal mask airway glottis माथि बस्छ।"],["The cuff of an endotracheal tube helps to:","Endotracheal tube को cuff ले के गर्छ?",["Provide a seal in the trachea","Measure blood glucose","Prevent all aspiration absolutely","Deliver IV drugs"],"The cuff helps create a seal for ventilation; it does not eliminate aspiration risk.","Cuff ले ventilation का लागि seal बनाउँछ तर aspiration पूर्ण रोक्दैन।"],["After patient repositioning, the ETT should be:","बिरामीको position बदलेपछि ETT के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Reassessed for position and security","Assumed unchanged","Removed routinely","Cut shorter"],"Movement can displace the tube, so reassess and confirm.","Movement ले tube सार्न सक्छ, त्यसैले पुनः जाँच्नुपर्छ।"],["Which is a major purpose of preoxygenation?","Preoxygenation को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["Increase oxygen reserve before apnoea","Reduce blood glucose","Cause muscle relaxation","Prevent all aspiration"],"Preoxygenation increases oxygen reserve during induction and apnoea.","Preoxygenation ले induction र apnoea समयमा oxygen reserve बढाउँछ।"],["Which item is essential for airway suction?","Airway suction का लागि के आवश्यक छ?",["Working suction source and catheter","Only thermometer","ECG paper","Vaporizer key"],"A functioning suction system and suitable catheter should be ready.","चल्ने suction र उपयुक्त catheter तयार हुनुपर्छ।"],["The main aim of patient positioning is to:","Patient positioning को मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?",["Provide access while protecting patient","Only improve surgical view","Compress all nerves","Obstruct ventilation"],"Positioning must balance surgical access with airway, circulation and nerve safety.","Surgical access सँगै airway, circulation र nerve सुरक्षा कायम गर्नुपर्छ।"],["Which area is especially vulnerable to pressure injury in supine patients?","Supine बिरामीमा pressure injury को जोखिम हुने स्थान कुन हो?",["Occiput and sacrum","Palm only","Forehead only","Fingertips only"],"Bony prominences such as occiput, sacrum and heels need protection.","Occiput, sacrum र heel जस्ता हड्डी निस्केका भाग जोगाउनुपर्छ।"],["A key step in IV cannulation is:","IV cannulation को मुख्य चरण कुन हो?",["Aseptic skin preparation","Touching cleaned site repeatedly","Using a damaged cannula","Leaving it unsecured"],"Aseptic preparation and secure fixation reduce infection and dislodgement.","Aseptic तयारी र fixation ले infection तथा cannula निस्कने जोखिम घटाउँछ।"],["Which fluid is a crystalloid?","कुन fluid crystalloid हो?",["0.9% sodium chloride","Albumin 5%","Packed red cells","Fresh frozen plasma"],"Normal saline is an isotonic crystalloid solution.","Normal saline isotonic crystalloid हो।"],["Packed red blood cells are primarily given to:","Packed red blood cell मुख्यतः किन दिइन्छ?",["Improve oxygen-carrying capacity","Replace platelets","Reverse heparin","Treat dehydration alone"],"Red cells improve oxygen-carrying capacity in appropriate indications.","उपयुक्त अवस्थामा RBC ले oxygen बोक्ने क्षमता बढाउँछ।"],["If a transfusion reaction is suspected, the first action is to:","Transfusion reaction शंका भए पहिलो काम के हो?",["Stop the transfusion","Increase the transfusion rate","Discard the blood bag immediately","Ignore symptoms"],"Stop transfusion and initiate the institutional reaction protocol.","Transfusion रोक्ने र संस्थागत reaction protocol सुरु गर्ने।"],["Which parameter is essential in fluid balance monitoring?","Fluid balance मा कुन parameter आवश्यक छ?",["Input and output","Hair growth","Visual acuity","Skin colour alone"],"Fluid input/output and clinical status help assess balance.","Fluid input/output र clinical अवस्था मूल्याङ्कन गर्न मद्दत गर्छ।"],["Hypothermia may contribute to:","Hypothermia ले के समस्या बढाउन सक्छ?",["Coagulopathy","Improved coagulation","Hyperglycaemia only","Bronchodilation"],"Low temperature can impair coagulation and prolong recovery.","कम तापक्रमले coagulation बिगार्न र recovery ढिलो गराउन सक्छ।"],["Which condition requires careful perioperative glucose monitoring?","कुन अवस्थामा perioperative glucose निगरानी आवश्यक हुन्छ?",["Diabetes mellitus","Myopia","Otitis externa","Simple dental plaque"],"Diabetes and fasting/medications can cause perioperative glucose changes.","Diabetes, fasting र औषधिले perioperative glucose बदल्न सक्छ।"],["Renal impairment can alter:","Renal impairment ले के बदल्न सक्छ?",["Drug clearance and electrolyte balance","Eye colour","Blood group","Bone length"],"Renal dysfunction affects drug elimination, fluid and electrolytes.","Kidney dysfunction ले औषधि निष्कासन, fluid र electrolyte असर गर्छ।"],["Liver disease may affect:","Liver रोगले के असर गर्न सक्छ?",["Drug metabolism and coagulation","Only hearing","Only vision","Nail growth"],"The liver is important for drug metabolism and clotting-factor synthesis.","कलेजो drug metabolism र clotting factor synthesis मा महत्त्वपूर्ण छ।"],["Pre-eclampsia is associated with:","Pre-eclampsia कुन अवस्थासँग सम्बन्धित छ?",["Hypertension in pregnancy","Low blood pressure only","Hypoglycaemia only","Isolated fever"],"Pre-eclampsia is a hypertensive disorder of pregnancy with potential organ involvement.","Pre-eclampsia गर्भावस्थाको hypertension सम्बन्धी रोग हो र अंगमा असर पर्न सक्छ।"],["Paediatric patients have higher oxygen consumption relative to body weight than adults, making them more vulnerable to:","बालबालिकामा तौलअनुसार oxygen खपत बढी हुँदा कुन जोखिम हुन्छ?",["Rapid desaturation","Slow desaturation always","No airway obstruction","No heat loss"],"Children can desaturate rapidly during apnoea.","Apnoea हुँदा बालबालिकाको oxygen saturation छिटो घट्न सक्छ।"],["A key neonatal resuscitation principle is to follow:","नवजात resuscitation मा कुन कुरा पालना गर्नुपर्छ?",["Current neonatal life-support algorithm","Adult-only algorithm","Unverified internet advice","Improvised drug doses"],"Use current neonatal guidance and trained team roles.","हालको neonatal guideline र प्रशिक्षित टोलीको भूमिका पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],["Spinal anaesthesia is administered into the:","Spinal anaesthesia कहाँ दिइन्छ?",["Subarachnoid space containing CSF","Epidural space","Muscle","Vein"],"Spinal local anaesthetic is injected into CSF in the subarachnoid space.","Spinal औषधि CSF भएको subarachnoid space मा दिइन्छ।"],["Epidural anaesthesia is administered into the:","Epidural anaesthesia कहाँ दिइन्छ?",["Epidural space","Subarachnoid CSF","Artery","Pleural cavity"],"The epidural space lies outside the dura mater.","Epidural space dura mater बाहिर हुन्छ।"],["A possible complication of spinal anaesthesia is:","Spinal anaesthesia को सम्भावित complication कुन हो?",["Hypotension","Hyperglycaemia always","Hearing improvement","Hypertension in every case"],"Sympathetic blockade can cause hypotension.","Sympathetic blockade ले hypotension गराउन सक्छ।"],["A high spinal block may compromise:","High spinal block ले कुन कुरा जोखिममा पार्न सक्छ?",["Respiration and cardiovascular function","Hair growth","Vision permanently in all cases","Renal anatomy"],"A high block can impair respiratory muscles and circulation.","High block ले श्वास मांसपेशी र circulation असर गर्न सक्छ।"],["A peripheral nerve stimulator is used to assess:","Peripheral nerve stimulator किन प्रयोग हुन्छ?",["Neuromuscular response to stimulation","Blood glucose","Oxygen cylinder pressure","Urine protein"],"It helps assess neuromuscular blockade and response.","यसले neuromuscular blockade र response मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ।"],["Neuromuscular blockers produce:","Neuromuscular blocker ले के गराउँछ?",["Skeletal muscle paralysis","Analgesia","Amnesia","Unconsciousness"],"They cause paralysis but do not provide analgesia or unconsciousness.","यसले paralysis गर्छ तर analgesia वा बेहोसी दिँदैन।"],["During recovery, delayed emergence requires assessment of:","Recovery मा होस आउन ढिलाइ भए के जाँच्नुपर्छ?",["Drug effects, ventilation, glucose and neurological causes","Only room lighting","Only patient's age","Only urine colour"],"Consider residual drugs, hypoventilation, metabolic and neurological causes.","औषधिको बाँकी असर, hypoventilation, metabolic र neurological कारण हेर्नुपर्छ।"],["A structured postoperative handover should include:","Postoperative handover मा के समावेश हुनुपर्छ?",["Airway, procedure, drugs, fluids and complications","Only patient's name","Only surgeon's name","Only room number"],"A complete handover communicates clinical risks and ongoing plans.","पूर्ण handover ले clinical risk र आगामी योजना बताउँछ।"],["Reusable anaesthesia equipment should be reprocessed according to:","Reusable anaesthesia उपकरण कसरी reprocess गर्नुपर्छ?",["Manufacturer instructions and infection-control policy","Personal preference","Rinsing with tap water only","No cleaning if visually clean"],"Cleaning/disinfection/sterilisation depends on device and validated policy.","उपकरणअनुसार cleaning/disinfection/sterilisation नीति पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],["Single-use airway equipment should be:","Single-use airway equipment के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Used once and discarded appropriately","Washed and reused routinely","Shared between patients","Stored uncleaned"],"Single-use items must not be reused.","Single-use सामान पुनःप्रयोग गर्नु हुँदैन।"],["When a patient deteriorates in recovery, the technologist should:","Recovery मा बिरामी बिग्रँदा technologist ले के गर्नुपर्छ?",["Recognise, call for help and support immediate assessment","Wait for routine rounds","Remove monitoring","Leave the patient alone"],"Early recognition, escalation and continuous monitoring are essential.","समयमै पहिचान, सहयोग बोलाउने र निगरानी आवश्यक हुन्छ।"]];
